   1343 RunPeriod,
   1344        \memo Specify a range of dates and other parameters for a simulation.
   1345        \memo Multiple run periods may be input, but they may not overlap.
   1346        \min-fields 7
   1347   A1 , \field Name
   1348        \required-field
   1349        \reference RunPeriodsAndDesignDays
   1350        \note descriptive name (used in reporting mainly)
   1351        \note Cannot be not blank and must be unique
   1352   N1 , \field Begin Month
   1353        \required-field
   1354        \minimum 1
   1355        \maximum 12
   1356        \type integer
   1357   N2 , \field Begin Day of Month
   1358        \required-field
   1359        \minimum 1
   1360        \maximum 31
   1361        \type integer
   1362   N3,  \field Begin Year
   1363        \note Start year of the simulation, if this field is specified it must agree with the Day of Week for Start Day
   1364        \note If this field is blank, the year will be selected to match the weekday, which is Sunday if not specified
   1365   N4 , \field End Month
   1366        \required-field
   1367        \minimum 1
   1368        \maximum 12
   1369        \type integer
   1370   N5 , \field End Day of Month
   1371        \required-field
   1372        \minimum 1
   1373        \maximum 31
   1374        \type integer
   1375   N6,  \field End Year
   1376        \note end year of simulation, if specified
   1377   A2 , \field Day of Week for Start Day
   1378        \note =[Sunday|Monday|Tuesday|Wednesday|Thursday|Friday|Saturday];
   1379        \note If no year is input, this field will default to Sunday
   1380        \note If a year is input and this field is blank, the correct weekday is determined
   1381        \type choice
   1382        \key Sunday
   1383        \key Monday
   1384        \key Tuesday
   1385        \key Wednesday
   1386        \key Thursday
   1387        \key Friday
   1388        \key Saturday
   1389   A3,  \field Use Weather File Holidays and Special Days
   1390        \note If yes or blank, use holidays as specified on Weatherfile.
   1391        \note If no, do not use the holidays specified on the Weatherfile.
   1392        \note Note: You can still specify holidays/special days using the RunPeriodControl:SpecialDays object(s).
   1393        \type choice
   1394        \default Yes
   1395        \key Yes
   1396        \key No
   1397   A4,  \field Use Weather File Daylight Saving Period
   1398        \note If yes or blank, use daylight saving period as specified on Weatherfile.
   1399        \note If no, do not use the daylight saving period as specified on the Weatherfile.
   1400        \type choice
   1401        \default Yes
   1402        \key Yes
   1403        \key No
   1404   A5,  \field Apply Weekend Holiday Rule
   1405        \note if yes and single day holiday falls on weekend, "holiday" occurs on following Monday
   1406        \type choice
   1407        \key Yes
   1408        \key No
   1409        \default No
   1410   A6,  \field Use Weather File Rain Indicators
   1411        \type choice
   1412        \key Yes
   1413        \key No
   1414        \default Yes
   1415   A7,  \field Use Weather File Snow Indicators
   1416        \type choice
   1417        \key Yes
   1418        \key No
   1419        \default Yes
   1420   A8;  \field Treat Weather as Actual
   1421        \type choice
   1422        \key Yes
   1423        \key No
   1424        \default No
   1425 
   1426 RunPeriodControl:SpecialDays,
   1427      \min-fields 4
   1428      \memo This object sets up holidays/special days to be used during weather file
   1429      \memo run periods.  (These are not used with SizingPeriod:* objects.)
   1430      \memo Depending on the value in the run period, days on the weather file may also
   1431      \memo be used.  However, the weather file specification will take precedence over
   1432      \memo any specification shown here.  (No error message on duplicate days or overlapping
   1433      \memo days).
   1434  A1, \field Name
   1435      \required-field
   1436  A2, \field Start Date
   1437      \required-field
   1438      \note  Dates can be several formats:
   1439      \note  <number>/<number>  (month/day)
   1440      \note  <number> <Month>
   1441      \note  <Month> <number>
   1442      \note <Nth> <Weekday> in <Month)
   1443      \note Last <WeekDay> in <Month>
   1444      \note <Month> can be January, February, March, April, May, June, July, August, September, October, November, December
   1445      \note Months can be the first 3 letters of the month
   1446      \note <Weekday> can be Sunday, Monday, Tuesday, Wednesday, Thursday, Friday, Saturday
   1447      \note <Nth> can be 1 or 1st, 2 or 2nd, etc. up to 5(?)
   1448  N1, \field Duration
   1449      \units days
   1450      \minimum 1
   1451      \maximum 366
   1452      \default 1
   1453  A3; \field Special Day Type
   1454        \note Special Day Type selects the schedules appropriate for each day so labeled
   1455        \type choice
   1456        \key Holiday
   1457        \key SummerDesignDay
   1458        \key WinterDesignDay
   1459        \key CustomDay1
   1460        \key CustomDay2
   1461        \default Holiday
   1462 
   1463 RunPeriodControl:DaylightSavingTime,
   1464      \unique-object
   1465      \min-fields 2
   1466      \memo This object sets up the daylight saving time period for any RunPeriod.
   1467      \memo Ignores any daylight saving time period on the weather file and uses this definition.
   1468      \memo These are not used with SizingPeriod:DesignDay objects.
   1469      \memo Use with SizingPeriod:WeatherFileDays object can be controlled in that object.
   1470  A1, \field Start Date
   1471      \required-field
   1472  A2; \field End Date
   1473      \required-field
   1474      \note  Dates can be several formats:
   1475      \note  <number>/<number>  (month/day)
   1476      \note  <number> <Month>
   1477      \note  <Month> <number>
   1478      \note <Nth> <Weekday> in <Month)
   1479      \note Last <WeekDay> in <Month>
   1480      \note <Month> can be January, February, March, April, May, June, July, August, September, October, November, December
   1481      \note Months can be the first 3 letters of the month
   1482      \note <Weekday> can be Sunday, Monday, Tuesday, Wednesday, Thursday, Friday, Saturday
   1483      \note <Nth> can be 1 or 1st, 2 or 2nd, etc. up to 5(?)
   1484 
   1485 WeatherProperty:SkyTemperature,
   1486        \memo This object is used to override internal sky temperature calculations.
   1487   A1,  \field Name
   1488        \note blank in this field will apply to all run periods (that is, all objects=
   1489        \note SizingPeriod:WeatherFileDays, SizingPeriod:WeatherFileConditionType or RunPeriod
   1490        \note otherwise, this name must match one of the environment object names.
   1491        \type object-list
   1492        \object-list RunPeriodsAndDesignDays
   1493   A2,  \field Calculation Type
   1494        \required-field
   1495        \note The field indicates that the sky temperature will be imported from external schedules or calculated by alternative methods other than default.
   1496        \type choice
   1497        \key ClarkAllen
   1498        \key Brunt
   1499        \key Idso
   1500        \key BerdahlMartin
   1501        \key ScheduleValue
   1502        \key DifferenceScheduleDryBulbValue
   1503        \key DifferenceScheduleDewPointValue
   1504        \default ClarkAllen
   1505   A3,  \field Schedule Name
   1506        \note if name matches a SizingPeriod:DesignDay, put in a day schedule of this name
   1507        \note if name is for a SizingPeriod:WeatherFileDays, SizingPeriod:WeatherFileConditionType or
   1508        \note RunPeriod, put in a full year schedule that covers the appropriate days.
   1509        \note Required if Calculation Type is ScheduleValue, DifferenceScheduleDryBulbValue or DifferenceScheduleDewPointValue.
   1510        \type object-list
   1511        \object-list DayScheduleNames
   1512        \object-list ScheduleNames
   1513   A4; \field Use Weather File Horizontal IR
   1514        \note If yes or blank, use Horizontal IR values from weather file when present, otherwise use the specified sky model.
   1515        \note If no, always use the specified sky model and ignore the horizontal IR values from the weather file.
   1516        \note For Calculation Type = ScheduleValue, DifferenceScheduleDryBulbValue or DifferenceScheduleDewPointValue, this field is ignored and the scheduled values are used.
   1517        \type choice
   1518        \default Yes
   1519        \key Yes
   1520        \key No
   1521 
   1522 Site:WeatherStation,
   1523        \unique-object
   1524        \memo This object should only be used for non-standard weather data.  Standard weather data
   1525        \memo such as TMY2, IWEC, and ASHRAE design day data are all measured at the
   1526        \memo default conditions and do not require this object.
   1527   N1 , \field Wind Sensor Height Above Ground
   1528        \type real
   1529        \units m
   1530        \default 10.0
   1531        \minimum> 0.0
   1532   N2 , \field Wind Speed Profile Exponent
   1533        \type real
   1534        \default 0.14
   1535        \minimum 0.0
   1536   N3 , \field Wind Speed Profile Boundary Layer Thickness
   1537        \type real
   1538        \units m
   1539        \default 270.0
   1540        \minimum 0.0
   1541   N4 ; \field Air Temperature Sensor Height Above Ground
   1542        \type real
   1543        \units m
   1544        \default 1.5
   1545        \minimum 0.0
   1546 
   1547 Site:HeightVariation,
   1548        \unique-object
   1549        \memo This object is used if the user requires advanced control over height-dependent
   1550        \memo variations in wind speed and temperature.  When this object is not present, the default model
   1551        \memo for temperature dependence on height is used, and the wind speed is modeled according
   1552        \memo to the Terrain field of the BUILDING object.
   1553   N1 , \field Wind Speed Profile Exponent
   1554        \note Set to zero for no wind speed dependence on height.
   1555        \type real
   1556        \default 0.22
   1557        \minimum 0.0
   1558   N2 , \field Wind Speed Profile Boundary Layer Thickness
   1559        \type real
   1560        \units m
   1561        \default 370.0
   1562        \minimum> 0.0
   1563   N3 ; \field Air Temperature Gradient Coefficient
   1564        \note Set to zero for no air temperature dependence on height.
   1565        \type real
   1566        \units K/m
   1567        \default 0.0065
   1568        \minimum 0.0
   1569 
   1570 Site:GroundTemperature:BuildingSurface,
   1571        \memo These temperatures are specifically for those surfaces that have the outside environment
   1572        \memo of "Ground".  Documentation about what values these should be is located in the
   1573        \memo Auxiliary programs document (Ground Heat Transfer) as well as the InputOutput Reference.
   1574        \memo CAUTION - Do not use the "undisturbed" ground temperatures from the weather data.
   1575        \memo These values are too extreme for the soil under a conditioned building.
   1576        \memo For best results, use the Slab or Basement program to calculate custom monthly
   1577        \memo average ground temperatures (see Auxiliary Programs).  For typical commercial
   1578        \memo buildings in the USA, a reasonable default value is 2C less than the average indoor space temperature.
   1579        \unique-object
