   1799 Site:GroundTemperature:Undisturbed:FiniteDifference,
   1800        \memo Undisturbed ground temperature object using a
   1801        \memo detailed finite difference 1-D model
   1802        \min-fields 7
   1803   A1,  \field Name
   1804        \required-field
   1805        \reference UndisturbedGroundTempModels
   1806   N1,  \field Soil Thermal Conductivity
   1807        \required-field
   1808        \type real
   1809        \units W/m-K
   1810        \minimum> 0.0
   1811   N2,  \field Soil Density
   1812        \required-field
   1813        \type real
   1814        \units kg/m3
   1815        \minimum> 0.0
   1816   N3,  \field Soil Specific Heat
   1817        \required-field
   1818        \type real
   1819        \units J/kg-K
   1820        \minimum> 0.0
   1821   N4,  \field Soil Moisture Content Volume Fraction
   1822        \type real
   1823        \units percent
   1824        \minimum 0
   1825        \maximum 100
   1826        \default 30
   1827   N5,  \field Soil Moisture Content Volume Fraction at Saturation
   1828        \type real
   1829        \units percent
   1830        \minimum 0
   1831        \maximum 100
   1832        \default 50
   1833    N6; \field Evapotranspiration Ground Cover Parameter
   1834        \type real
   1835        \units dimensionless
   1836        \minimum 0
   1837        \maximum 1.5
   1838        \default 0.4
   1839        \note This specifies the ground cover effects during evapotranspiration
   1840        \note  calculations.  The value roughly represents the following cases:
   1841        \note  = 0   : concrete or other solid, non-permeable ground surface material
   1842        \note  = 0.5 : short grass, much like a manicured lawn
   1843        \note  = 1   : standard reference state (12 cm grass)
   1844        \note  = 1.5 : wild growth
   1845 
   1846 Site:GroundTemperature:Undisturbed:KusudaAchenbach,
   1847        \memo Undisturbed ground temperature object using the
   1848        \memo Kusuda-Achenbach 1965 correlation.
   1849        \min-fields 7
   1850   A1,  \field Name
   1851        \required-field
   1852        \reference UndisturbedGroundTempModels
   1853   N1,  \field Soil Thermal Conductivity
   1854        \required-field
   1855        \type real
   1856        \units W/m-K
   1857        \minimum> 0.0
   1858   N2,  \field Soil Density
   1859        \required-field
   1860        \type real
   1861        \units kg/m3
   1862        \minimum> 0.0
   1863   N3,  \field Soil Specific Heat
   1864        \required-field
   1865        \type real
   1866        \units J/kg-K
   1867        \minimum> 0.0
   1868   N4,  \field Average Soil Surface Temperature
   1869        \type real
   1870        \units C
   1871        \note Annual average surface temperature
   1872        \note If left blank the Site:GroundTemperature:Shallow object must be included in the input
   1873        \note The soil temperature, amplitude, and phase shift must all be included or omitted together
   1874   N5,  \field Average Amplitude of Surface Temperature
   1875        \type real
   1876        \units deltaC
   1877        \minimum 0
   1878        \note Annual average surface temperature variation from average.
   1879        \note If left blank the Site:GroundTemperature:Shallow object must be included in the input
   1880        \note The soil temperature, amplitude, and phase shift must all be included or omitted together
   1881   N6;  \field Phase Shift of Minimum Surface Temperature
   1882        \type real
   1883        \units days
   1884        \minimum 0
   1885        \maximum< 365
   1886        \note The phase shift of minimum surface temperature, or the day
   1887        \note of the year when the minimum surface temperature occurs.
   1888        \note If left blank the Site:GroundTemperature:Shallow object must be included in the input
   1889        \note The soil temperature, amplitude, and phase shift must all be included or omitted together
   1890 
