   2199 Site:GroundReflectance,
   2200         \memo Specifies the ground reflectance values used to calculate ground reflected solar.
   2201         \memo The ground reflectance can be further modified when snow is on the ground
   2202         \memo by Site:GroundReflectance:SnowModifier.
   2203   \unique-object
   2204   \min-fields 12
   2205   \format singleLine
   2206   N1 , \field January Ground Reflectance
   2207         \default 0.2
   2208         \type real
   2209         \minimum 0.0
   2210         \maximum 1.0
   2211         \units dimensionless
   2212    N2 , \field February Ground Reflectance
   2213         \default 0.2
   2214         \type real
   2215         \minimum 0.0
   2216         \maximum 1.0
   2217         \units dimensionless
   2218    N3 , \field March Ground Reflectance
   2219         \default 0.2
   2220         \type real
   2221         \minimum 0.0
   2222         \maximum 1.0
   2223         \units dimensionless
   2224    N4 , \field April Ground Reflectance
   2225         \default 0.2
   2226         \type real
   2227         \minimum 0.0
   2228         \maximum 1.0
   2229         \units dimensionless
   2230    N5 , \field May Ground Reflectance
   2231         \default 0.2
   2232         \type real
   2233         \minimum 0.0
   2234         \maximum 1.0
   2235         \units dimensionless
   2236    N6 , \field June Ground Reflectance
   2237         \default 0.2
   2238         \type real
   2239         \minimum 0.0
   2240         \maximum 1.0
   2241         \units dimensionless
   2242    N7 , \field July Ground Reflectance
   2243         \default 0.2
   2244         \type real
   2245         \minimum 0.0
   2246         \maximum 1.0
   2247         \units dimensionless
   2248    N8 , \field August Ground Reflectance
   2249         \default 0.2
   2250         \type real
   2251         \minimum 0.0
   2252         \maximum 1.0
   2253         \units dimensionless
   2254    N9 , \field September Ground Reflectance
   2255          \default 0.2
   2256          \type real
   2257          \minimum 0.0
   2258          \maximum 1.0
   2259          \units dimensionless
   2260    N10 , \field October Ground Reflectance
   2261          \default 0.2
   2262          \type real
   2263          \minimum 0.0
   2264          \maximum 1.0
   2265          \units dimensionless
   2266    N11 , \field November Ground Reflectance
   2267          \default 0.2
   2268          \type real
   2269          \minimum 0.0
   2270          \maximum 1.0
   2271          \units dimensionless
   2272    N12 ; \field December Ground Reflectance
   2273          \default 0.2
   2274          \type real
   2275          \minimum 0.0
   2276          \maximum 1.0
   2277          \units dimensionless
   2278 
   2279 Site:GroundReflectance:SnowModifier,
   2280       \memo Specifies ground reflectance multipliers when snow resident on the ground.
   2281       \memo These multipliers are applied to the "normal" ground reflectances specified
   2282       \memo in Site:GroundReflectance.
   2283   N1, \field Ground Reflected Solar Modifier
   2284   \minimum 0.0
   2285   \default 1.0
   2286     \note Value for modifying the "normal" ground reflectance when Snow is on ground
   2287     \note  when calculating the "Ground Reflected Solar Radiation Value"
   2288     \note  a value of 1.0 here uses the "normal" ground reflectance
   2289     \note  Ground Reflected Solar = (BeamSolar*CosSunZenith + DiffuseSolar)*GroundReflectance
   2290     \note    This would be further modified by the Snow Ground Reflectance Modifier when Snow was on the ground
   2291     \note    When Snow on ground, effective GroundReflectance is normal GroundReflectance*"Ground Reflectance Snow Modifier"
   2292     \note  Ground Reflectance achieved in this manner will be restricted to [0.0,1.0]
   2293   N2; \field Daylighting Ground Reflected Solar Modifier
   2294   \minimum 0.0
   2295   \default 1.0
   2296     \note Value for modifying the "normal" daylighting ground reflectance when Snow is on ground
   2297     \note  when calculating the "Ground Reflected Solar Radiation Value"
   2298     \note  a value of 1.0 here uses the "normal" ground reflectance
   2299     \note  Ground Reflected Solar = (BeamSolar*CosSunZenith + DiffuseSolar)*GroundReflectance
   2300     \note    This would be further modified by the Snow Ground Reflectance Modifier when Snow was on the ground
   2301     \note    When Snow on ground, effective GroundReflectance is normal GroundReflectance*"Daylighting Ground Reflectance Snow Modifier"
   2302     \note  Ground Reflectance achieved in this manner will be restricted to [0.0,1.0]
   2303 
   2304 Site:WaterMainsTemperature,
   2305        \memo Used to calculate water mains temperatures delivered by underground water main pipes.
   2306        \memo Water mains temperatures are a function of outdoor climate conditions
   2307        \memo and vary with time of year.
   2308   A1 , \field Calculation Method
   2309        \required-field
   2310        \type choice
   2311        \key Schedule
   2312        \key Correlation
   2313        \key CorrelationFromWeatherFile
   2314        \default CorrelationFromWeatherFile
   2315        \note If calculation method is CorrelationFromWeatherFile, the two numeric input
   2316        \note fields are ignored. Instead, EnergyPlus calculates them from weather file.
   2317   A2 , \field Temperature Schedule Name
   2318        \type object-list
   2319        \object-list ScheduleNames
   2320   N1 , \field Annual Average Outdoor Air Temperature
   2321        \note If calculation method is CorrelationFromWeatherFile or Schedule, this input
   2322        \note field is ignored.
   2323        \type real
   2324        \units C
   2325   N2 ; \field Maximum Difference In Monthly Average Outdoor Air Temperatures
   2326        \note If calculation method is CorrelationFromWeatherFile or Schedule, this input
   2327        \note field is ignored.
   2328        \type real
   2329        \units deltaC
   2330        \minimum 0
   2331 
   2332 Site:Precipitation,
   2333       \memo Used to describe the amount of water precipitation at the building site.
   2334       \memo Precipitation includes both rain and the equivalent water content of snow.
   2335   A1, \field Precipitation Model Type
   2336       \type choice
   2337       \key ScheduleAndDesignLevel
   2338   N1, \field Design Level for Total Annual Precipitation
   2339       \note meters of water per year used for design level
   2340       \units m/yr
   2341   A2, \field Precipitation Rates Schedule Name
   2342       \type object-list
   2343       \object-list ScheduleNames
   2344       \note Schedule values in meters of water per hour
   2345       \note values should be non-negative
   2346   N2; \field Average Total Annual Precipitation
   2347       \note meters of water per year from average weather statistics
   2348       \minimum 0
   2349       \units m/yr
   2350 
   2351 RoofIrrigation,
   2352       \memo Used to describe the amount of irrigation on the ecoroof surface over the course
   2353       \memo of the simulation runperiod.
   2354   A1, \field Irrigation Model Type
   2355       \type choice
   2356       \key Schedule
   2357       \key SmartSchedule
   2358       \note SmartSchedule will not allow irrigation when soil is already moist.
   2359       \note Current threshold set at 30% of saturation.
   2360   A2, \field Irrigation Rate Schedule Name
   2361       \type object-list
   2362       \object-list ScheduleNames
   2363       \note Schedule values in meters of water per hour
   2364       \note values should be non-negative
   2365   N1; \field Irrigation Maximum Saturation Threshold
   2366       \note Used with SmartSchedule to set the saturation level at which no
   2367       \note irrigation is allowed.
   2368       \units percent
   2369       \minimum 0.0
   2370       \maximum 100.0
   2371       \default 40.0
   2372 
   2373 Site:SolarAndVisibleSpectrum,
   2374       \memo If this object is omitted, the default solar and visible spectrum data will be used.
   2375       \unique-object
   2376   A1, \field Name
   2377       \required-field
   2378       \type alpha
   2379   A2, \field Spectrum Data Method
   2380       \note The method specifies which of the solar and visible spectrum data to use in the calculations.
   2381       \note Choices: Default - existing hard-wired spectrum data in EnergyPlus.
