   6209 WindowMaterial:Screen,
   6210        \memo Window screen physical properties. Can only be located on the exterior side of a window construction.
   6211        \min-fields 9
   6212   A1 , \field Name
   6213        \note Enter a unique name for this window screen material.
   6214        \required-field
   6215        \type alpha
   6216        \reference MaterialName
   6217        \reference WindowShadesScreensAndBlinds
   6218   A2 , \field Reflected Beam Transmittance Accounting Method
   6219        \note Select the method used to account for the beam solar reflected off the material surface.
   6220        \type choice
   6221        \key DoNotModel
   6222        \key ModelAsDirectBeam
   6223        \key ModelAsDiffuse
   6224        \default ModelAsDiffuse
   6225   N1 , \field Diffuse Solar Reflectance
   6226        \note Diffuse reflectance of the screen material over the entire solar radiation spectrum.
   6227        \note Assumed to be the same for both sides of the screen.
   6228        \required-field
   6229        \type real
   6230        \units dimensionless
   6231        \minimum 0
   6232        \maximum< 1
   6233   N2 , \field Diffuse Visible Reflectance
   6234        \note Diffuse visible reflectance of the screen material averaged over the solar spectrum
   6235        \note and weighted by the response of the human eye.
   6236        \note Assumed to be the same for both sides of the screen.
   6237        \required-field
   6238        \type real
   6239        \units dimensionless
   6240        \minimum 0
   6241        \maximum< 1
   6242   N3 , \field Thermal Hemispherical Emissivity
   6243        \note Long-wave emissivity of the screen material.
   6244        \note Assumed to be the same for both sides of the screen.
   6245        \type real
   6246        \units dimensionless
   6247        \maximum< 1
   6248        \minimum> 0
   6249        \default 0.9
   6250   N4 , \field Conductivity
   6251        \note Thermal conductivity of the screen material.
   6252        \type real
   6253        \units W/m-K
   6254        \minimum> 0
   6255        \default 221.0
   6256        \note Default is for aluminum.
   6257   N5 , \field Screen Material Spacing
   6258        \note Spacing assumed to be the same in both directions.
   6259        \required-field
   6260        \type real
   6261        \units m
   6262        \minimum> 0
   6263        \ip-units in
   6264   N6 , \field Screen Material Diameter
   6265        \note Diameter assumed to be the same in both directions.
   6266        \required-field
   6267        \type real
   6268        \units m
   6269        \minimum> 0
   6270        \ip-units in
   6271   N7 , \field Screen to Glass Distance
   6272        \note Distance from the window screen to the adjacent glass surface.
   6273        \type real
   6274        \units m
   6275        \minimum 0.001
   6276        \maximum 1.0
   6277        \default 0.025
   6278        \ip-units in
   6279   N8 , \field Top Opening Multiplier
   6280        \note Effective area for air flow at the top of the screen divided by the perpendicular
   6281        \note area between the glass and the top of the screen.
   6282        \type real
   6283        \units dimensionless
   6284        \minimum 0.0
   6285        \maximum 1.0
   6286        \default 0.0
   6287   N9 , \field Bottom Opening Multiplier
   6288        \note Effective area for air flow at the bottom of the screen divided by the perpendicular
   6289        \note area between the glass and the bottom of the screen.
   6290        \type real
   6291        \units dimensionless
   6292        \minimum 0.0
   6293        \maximum 1.0
   6294        \default 0.0
   6295   N10, \field Left Side Opening Multiplier
   6296        \note Effective area for air flow at the left side of the screen divided by the perpendicular
   6297        \note area between the glass and the left side of the screen.
   6298        \type real
   6299        \units dimensionless
   6300        \minimum 0.0
   6301        \maximum 1.0
   6302        \default 0.0
   6303   N11, \field Right Side Opening Multiplier
   6304        \note Effective area for air flow at the right side of the screen divided by the perpendicular
   6305        \note area between the glass and the right side of the screen.
   6306        \type real
   6307        \units dimensionless
   6308        \minimum 0.0
   6309        \maximum 1.0
   6310        \default 0.0
   6311   N12; \field Angle of Resolution for Screen Transmittance Output Map
   6312        \note Select the resolution of azimuth and altitude angles for the screen transmittance map.
   6313        \note A value of 0 means no transmittance map will be generated.
   6314        \note Valid values for this field are 0, 1, 2, 3 and 5.
   6315        \type choice
   6316        \units deg
   6317        \key 0
   6318        \key 1
   6319        \key 2
   6320        \key 3
   6321        \key 5
   6322        \default 0
   6323 
   6324 WindowMaterial:Shade:EquivalentLayer,
   6325        \memo Specifies the properties of equivalent layer window shade material
   6326        \memo Shades are considered to be perfect diffusers (all transmitted and
   6327        \memo reflected radiation is hemispherically-diffuse) independent of angle
   6328        \memo  of incidence.  Shade represents roller blinds.
   6329        \min-fields 6
   6330   A1 , \field Name
   6331        \required-field
   6332        \type alpha
   6333        \reference WindowEquivalentLayerMaterialNames
   6334   N1 , \field Shade Beam-Beam Solar Transmittance
   6335        \note The beam-beam solar transmittance at normal incidence.  This value is
   6336        \note the same as the openness area fraction of the shade material. Assumed
   6337        \note to be the same for front and back sides.
   6338        \type real
   6339        \units dimensionless
   6340        \minimum 0.0
   6341        \maximum 0.8
   6342        \default 0.0
   6343   N2 , \field Front Side Shade Beam-Diffuse Solar Transmittance
   6344        \required-field
   6345        \note The front side beam-diffuse solar transmittance at normal incidence averaged
   6346        \note over the entire spectrum of solar radiation.
   6347        \type real
   6348        \units dimensionless
   6349        \minimum 0
   6350        \maximum< 1
   6351   N3 , \field Back Side Shade Beam-Diffuse Solar Transmittance
   6352        \required-field
   6353        \note The back side beam-diffuse solar transmittance at normal incidence averaged
   6354        \note over the entire spectrum of solar radiation.
   6355        \type real
   6356        \units dimensionless
   6357        \minimum 0
   6358        \maximum< 1
   6359   N4 , \field Front Side Shade Beam-Diffuse Solar Reflectance
   6360        \required-field
   6361        \note The front side beam-diffuse solar reflectance at normal incidence averaged
   6362        \note over the entire spectrum of solar radiation.
   6363        \type real
   6364        \units dimensionless
   6365        \minimum 0
   6366        \maximum< 1
   6367   N5 , \field Back Side Shade Beam-Diffuse Solar Reflectance
   6368        \required-field
   6369        \note The back side beam-diffuse solar reflectance at normal incidence averaged
   6370        \note over the entire spectrum of solar radiation.
   6371        \type real
   6372        \units dimensionless
   6373        \minimum 0
   6374        \maximum< 1
   6375   N6 , \field Shade Beam-Beam Visible Transmittance at Normal Incidence
   6376        \note The beam-beam visible transmittance at normal incidence averaged over the
   6377        \note visible spectrum range of solar radiation. Assumed to be the same for
   6378        \note front and back sides of the shade.
   6379        \type real
   6380        \units dimensionless
   6381        \minimum 0
   6382        \maximum< 1
   6383   N7 , \field Shade Beam-Diffuse Visible Transmittance at Normal Incidence
   6384        \note The beam-diffuse visible transmittance at normal incidence averaged over the
   6385        \note visible spectrum range of solar radiation. Assumed to be the same for
   6386        \note front and back sides of the shade.
   6387        \type real
   6388        \units dimensionless
   6389        \minimum 0
   6390        \maximum< 1
   6391   N8 , \field Shade Beam-Diffuse Visible Reflectance at Normal Incidence
   6392        \note The beam-diffuse visible reflectance at normal incidence averaged over the
   6393        \note visible spectrum range of solar radiation. Assumed to be the same for
   6394        \note front and back sides of the shade.
   6395        \type real
   6396        \units dimensionless
   6397        \minimum 0
   6398        \maximum< 1
   6399   N9 , \field Shade Material Infrared Transmittance
   6400        \note The long-wave transmittance of the shade material at zero shade openness.
   6401        \note Assumed to be the same for front and back sides of the shade.
   6402        \type real
   6403        \units dimensionless
   6404        \maximum< 1
   6405        \minimum 0
   6406        \default 0.05
   6407   N10, \field Front Side Shade Material Infrared Emissivity
   6408        \note The front side long-wave emissivity of the shade material at zero shade
   6409        \note openness. Openness fraction is used to calculate the effective emissivity
   6410        \note value.
