   6545 WindowMaterial:Blind:EquivalentLayer,
   6546        \memo Window equivalent layer blind slat optical and thermal properties.
   6547        \memo The model assumes that slats are thin and flat, applies correction
   6548        \memo empirical correlation to account for curvature effect. Slats are
   6549        \memo assumed to transmit and reflect diffusely.
   6550        \min-fields 10
   6551   A1 , \field Name
   6552        \required-field
   6553        \type alpha
   6554        \reference WindowEquivalentLayerMaterialNames
   6555   A2 , \field Slat Orientation
   6556        \type choice
   6557        \key Horizontal
   6558        \key Vertical
   6559        \default Horizontal
   6560   N1 , \field Slat Width
   6561        \required-field
   6562        \units m
   6563        \type real
   6564        \minimum> 0
   6565        \maximum 0.025
   6566        \ip-units in
   6567   N2 , \field Slat Separation
   6568        \required-field
   6569        \note Distance between adjacent slat faces
   6570        \units m
   6571        \type real
   6572        \minimum> 0
   6573        \maximum 0.025
   6574        \ip-units in
   6575   N3 , \field Slat Crown
   6576        \note Perpendicular length between the cord and the curve.
   6577        \note Slat is assumed to be rectangular in cross section
   6578        \note and flat. Crown=0.0625x"Slat width"
   6579        \type real
   6580        \units m
   6581        \minimum 0
   6582        \maximum 0.00156
   6583        \default 0.0015
   6584        \ip-units in
   6585   N4 , \field Slat Angle
   6586        \type real
   6587        \units deg
   6588        \minimum -90
   6589        \maximum 90
   6590        \default 45
   6591        \note Slat angle is +ve if the tip of the slat front face is tilted upward, else
   6592        \note the slat angle is -ve if the tip of the slat front face is tilted downward.
   6593        \note The slat angle varies between -90 to +90. The default value is 45 degrees.
   6594   N5 , \field Front Side Slat Beam-Diffuse Solar Transmittance
   6595        \note The front side beam-diffuse solar transmittance of the slat at normal
   6596        \note incidence averaged over the entire spectrum of solar radiation.
