   7358 MaterialProperty:PhaseChangeHysteresis,
   7359     \memo Additional properties for temperature dependent thermal conductivity
   7360     \memo and enthalpy for Phase Change Materials (PCM) with separate melting and freezing curves.
   7361     \memo HeatBalanceAlgorithm = CondFD (ConductionFiniteDifference) solution algorithm only.
   7362     \memo Constructions with this should use the detailed CondFD process.
   7363     \memo Has no effect with other HeatBalanceAlgorithm solution algorithms.
   7364   A1,  \field Name
   7365        \required-field
   7366        \type object-list
   7367        \object-list MaterialName
   7368        \note Regular Material Name to which the additional properties will be added.
   7369        \note this the material name for the basic material properties.
   7370   N1 , \field Latent Heat during the Entire Phase Change Process
   7371        \note The total latent heat absorbed or rejected during the transition from solid to liquid, or back
   7372        \required-field
   7373        \units J/kg
   7374        \type real
   7375        \minimum> 0
   7376   N2 , \field Liquid State Thermal Conductivity
   7377        \note The thermal conductivity used by this material when the material is fully liquid
   7378        \required-field
   7379        \units W/m-K
   7380        \type real
   7381        \minimum> 0
   7382   N3 , \field Liquid State Density
   7383        \note The density used by this material when the material is fully liquid
   7384        \required-field
   7385        \units kg/m3
   7386        \type real
   7387        \minimum> 0
   7388   N4 , \field Liquid State Specific Heat
   7389        \note The constant specific heat used for the fully melted (liquid) state
   7390        \required-field
   7391        \units J/kg-K
   7392        \type real
   7393        \minimum> 0
   7394   N5 , \field High Temperature Difference of Melting Curve
   7395        \note The total melting range of the material is the sum of low and high temperature difference of melting curve.
   7396        \required-field
   7397        \units deltaC
   7398        \type real
   7399        \minimum> 0
   7400   N6 , \field Peak Melting Temperature
   7401        \note The temperature at which the melting curve peaks
   7402        \required-field
   7403        \units C
   7404        \type real
   7405        \minimum> 0
   7406   N7 , \field Low Temperature Difference of Melting Curve
   7407        \note The total melting range of the material is the sum of low and high temperature difference of melting curve.
   7408        \required-field
   7409        \units deltaC
   7410        \type real
   7411        \minimum> 0
   7412   N8 , \field Solid State Thermal Conductivity
   7413        \note The thermal conductivity used by this material when the material is fully solid
   7414        \required-field
   7415        \units W/m-K
   7416        \type real
   7417        \minimum> 0
   7418   N9 , \field Solid State Density
   7419        \note The density used by this material when the material is fully solid
   7420        \required-field
   7421        \units kg/m3
   7422        \type real
   7423        \minimum> 0
   7424   N10, \field Solid State Specific Heat
   7425        \note The constant specific heat used for the fully frozen (crystallized) state
   7426        \required-field
   7427        \units J/kg-K
   7428        \type real
   7429        \minimum> 0
   7430   N11, \field High Temperature Difference of Freezing Curve
   7431        \note The total freezing range of the material is the sum of low and high temperature difference of freezing curve.
   7432        \required-field
   7433        \units deltaC
   7434        \type real
   7435        \minimum> 0
   7436   N12, \field Peak Freezing Temperature
   7437        \note The temperature at which the freezing curve peaks
   7438        \required-field
   7439        \units C
   7440        \type real
   7441        \minimum> 0
   7442   N13; \field Low Temperature Difference of Freezing Curve
   7443        \note The total freezing range of the material is the sum of low and high temperature difference of freezing curve.
   7444        \required-field
   7445        \units deltaC
   7446        \type real
   7447        \minimum> 0
