   9709 ZoneGroup,
   9710        \memo Adds a multiplier to a ZoneList. This can be used to reduce the amount of input
   9711        \memo necessary for simulating repetitive structures, such as the identical floors of a
   9712        \memo multi-story building.
   9713        \min-fields 2
   9714   A1 , \field Name
   9715        \note Name of the Zone Group
   9716        \required-field
   9717        \type alpha
   9718   A2,  \field Zone List Name
   9719        \required-field
   9720        \type object-list
   9721        \object-list ZoneListNames
   9722   N1;  \field Zone List Multiplier
   9723        \type integer
   9724        \default 1
   9725        \minimum 1
   9726 
   9727 BuildingSurface:Detailed,
   9728   \memo Allows for detailed entry of building heat transfer surfaces.  Does not include subsurfaces such as windows or doors.
   9729   \extensible:3 -- duplicate last set of x,y,z coordinates (last 3 fields), remembering to remove ; from "inner" fields.
   9730   \format vertices
   9731   \min-fields 19
   9732   A1 , \field Name
   9733        \required-field
   9734        \type alpha
   9735        \reference SurfaceNames
   9736        \reference SurfAndSubSurfNames
   9737        \reference AllHeatTranSurfNames
   9738        \reference OutFaceEnvNames
   9739        \reference AllHeatTranAngFacNames
   9740        \reference RadiantSurfaceNames
   9741        \reference AllShadingAndHTSurfNames
   9742        \reference FloorSurfaceNames
   9743   A2 , \field Surface Type
   9744        \required-field
   9745        \type choice
   9746        \key Floor
   9747        \key Wall
   9748        \key Ceiling
   9749        \key Roof
   9750   A3 , \field Construction Name
   9751        \required-field
   9752        \note To be matched with a construction in this input file
   9753        \type object-list
   9754        \object-list ConstructionNames
   9755   A4 , \field Zone Name
   9756        \required-field
   9757        \note Zone the surface is a part of
   9758        \type object-list
   9759        \object-list ZoneNames
   9760   A5 , \field Outside Boundary Condition
   9761        \required-field
   9762        \type choice
   9763        \key Adiabatic
   9764        \key Surface
   9765        \key Zone
   9766        \key Outdoors
   9767        \key Foundation
   9768        \key Ground
   9769        \key GroundFCfactorMethod
   9770        \key OtherSideCoefficients
   9771        \key OtherSideConditionsModel
   9772        \key GroundSlabPreprocessorAverage
   9773        \key GroundSlabPreprocessorCore
   9774        \key GroundSlabPreprocessorPerimeter
   9775        \key GroundBasementPreprocessorAverageWall
   9776        \key GroundBasementPreprocessorAverageFloor
   9777        \key GroundBasementPreprocessorUpperWall
   9778        \key GroundBasementPreprocessorLowerWall
   9779   A6,  \field Outside Boundary Condition Object
   9780        \type object-list
   9781        \object-list OutFaceEnvNames
   9782        \note Non-blank only if the field Outside Boundary Condition is Surface,
   9783        \note Zone, OtherSideCoefficients or OtherSideConditionsModel
   9784        \note If Surface, specify name of corresponding surface in adjacent zone or
   9785        \note specify current surface name for internal partition separating like zones
   9786        \note If Zone, specify the name of the corresponding zone and
   9787        \note the program will generate the corresponding interzone surface
   9788        \note If Foundation, specify the name of the corresponding Foundation object and
   9789        \note the program will calculate the heat transfer appropriately
   9790        \note If OtherSideCoefficients, specify name of SurfaceProperty:OtherSideCoefficients
   9791        \note If OtherSideConditionsModel, specify name of SurfaceProperty:OtherSideConditionsModel
   9792   A7 , \field Sun Exposure
   9793        \type choice
   9794        \key SunExposed
   9795        \key NoSun
   9796        \default SunExposed
   9797   A8,  \field Wind Exposure
   9798        \type choice
   9799        \key WindExposed
   9800        \key NoWind
   9801        \default WindExposed
   9802   N1,  \field View Factor to Ground
   9803        \type real
   9804        \note From the exterior of the surface
   9805        \note Unused if one uses the "reflections" options in Solar Distribution in Building input
   9806        \note unless a DaylightingDevice:Shelf or DaylightingDevice:Tubular object has been specified.
   9807        \note autocalculate will automatically calculate this value from the tilt of the surface
   9808        \autocalculatable
   9809        \minimum 0.0
   9810        \maximum 1.0
   9811        \default autocalculate
   9812   N2 , \field Number of Vertices
   9813        \note shown with 120 vertex coordinates -- extensible object
   9814        \note  "extensible" -- duplicate last set of x,y,z coordinates (last 3 fields),
   9815        \note remembering to remove ; from "inner" fields.
   9816        \note for clarity in any error messages, renumber the fields as well.
   9817        \note (and changing z terminator to a comma "," for all but last one which needs a semi-colon ";")
   9818        \autocalculatable
   9819        \minimum 3
   9820        \default autocalculate
   9821        \note vertices are given in GlobalGeometryRules coordinates -- if relative, all surface coordinates
   9822        \note are "relative" to the Zone Origin.  If world, then building and zone origins are used
   9823        \note for some internal calculations, but all coordinates are given in an "absolute" system.
