  12359 WindowShadingControl,
  12360        \memo Specifies the type, location, and controls for window shades, window blinds, and
  12361        \memo switchable glazing. Referencing the surface objects for exterior windows and glass
  12362        \memo doors (ref: FenestrationSurface:Detailed, Window, and GlazedDoor).
  12363        \extensible:1
  12364   A1 , \field Name
  12365        \required-field
  12366        \type alpha
  12367        \reference WindowShadeControlNames
  12368        \note Referenced by surfaces that are exterior windows
  12369        \note Not used by interzone windows
  12370   A2 , \field Zone Name
  12371        \required-field
  12372        \type object-list
  12373        \object-list ZoneNames
  12374   N1 , \field Shading Control Sequence Number
  12375        \type integer
  12376        \minimum 1
  12377        \default 1
  12378        \note If multiple WindowShadingControl objects are used than the order that they deploy the window shades
  12379        \note can be set with this field. The first WindowShadingControl should be 1 and subsequent
  12380        \note WindowShadingControl should 2 or 3 or higher. This is usually used when the Multiple Surface Control Type
  12381        \note field is set to Group and groups of windows are being controlled in a certain order.
  12382   A3 , \field Shading Type
  12383        \required-field
  12384        \type choice
  12385        \key InteriorShade
  12386        \key ExteriorShade
  12387        \key ExteriorScreen
  12388        \key InteriorBlind
  12389        \key ExteriorBlind
  12390        \key BetweenGlassShade
  12391        \key BetweenGlassBlind
  12392        \key SwitchableGlazing
  12393   A4 , \field Construction with Shading Name
  12394        \type object-list
  12395        \object-list ConstructionNames
  12396        \note Required if Shading Type = SwitchableGlazing
  12397        \note Required if Shading Type = interior or exterior shade or blind, or exterior screen, and
  12398        \note "Shading Device Material Name" is not specified.
  12399        \note If both "Construction with Shading Name" and "Shading Device Material Name" are entered,
  12400        \note the former takes precedence.
  12401   A5 , \field Shading Control Type
  12402        \required-field
  12403        \type choice
  12404        \key AlwaysOn
  12405        \key AlwaysOff
  12406        \key OnIfScheduleAllows
  12407        \note OnIfScheduleAllows requires that Schedule Name be specified and
  12408        \note Shading Control Is Scheduled = Yes.
  12409        \note AlwaysOn, AlwaysOff and OnIfScheduleAllows are the only valid control types for ExteriorScreen.
  12410        \note The following six control types are used primarily to reduce
  12411        \note zone cooling load due to window solar gain
  12412        \key OnIfHighSolarOnWindow
  12413        \key OnIfHighHorizontalSolar
  12414        \key OnIfHighOutdoorAirTemperature
  12415        \key OnIfHighZoneAirTemperature
  12416        \key OnIfHighZoneCooling
  12417        \key OnIfHighGlare
  12418        \note Following entry should be used only if Shading Type = SwitchableGlazing
  12419        \note and window is in a daylit zone
  12420        \key MeetDaylightIlluminanceSetpoint
  12421        \note The following three control types are used to reduce zone Heating load. They can be
  12422        \note used with any Shading Type but are most appropriate for opaque interior or exterior
  12423        \note shades with high insulating value ("opaque movable insulation")
  12424        \key OnNightIfLowOutdoorTempAndOffDay
  12425        \key OnNightIfLowInsideTempAndOffDay
  12426        \key OnNightIfHeatingAndOffDay
  12427        \note The following two control types are used to reduce zone heating and cooling load.
  12428        \note They can be used with any Shading Type but are most appropriate for translucent interior
  12429        \note or exterior shades with high insulating value ("translucent movable insulation")
  12430        \key OnNightIfLowOutdoorTempAndOnDayIfCooling
  12431        \key OnNightIfHeatingAndOnDayIfCooling
  12432        \note The following two control types are used to reduce zone Cooling load.
  12433        \note They can be used with any Shading Type but are most appropriate for interior
  12434        \note or exterior blinds,interior or exterior shades with low insulating value, or
  12435        \note switchable glazing
  12436        \key OffNightAndOnDayIfCoolingAndHighSolarOnWindow
  12437        \key OnNightAndOnDayIfCoolingAndHighSolarOnWindow
  12438        \note The following four control types require that both Setpoint and Setpoint2 be specified
  12439        \note Setpoint will correspond to outdoor air temp or zone air temp (deg C)
  12440        \note Setpoint2 will correspond to solar on window or horizontal solar (W/m2)
  12441        \key OnIfHighOutdoorAirTempAndHighSolarOnWindow
  12442        \key OnIfHighOutdoorAirTempAndHighHorizontalSolar
  12443        \key OnIfHighZoneAirTempAndHighSolarOnWindow
  12444        \key OnIfHighZoneAirTempAndHighHorizontalSolar
  12445   A6 , \field Schedule Name
  12446        \type object-list
  12447        \object-list ScheduleNames
  12448        \note Required if Shading Control Is Scheduled = Yes.
  12449        \note If schedule value = 1, shading control is active, i.e., shading can take place only
  12450        \note if the control test passes. If schedule value = 0, shading is off whether or not
  12451        \note the control test passes. Schedule Name is required if Shading Control Is Scheduled = Yes.
  12452        \note If Schedule Name is not specified, shading control is assumed to be active at all times.
  12453   N2 , \field Setpoint
  12454        \units W/m2, W or deg C
  12455        \note W/m2 for solar-based controls, W for cooling- or heating-based controls,
  12456        \note deg C for temperature-based controls.
  12457        \note Unused for Shading Control Type = AlwaysOn, AlwaysOff, OnIfScheduleAllows,
  12458        \note OnIfHighGlare, Glare, and DaylightIlluminance
  12459        \type real
  12460   A7 , \field Shading Control Is Scheduled
  12461        \type choice
  12462        \key No
  12463        \key Yes
  12464        \default No
  12465        \note If Yes, Schedule Name is required; if No, Schedule Name is not used.
  12466        \note Shading Control Is Scheduled = Yes is required if Shading Control Type = OnIfScheduleAllows.
  12467   A8 , \field Glare Control Is Active
  12468        \type choice
  12469        \key No
  12470        \key Yes
  12471        \default No
  12472        \note If Yes and window is in a daylit zone, shading is on if zone's discomfort glare index exceeds
  12473        \note the maximum discomfort glare index specified in the Daylighting object referenced by the zone.
  12474        \note The glare test is OR'ed with the test specified by Shading Control Type.
  12475        \note Glare Control Is Active = Yes is required if Shading Control Type = OnIfHighGlare.
  12476   A9 , \field Shading Device Material Name
  12477        \type object-list
  12478        \object-list WindowShadesScreensAndBlinds
  12479        \note Enter the name of a WindowMaterial:Shade, WindowMaterial:Screen or WindowMaterial:Blind object.
  12480        \note Required if "Construction with Shading Name" is not specified.
  12481        \note Not used if Shading Control Type = SwitchableGlazing, BetweenGlassShade, or BetweenGlassBlind.
  12482        \note If both "Construction with Shading Name" and "Shading Device Material Name" are entered,
  12483        \note the former takes precedence.
  12484   A10, \field Type of Slat Angle Control for Blinds
  12485        \type choice
  12486        \key FixedSlatAngle
  12487        \key ScheduledSlatAngle
  12488        \key BlockBeamSolar
  12489        \default FixedSlatAngle
  12490        \note Used only if Shading Type = InteriorBlind, ExteriorBlind or BetweenGlassBlind.
  12491        \note If choice is ScheduledSlatAngle then Slat Angle Schedule Name is required.
  12492   A11, \field Slat Angle Schedule Name
  12493        \type object-list
  12494        \object-list ScheduleNames
  12495        \note Used only if Shading Type = InteriorBlind, ExteriorBlind or BetweenGlassBlind.
  12496        \note Required if Type of Slat Angle Control for Blinds = ScheduledSlatAngle
  12497        \note Schedule values should be degrees (0 minimum, 180 maximum)
  12498   N3 , \field Setpoint 2
  12499        \units W/m2 or deg C
  12500        \note W/m2 for solar-based controls, deg C for temperature-based controls.
  12501        \note Used only as the second setpoint for the following two-setpoint control types:
  12502        \note OnIfHighOutdoorAirTempAndHighSolarOnWindow, OnIfHighOutdoorAirTempAndHighHorizontalSolar,
  12503        \note OnIfHighZoneAirTempAndHighSolarOnWindow, and OnIfHighZoneAirTempAndHighHorizontalSolar
  12504        \type real
  12505        \ip-units unknown
  12506   A12, \field Daylighting Control Object Name
  12507        \type object-list
  12508        \object-list DaylightingControlNames
  12509        \note Reference to the Daylighting:Controls object that provides the glare and illuminance control to the zone.
  12510   A13, \field Multiple Surface Control Type
  12511        \type choice
  12512        \key Sequential
  12513        \key Group
  12514        \default Sequential
  12515        \note When Sequential is used the list of fenestration surfaces are controlled individually in the order specified
  12516        \note When Group is used the entire list is controlled simultaneously and if glare control is needed the entire
  12517        \note group of window shades are deployed together a the same time
  12518   A14, \field Fenestration Surface 1 Name
  12519        \required-field
  12520        \begin-extensible
  12521        \type object-list
  12522        \object-list GlazedExtSubSurfNames
  12523        \note When Multiple Surface Control Type is set to Sequential the shades will be deployed for the referenced surface objects in order.
  12524        \note When that field is set to Group the entire list is controlled simultaneously.
  12525   A15, \field Fenestration Surface 2 Name
  12526        \type object-list
  12527        \object-list GlazedExtSubSurfNames
  12528        \note When Multiple Surface Control Type is set to Sequential the shades will be deployed for the referenced surface objects in order.
  12529        \note When that field is set to Group the entire list is controlled simultaneously.
  12530   A16, \field Fenestration Surface 3 Name
  12531        \type object-list
  12532        \object-list GlazedExtSubSurfNames
  12533        \note When Multiple Surface Control Type is set to Sequential the shades will be deployed for the referenced surface objects in order.
  12534        \note When that field is set to Group the entire list is controlled simultaneously.
  12535   A17, \field Fenestration Surface 4 Name
  12536        \type object-list
  12537        \object-list GlazedExtSubSurfNames
  12538        \note When Multiple Surface Control Type is set to Sequential the shades will be deployed for the referenced surface objects in order.
  12539        \note When that field is set to Group the entire list is controlled simultaneously.
  12540   A18, \field Fenestration Surface 5 Name
  12541        \type object-list
  12542        \object-list GlazedExtSubSurfNames
  12543        \note When Multiple Surface Control Type is set to Sequential the shades will be deployed for the referenced surface objects in order.
  12544        \note When that field is set to Group the entire list is controlled simultaneously.
  12545   A19, \field Fenestration Surface 6 Name
  12546        \type object-list
  12547        \object-list GlazedExtSubSurfNames
  12548        \note When Multiple Surface Control Type is set to Sequential the shades will be deployed for the referenced surface objects in order.
  12549        \note When that field is set to Group the entire list is controlled simultaneously.
  12550   A20, \field Fenestration Surface 7 Name
  12551        \type object-list
  12552        \object-list GlazedExtSubSurfNames
  12553        \note When Multiple Surface Control Type is set to Sequential the shades will be deployed for the referenced surface objects in order.
  12554        \note When that field is set to Group the entire list is controlled simultaneously.
  12555   A21, \field Fenestration Surface 8 Name
  12556        \type object-list
  12557        \object-list GlazedExtSubSurfNames
  12558        \note When Multiple Surface Control Type is set to Sequential the shades will be deployed for the referenced surface objects in order.
  12559        \note When that field is set to Group the entire list is controlled simultaneously.
  12560   A22, \field Fenestration Surface 9 Name
  12561        \type object-list
  12562        \object-list GlazedExtSubSurfNames
  12563        \note When Multiple Surface Control Type is set to Sequential the shades will be deployed for the referenced surface objects in order.
  12564        \note When that field is set to Group the entire list is controlled simultaneously.
  12565   A23; \field Fenestration Surface 10 Name
  12566        \type object-list
  12567        \object-list GlazedExtSubSurfNames
  12568        \note When Multiple Surface Control Type is set to Sequential the shades will be deployed for the referenced surface objects in order.
