  14034 Shading:Building:Detailed,
  14035   \extensible:3 -- duplicate last set of x,y,z coordinates, renumbering please (and changing z terminator to , for all but last)
  14036        \memo used for shading elements such as trees, other buildings, parts of this building not being modeled
  14037        \memo these items are relative to the current building and would move with relative geometry
  14038        \format vertices
  14039        \min-fields 12
  14040   A1 , \field Name
  14041        \required-field
  14042        \type alpha
  14043        \reference AllShadingAndHTSurfNames
  14044        \reference AllShadingSurfNames
  14045   A2,  \field Transmittance Schedule Name
  14046        \note Transmittance schedule for the shading device, defaults to zero (always opaque)
  14047        \type object-list
  14048        \object-list ScheduleNames
  14049   N1 , \field Number of Vertices
  14050        \note shown with 6 vertex coordinates -- extensible object
  14051        \autocalculatable
  14052        \default autocalculate
  14053        \minimum 3
  14054        \note Rules for vertices are given in GlobalGeometryRules coordinates --
  14055        \note For this object all surface coordinates are relative to the building origin (0,0,0)
  14056        \note and will rotate with the BUILDING north axis.
  14057   N2,  \field Vertex 1 X-coordinate
