  20748 \group Internal Gains
  20749 
  20750 People,
  20751    \memo Sets internal gains and contaminant rates for occupants in the zone.
  20752    \memo If you use a ZoneList in the Zone or ZoneList name field then this definition applies
  20753    \memo to all the zones in the ZoneList.
  20754    \min-fields 10
  20755   A1 , \field Name
  20756        \required-field
  20757        \type alpha
  20758        \reference PeopleNames
  20759   A2 , \field Zone or ZoneList Name
  20760        \required-field
  20761        \type object-list
  20762        \object-list ZoneAndZoneListNames
  20763   A3 , \field Number of People Schedule Name
  20764        \required-field
  20765        \type object-list
  20766        \note units in schedule should be fraction applied to number of people (0.0 - 1.0)
  20767        \object-list ScheduleNames
  20768   A4 , \field Number of People Calculation Method
  20769        \note The entered calculation method is used to create the maximum number of people
  20770        \note for this set of attributes (i.e. sensible fraction, schedule, etc)
  20771        \note Choices: People -- simply enter number of occupants.
  20772        \note People per Zone Floor Area -- enter the number to apply.  Value * Floor Area = Number of people
  20773        \note Zone Floor Area per Person -- enter the number to apply.  Floor Area / Value = Number of people
  20774        \type choice
  20775        \key People
  20776        \key People/Area
  20777        \key Area/Person
  20778        \default People
  20779   N1 , \field Number of People
  20780        \type real
  20781        \minimum 0
  20782   N2 , \field People per Zone Floor Area
  20783        \type real
  20784        \minimum 0
  20785        \units person/m2
  20786   N3 , \field Zone Floor Area per Person
  20787        \type real
  20788        \minimum 0
  20789        \units m2/person
  20790   N4 , \field Fraction Radiant
  20791        \type real
  20792        \minimum 0.0
  20793        \maximum 1.0
  20794        \default 0.3
  20795        \note This is radiant fraction of the sensible heat released by people in a zone. This value will be
  20796        \note multiplied by the total sensible heat released by people yields the amount of long wavelength
  20797        \note radiation gain from people in a zone. Default value is 0.30.
  20798   N5,  \field Sensible Heat Fraction
  20799        \note if input, overrides program calculated sensible/latent split
  20800        \autocalculatable
  20801        \default autocalculate
  20802        \minimum 0.0
  20803        \maximum 1.0
  20804   A5 , \field Activity Level Schedule Name
  20805        \required-field
  20806        \note Note that W has to be converted to mets in TC routine
  20807        \type object-list
  20808        \note units in schedule are W/person
  20809        \object-list ScheduleNames
  20810   N6 , \field Carbon Dioxide Generation Rate
  20811        \note CO2 generation rate per unit of activity level.
  20812        \type real
  20813        \units m3/s-W
  20814        \default 3.82E-8
  20815        \minimum 0.0
  20816        \maximum 3.82E-7
  20817        \note The default value is obtained from ASHRAE Std 62.1 at 0.0084 cfm/met/person over
  20818        \note the general adult population.
  20819   A6 , \field Enable ASHRAE 55 Comfort Warnings
  20820        \type choice
  20821        \key Yes
  20822        \key No
  20823        \default No
  20824   A7 , \field Mean Radiant Temperature Calculation Type
  20825        \note optional (only required for thermal comfort runs)
  20826        \type choice
  20827        \key ZoneAveraged
  20828        \key SurfaceWeighted
  20829        \key AngleFactor
  20830        \default ZoneAveraged
  20831   A8 , \field Surface Name/Angle Factor List Name
  20832        \type object-list
  20833        \object-list AllHeatTranAngFacNames
  20834        \note optional (only required for runs of thermal comfort models: Fanger, Pierce and KSU)
  20835   A9 , \field Work Efficiency Schedule Name
  20836        \type object-list
  20837        \object-list ScheduleNames
  20838        \note units in schedule are 0.0 to 1.0
  20839        \note optional (only required for runs of thermal comfort models: Fanger, Pierce and KSU)
  20840   A10, \field Clothing Insulation Calculation Method
  20841        \type choice
  20842        \key ClothingInsulationSchedule
  20843        \key DynamicClothingModelASHRAE55
  20844        \key CalculationMethodSchedule
  20845        \default ClothingInsulationSchedule
  20846   A11, \field Clothing Insulation Calculation Method Schedule Name
  20847        \type object-list
  20848        \object-list ScheduleNames
  20849        \note a schedule value of 1 for the Scheduled method, and 2 for the DynamicClothingModelASHRAE55 method
  20850   A12, \field Clothing Insulation Schedule Name
  20851        \type object-list
  20852        \object-list ScheduleNames
  20853        \note use "Clo" from ASHRAE or Thermal Comfort guides
  20854        \note optional (only required for runs of thermal comfort models: Fanger, Pierce and KSU)
  20855   A13, \field Air Velocity Schedule Name
  20856        \type object-list
  20857        \object-list ScheduleNames
  20858        \note units in the schedule are m/s
  20859        \note optional (only required for runs of thermal comfort models: Fanger, Pierce and KSU)
  20860   A14, \field Thermal Comfort Model 1 Type
  20861        \type choice
  20862        \key Fanger
  20863        \key Pierce
  20864        \key KSU
  20865        \key AdaptiveASH55
  20866        \key AdaptiveCEN15251
  20867        \note optional (only needed for people thermal comfort results reporting)
  20868   A15, \field Thermal Comfort Model 2 Type
  20869        \type choice
  20870        \key Fanger
  20871        \key Pierce
  20872        \key KSU
  20873        \key AdaptiveASH55
  20874        \key AdaptiveCEN15251
  20875        \note optional (second type of thermal comfort model and results reporting)
  20876   A16, \field Thermal Comfort Model 3 Type
  20877        \type choice
  20878        \key Fanger
  20879        \key Pierce
  20880        \key KSU
  20881        \key AdaptiveASH55
  20882        \key AdaptiveCEN15251
  20883        \note optional (third thermal comfort model and report type)
  20884   A17, \field Thermal Comfort Model 4 Type
  20885        \type choice
  20886        \key Fanger
  20887        \key Pierce
  20888        \key KSU
  20889        \key AdaptiveASH55
  20890        \key AdaptiveCEN15251
  20891        \note optional (fourth thermal comfort model and report type)
  20892   A18; \field Thermal Comfort Model 5 Type
  20893        \type choice
  20894        \key Fanger
  20895        \key Pierce
  20896        \key KSU
  20897        \key AdaptiveASH55
  20898        \key AdaptiveCEN15251
  20899        \note optional (fifth thermal comfort model and report type)
  20900 
