  21515        \type object-list
  21516        \object-list ZoneNames
  21517   A3 , \field Air Flow Calculation Method
  21518        \note The specified method is used to calculate the IT inlet temperature and zone return
  21519        \note air temperature. If FlowFromSystem is chosen, the zone is assumed to be well-mixed.
  21520        \note If FlowControlWithApproachTemperatures is chosen, Supply and Return approach temperature
  21521        \note should be defined to indicate the temperature difference due to the air distribution. When
  21522        \note FlowControlWithApproachTemperatures is chosen, the inputs of Air Inlet Connection Type, Design Recirculation Fraction
  21523        \note and Recirculation Function of Loading and Supply Temperature Curve Name are ignored. For multiple
  21524        \note ITE objects defined for one zone, the same calculation method should apply.
  21525        \note The FlowControlWithApproachTemperatures only applies to ITE zones with single duct VAV terminal unit.
  21526        \note Other return air heat gains from window or lights are not allowed when FlowControlWithApproachTemperatures is chosen.
  21527        \type choice
  21528        \key FlowFromSystem
  21529        \key FlowControlWithApproachTemperatures
  21530        \default FlowFromSystem
  21531   A4 , \field Design Power Input Calculation Method
  21532        \note The entered calculation method is used to specify the design power input
  21533        \note Watts/Unit => Watts per Unit -- Design Power = Watts per Unit * Number of Units
  21534        \note Watts/Area => Watts per Zone Floor Area -- Design Power = Watts per Zone Floor Area * Floor Area
  21535        \type choice
  21536        \key Watts/Unit
  21537        \key Watts/Area
  21538        \default Watts/Unit
  21539   N1 , \field Watts per Unit
  21540        \units W
  21541        \type real
  21542        \minimum 0
  21543        \ip-units W
  21544   N2 , \field Number of Units
  21545        \type real
  21546        \minimum 0
  21547        \default 1
  21548   N3 , \field Watts per Zone Floor Area
  21549        \type real
  21550        \minimum 0
  21551        \units W/m2
  21552        \ip-units W/ft2
  21553   A5 , \field Design Power Input Schedule Name
  21554        \note Operating schedule for this equipment, fraction applied to the design power input,
  21555        \note generally (0.0 - 1.0)
  21556        \note If this field is blank, the schedule is assumed to always be 1.0.
  21557        \type object-list
  21558        \object-list ScheduleNames
  21559   A6 , \field CPU Loading  Schedule Name
  21560        \note CPU loading schedule for this equipment as a fraction from 0.0 (idle) to 1.0 (full load).
  21561        \note If this field is blank, the schedule is assumed to always be 1.0.
  21562        \type object-list
  21563        \object-list ScheduleNames
  21564   A7 , \field CPU Power Input Function of Loading and Air Temperature Curve Name
  21565        \required-field
  21566        \type object-list
  21567        \object-list BivariateFunctions
  21568        \note The name of a two-variable curve or table lookup object which modifies the CPU power
  21569        \note input as a function of CPU loading (x) and air inlet node temperature (y).
  21570        \note This curve (table) should equal 1.0 at design conditions (CPU loading = 1.0 and
  21571        \note Design Entering Air Temperature).
  21572   N4 , \field Design Fan Power Input Fraction
  21573        \note The fraction of the total power input at design conditions which is for the cooling fan(s)
  21574        \type real
  21575        \minimum 0.0
  21576        \maximum 1.0
  21577        \default 0.0
  21578   N5,  \field Design Fan Air Flow Rate per Power Input
  21579        \note The cooling fan air flow rate per total electric power input at design conditions
  21580        \required-field
  21581        \type real
  21582        \units m3/s-W
  21583        \minimum 0.0
  21584   A8 , \field Air Flow Function of Loading and Air Temperature Curve Name
  21585        \required-field
  21586        \type object-list
  21587        \object-list BivariateFunctions
  21588        \note The name of a two-variable curve or table lookup object which modifies the cooling
  21589        \note air flow rate as a function of CPU loading (x) and air inlet node temperature (y).
  21590        \note This curve (table) should equal 1.0 at design conditions (CPU loading = 1.0 and
  21591        \note Design Entering Air Temperature).
  21592   A9 , \field Fan Power Input Function of Flow Curve Name
  21593        \required-field
  21594        \type object-list
  21595        \object-list UnivariateFunctions
  21596        \note The name of a single-variable curve or table lookup object which modifies the cooling
  21597        \note fan power as a function of flow fraction (x).
  21598        \note This curve (table) should equal 1.0 at a flow fraction of 1.0.
  21599   N6,  \field Design Entering Air Temperature
  21600        \note The entering air temperature at design conditions.
  21601        \type real
  21602        \units C
  21603        \default 15.0
  21604   A10, \field Environmental Class
  21605        \note Specifies the allowable operating conditions for the air inlet conditions.
  21606        \note Used for reporting time outside allowable conditions.
  21607        \type choice
  21608        \key None
  21609        \key A1
  21610        \key A2
  21611        \key A3
  21612        \key A4
  21613        \key B
  21614        \key C
  21615        \default None
  21616   A11, \field Air Inlet Connection Type
  21617        \note Specifies the type of connection between the zone and the ITE air inlet node.
  21618        \note AdjustedSupply = ITE inlet temperature will be the current Supply Air Node temperature
  21619        \note adjusted by the current recirculation fraction.
  21620        \note All heat output is added to the zone air heat balance as a convective gain.
  21621        \note ZoneAirNode = ITE air inlet condition is  the average zone condition.
  21622        \note All heat output is added to the zone air heat balance as a convective gain.
  21623        \note RoomAirModel = ITE air inlet and outlet are connected to room air model nodes.
  21624        \note This field is only used when Air Flow Calculation Method is FlowFromSystem.
  21625        \type choice
  21626        \key AdjustedSupply
  21627        \key ZoneAirNode
  21628        \key RoomAirModel
  21629        \default AdjustedSupply
  21630   A12, \field Air Inlet Room Air Model Node Name
  21631        \note Name of a RoomAir:Node object which is connected to the ITE air inlet.
  21632        \type object-list
  21633        \object-list RoomAirNodes
  21634   A13, \field Air Outlet Room Air Model Node Name
  21635        \note Name of a RoomAir:Node object which is connected to the ITE air outlet.
  21636        \type object-list
  21637        \object-list RoomAirNodes
  21638   A14, \field Supply Air Node Name
  21639        \note Name of the supply air inlet node serving this ITE. Required if the
  21640        \note Air Node Connection Type = AdjustedSupply. Also required if
  21641        \note Calculation Method = FlowControlWithApproachTemperatures. Also required if reporting of
  21642        \note Supply Heat Index is desired.
  21643        \type node
  21644   N7,  \field Design Recirculation Fraction
  21645        \note The recirculation fraction for this equipment at design conditions. This field is used only
  21646        \note if the Air Node Connection Type = AdjustedSupply. The default is 0.0 (no recirculation).
  21647        \note This field is only used when Air Flow Calculation Method is FlowFromSystem.
  21648        \type real
  21649        \minimum 0.0
  21650        \maximum 0.5
  21651        \default 0.0
  21652   A15, \field Recirculation Function of Loading and Supply Temperature Curve Name
  21653        \type object-list
  21654        \object-list BivariateFunctions
  21655        \note The name of a two-variable curve or table lookup object which modifies the recirculation
  21656        \note fractionas a function of CPU loading (x) and supply air node temperature (y).
  21657        \note This curve (table) should equal 1.0 at design conditions (CPU loading = 1.0 and
  21658        \note Design Entering Air Temperature).This field is used only if the
  21659        \note Air Node Connection Type = AdjustedSupply. If this curve is left blank, then the curve
  21660        \note is assumed to always equal 1.0.
  21661        \note This field is only used when Air Flow Calculation Method is FlowFromSystem.
  21662   N8 , \field Design Electric Power Supply Efficiency
  21663        \note The efficiency of the power supply system serving this ITE
  21664        \type real
  21665        \minimum> 0.0
  21666        \maximum 1.0
  21667        \default 1.0
  21668   A16, \field Electric Power Supply Efficiency Function of Part Load Ratio Curve Name
  21669        \type object-list
  21670        \object-list UnivariateFunctions
  21671        \note The name of a single-variable curve or table lookup object which modifies the electric
  21672        \note power supply efficiency as a function of part-load ratio (x).
  21673        \note This curve (table) should equal 1.0 at full load (PLR = 1.0).
  21674        \note If this curve is left blank, then the curve is assumed to always equal 1.0.
  21675   N9 , \field Fraction of Electric Power Supply Losses to Zone
  21676        \note Fraction of the electric power supply losses which are a heat gain to the zone
  21677        \note If this field is <1.0, the remainder of the losses are assumed to be lost to the outdoors.
  21678        \type real
  21679        \minimum 0.0
  21680        \maximum 1.0
  21681        \default 1.0
  21682   A17, \field CPU End-Use Subcategory
  21683        \note Any text may be used here to categorize the end-uses in the ABUPS End Uses by Subcategory table.
  21684        \type alpha
  21685        \retaincase
  21686        \default ITE-CPU
  21687   A18, \field Fan End-Use Subcategory
  21688        \note Any text may be used here to categorize the end-uses in the ABUPS End Uses by Subcategory table.
  21689        \type alpha
  21690        \retaincase
  21691        \default ITE-Fans
  21692   A19, \field Electric Power Supply End-Use Subcategory
  21693        \note Any text may be used here to categorize the end-uses in the ABUPS End Uses by Subcategory table.
  21694        \type alpha
  21695        \retaincase
  21696        \default ITE-UPS
  21697   N10, \field Supply Temperature Difference
  21698        \note The difference of the IT inlet temperature from the AHU supply air temperature.
  21699        \note Either Supply Temperature Difference or Supply Temperature Difference Schedule is required if Air Flow Calculation Method is set to FlowControlWithApproachTemperatures.
  21700        \note This field is ignored when Air Flow Calculation Method is FlowFromSystem.
  21701        \type real
  21702        \units deltaC
  21703   A20, \field Supply Temperature Difference Schedule
  21704        \note The difference schedule of the IT inlet temperature from the AHU supply air temperature.
  21705        \note Either Supply Temperature Difference or Supply Temperature Difference Schedule is required if Air Flow Calculation Method is set to FlowControlWithApproachTemperatures.
  21706        \note This field is ignored when Air Flow Calculation Method is FlowFromSystem.
  21707        \type object-list
  21708        \object-list ScheduleNames
  21709   N11, \field Return Temperature Difference
  21710        \note The difference of the the actual AHU return air temperature to the IT equipment outlet temperature.
  21711        \note Either Return Temperature Difference or Return Temperature Difference Schedule is required if Air Flow Calculation Method is set to FlowControlWithApproachTemperatures.
  21712        \note This field is ignored when Air Flow Calculation Method is FlowFromSystem.
  21713        \type real
  21714        \units deltaC
  21715   A21; \field Return Temperature Difference Schedule
  21716        \note The difference schedule of the actual AHU return air temperature to the IT equipment outlet temperature.
  21717        \note Either Return Temperature Difference or Return Temperature Difference Schedule is required if Air Flow Calculation Method is set to FlowControlWithApproachTemperatures.
  21718        \note This field is ignored when Air Flow Calculation Method is FlowFromSystem.
  21719        \type object-list
  21720        \object-list ScheduleNames
