  22490 OutputControl:IlluminanceMap:Style,
  22491        \memo default style for the Daylighting Illuminance Map is comma -- this works well for
  22492        \memo importing into spreadsheet programs such as Excel(tm) but not so well for word
  22493        \memo processing programs -- there tab may be a better choice.  fixed puts spaces between
  22494        \memo the "columns"
  22495        \unique-object
  22496    A1; \field Column Separator
  22497        \type choice
  22498        \key Comma
  22499        \key Tab
  22500        \key Fixed
  22501        \default Comma
  22502 
  22503 \group Zone Airflow
  22504 
  22505 ZoneInfiltration:DesignFlowRate,
  22506        \memo  Infiltration is specified as a design level which is modified by a Schedule fraction, temperature difference and wind speed:
  22507        \memo  Infiltration=Idesign * FSchedule * (A + B*|(Tzone-Todb)| + C*WindSpd + D * WindSpd**2)
  22508        \memo If you use a ZoneList in the Zone or ZoneList name field then this definition applies
  22509        \memo to all the zones in the ZoneList.
  22510        \min-fields 12
  22511   A1 , \field Name
  22512        \required-field
  22513        \type alpha
  22514   A2 , \field Zone or ZoneList Name
  22515        \required-field
  22516        \type object-list
  22517        \object-list ZoneAndZoneListNames
  22518   A3 , \field Schedule Name
  22519        \required-field
  22520        \type object-list
  22521        \object-list ScheduleNames
  22522   A4 , \field Design Flow Rate Calculation Method
  22523        \note The entered calculation method is used to create the maximum amount of infiltration
  22524        \note for this set of attributes
  22525        \note Choices: Flow/Zone => Design Flow Rate -- simply enter Design Flow Rate
  22526        \note Flow/Area => Flow per Zone Floor Area - Value * Floor Area (zone) = Design Flow Rate
  22527        \note Flow/ExteriorArea => Flow per Exterior Surface Area - Value * Exterior Surface Area (zone) = Design Flow Rate
  22528        \note Flow/ExteriorWallArea => Flow per Exterior Surface Area - Value * Exterior Wall Surface Area (zone) = Design Flow Rate
  22529        \note AirChanges/Hour => Air Changes per Hour - Value * Floor Volume (zone) adjusted for m3/s = Design Volume Flow Rate
  22530        \note  "Idesign" in Equation is the result.
  22531        \type choice
  22532        \key Flow/Zone
  22533        \key Flow/Area
  22534        \key Flow/ExteriorArea
  22535        \key Flow/ExteriorWallArea
  22536        \key AirChanges/Hour
  22537        \default Flow/Zone
  22538   N1 , \field Design Flow Rate
  22539        \units m3/s
  22540        \type real
  22541        \minimum 0
  22542        \ip-units ft3/min
  22543   N2 , \field Flow per Zone Floor Area
  22544        \type real
  22545        \minimum 0
  22546        \units m3/s-m2
  22547   N3 , \field Flow per Exterior Surface Area
  22548        \note use key Flow/ExteriorArea for all exterior surface area
  22549        \note use key Flow/ExteriorWallArea to include only exterior wall area
  22550        \units m3/s-m2
  22551        \type real
  22552        \minimum 0
  22553   N4 , \field Air Changes per Hour
  22554        \units 1/hr
  22555        \type real
  22556        \minimum 0
  22557   N5 , \field Constant Term Coefficient
  22558        \note  "A" in Equation
  22559        \type real
  22560        \default 1
  22561   N6 , \field Temperature Term Coefficient
  22562        \note  "B" in Equation
  22563        \type real
  22564        \default 0
  22565   N7 , \field Velocity Term Coefficient
  22566        \note  "C" in Equation
  22567        \type real
  22568        \default 0
  22569   N8 ; \field Velocity Squared Term Coefficient
  22570        \note  "D" in Equation
  22571        \type real
  22572        \default 0
  22573 
  22574 ZoneInfiltration:EffectiveLeakageArea,
  22575        \min-fields 6
  22576        \memo  Infiltration is specified as effective leakage area at 4 Pa, schedule fraction, stack and wind coefficients, and
  22577        \memo  is a function of temperature difference and wind speed:
  22578        \memo  Infiltration=FSchedule * (AL /1000) SQRT(Cs*|(Tzone-Todb)| +  Cw*WindSpd**2 )
  22579   A1 , \field Name
  22580        \required-field
  22581        \type alpha
  22582   A2 , \field Zone Name
  22583        \required-field
  22584        \type object-list
  22585        \object-list ZoneNames
  22586   A3 , \field Schedule Name
  22587        \required-field
  22588        \type object-list
  22589        \object-list ScheduleNames
  22590   N1 , \field Effective Air Leakage Area
  22591        \units cm2
  22592        \note "AL" in Equation
  22593        \note units are cm2 (square centimeters)
  22594        \minimum> 0
  22595        \type real
  22596        \required-field
  22597   N2 , \field Stack Coefficient
  22598        \note "Cs" in Equation
  22599        \minimum> 0
  22600        \type real
  22601        \required-field
  22602   N3 ; \field Wind Coefficient
  22603        \note "Cw" in Equation
  22604        \minimum> 0
  22605        \type real
  22606        \required-field
  22607 
  22608 ZoneInfiltration:FlowCoefficient,
  22609        \min-fields 8
  22610        \memo  Infiltration is specified as flow coefficient, schedule fraction, stack and wind coefficients, and
  22611        \memo  is a function of temperature difference and wind speed:
  22612        \memo  Infiltration=FSchedule * SQRT( (c * Cs*|(Tzone-Todb)|**n)**2 + (c* Cw*(s * WindSpd)**2n)**2 )
  22613   A1 , \field Name
  22614        \required-field
  22615        \type alpha
  22616   A2 , \field Zone Name
  22617        \required-field
  22618        \type object-list
  22619        \object-list ZoneNames
  22620   A3 , \field Schedule Name
  22621        \required-field
  22622        \type object-list
  22623        \object-list ScheduleNames
  22624   N1 , \field Flow Coefficient
  22625        \note "c" in Equation
  22626        \minimum> 0
  22627        \type real
  22628        \required-field
  22629   N2 , \field Stack Coefficient
  22630        \note "Cs" in Equation
  22631        \minimum> 0
  22632        \type real
  22633        \required-field
  22634   N3 , \field Pressure Exponent
  22635        \note "n" in Equation
  22636        \minimum> 0
  22637        \type real
  22638        \default 0.67
  22639   N4 , \field Wind Coefficient
  22640        \note "Cw" in Equation
  22641        \minimum> 0
  22642        \type real
  22643        \required-field
  22644   N5 ; \field Shelter Factor
  22645        \note "s" in Equation
  22646        \minimum> 0
  22647        \type real
  22648        \required-field
  22649 
  22650 ZoneVentilation:DesignFlowRate,
  22651    \memo  Ventilation is specified as a design level which is modified by a schedule fraction, temperature difference and wind speed:
  22652    \memo  Ventilation=Vdesign * Fschedule * (A + B*|(Tzone-Todb)| + C*WindSpd + D * WindSpd**2)
  22653    \memo If you use a ZoneList in the Zone or ZoneList name field then this definition applies
  22654    \memo to all the zones in the ZoneList.
  22655    \min-fields 15
  22656   A1 , \field Name
  22657        \required-field
  22658        \type alpha
  22659        \reference VentilationNames
  22660   A2 , \field Zone or ZoneList Name
  22661        \required-field
  22662        \type object-list
  22663        \object-list ZoneAndZoneListNames
  22664   A3 , \field Schedule Name
  22665        \required-field
  22666        \type object-list
  22667        \object-list ScheduleNames
  22668   A4 , \field Design Flow Rate Calculation Method
  22669        \note The entered calculation method is used to create the maximum amount of ventilation
  22670        \note for this set of attributes
  22671        \note Choices: Flow/Zone => Design Flow Rate -- simply enter Design Flow Rate
  22672        \note Flow/Area => Flow Rate per Zone Floor Area - Value * Floor Area (zone) = Design Flow Rate
  22673        \note Flow/Person => Flow Rate per Person - Value * #people = Design Flow Rate
  22674        \note AirChanges/Hour => Air Changes per Hour - Value * Floor Volume (zone) adjusted for m3/s = Design Volume Flow Rate
  22675        \note  "Vdesign" in Equation is the result.
  22676        \type choice
  22677        \key Flow/Zone
  22678        \key Flow/Area
  22679        \key Flow/Person
  22680        \key AirChanges/Hour
  22681        \default Flow/Zone
