  23152 ZoneRefrigerationDoorMixing,
  23153   \min-fields 4
  23154        \memo Refrigeration Door Mixing is used for an opening between two zones that are at the
  23155        \memo   same elevation but have different air temperatures.  In this case, the mixing air flow
  23156        \memo   between the two zones is determined by the density difference between the two zones.
  23157        \memo   This would typically be used between two zones in a refrigerated warehouse that are
  23158        \memo   controlled at different temperatures.  It could also be used to model a door to a walk-in
  23159        \memo   refrigerated space if that space were modeled as a zone instead of using the object Refrigeration:WalkIn.
  23160   A1 , \field Name
  23161        \required-field
  23162        \type alpha
  23163   A2 , \field Zone 1 Name
  23164        \required-field
  23165        \type object-list
  23166        \object-list ZoneNames
  23167   A3 , \field Zone 2 Name
  23168        \required-field
  23169        \type object-list
  23170        \object-list ZoneNames
  23171   A4 , \field Schedule Name
  23172        \note This schedule defines the fraction of the time the refrigeration door is open
  23173        \note  For example, if the warehouse is closed at night and there are no door openings
  23174        \note   between two zones, the value for that time period would be 0.
  23175        \note   If doors were propped open, the value  over that time period would be 1.0
  23176        \note   If the doors were open about 20% of the time, the value over that period would be 0.2
  23177        \note   Schedule values must lie between 0 and 1.0
  23178        \required-field
  23179        \type object-list
  23180        \object-list ScheduleNames
  23181   N1 , \field Door Height
  23182        \units m
  23183        \type real
  23184        \minimum 0
  23185        \maximum 50.
  23186        \default 3.0
  23187   N2 , \field Door Area
  23188        \type real
  23189        \minimum 0
  23190        \maximum 400.
  23191        \default 9.
  23192        \units m2
  23193   A5;  \field Door Protection Type
  23194        \note Door protection can reduce the air flow through a refrigeration door
  23195        \note The default value is "None"
  23196        \note Choices: "None", "AirCurtain", and "StripCurtain"
  23197        \note A strip curtain reduces the air flow more than an air curtain
  23198        \type choice
  23199        \key None
  23200        \key AirCurtain
  23201        \key StripCurtain
  23202        \default None
  23203 
  23204 ZoneEarthtube,
