  23321 ZoneCoolTower:Shower,
  23322      \memo A cooltower (sometimes referred to as a wind tower or a shower cooling tower)
  23323      \memo models passive downdraught evaporative cooling (PDEC) that is designed to capture the
  23324      \memo wind at the top of a tower and cool the outdoor air using water evaporation before
  23325      \memo delivering it to a space.
  23326  A1, \field Name
  23327      \required-field
  23328  A2, \field Availability Schedule Name
  23329      \note Availability schedule name for this system. Schedule value > 0 means the system is available.
  23330      \note If this field is blank, the system is always available.
  23331      \type object-list
  23332      \object-list ScheduleNames
  23333  A3, \field Zone Name
  23334      \required-field
  23335      \type object-list
  23336      \object-list ZoneNames
  23337  A4, \field Water Supply Storage Tank Name
  23338      \note In case of stand alone tank or underground water, leave this input blank
  23339      \type object-list
  23340      \object-list WaterStorageTankNames
  23341  A5, \field Flow Control Type
  23342      \note Water flow schedule should be selected when the water flow rate is known.
  23343      \note Wind-driven flow should be selected when the water flow rate is unknown.
  23344      \type choice
  23345      \key WaterFlowSchedule
  23346      \key WindDrivenFlow
  23347      \default WindDrivenFlow
  23348  A6, \field Pump Flow Rate Schedule Name
  23349      \required-field
  23350      \type object-list
  23351      \object-list ScheduleNames
  23352  N1, \field Maximum Water Flow Rate
  23353      \required-field
  23354      \units m3/s
  23355      \ip-units gal/min
  23356      \type real
  23357  N2, \field Effective Tower Height
  23358      \note This field is from either the spray or the wet pad to the top of the outlet.
  23359      \required-field
  23360      \units m
  23361      \type real
  23362  N3, \field Airflow Outlet Area
  23363      \note User have to specify effective area when outlet area is relatively bigger than the cross sectional area
  23364      \note of cooltower. If the number of outlet is more than one, assume the air passes through only one.
  23365      \required-field
  23366      \units m2
  23367      \type real
  23368  N4, \field Maximum Air Flow Rate
  23369      \required-field
  23370      \units m3/s
  23371      \type real
  23372      \minimum 0
  23373  N5, \field Minimum Indoor Temperature
  23374      \required-field
  23375      \note This field is to specify the indoor temperature below which cooltower is shutoff.
  23376      \units C
  23377      \type real
  23378      \minimum -100
  23379      \maximum 100
  23380  N6, \field Fraction of Water Loss
  23381      \minimum 0
  23382      \maximum 1
  23383  N7, \field Fraction of Flow Schedule
  23384      \minimum 0
  23385      \maximum 1
  23386  N8; \field Rated Power Consumption
  23387      \required-field
  23388      \units W
  23389      \type real
  23390 
  23391 ZoneThermalChimney,
  23392        \memo A thermal chimney is a vertical shaft utilizing solar radiation to enhance natural
  23393        \memo ventilation. It consists of an absorber wall, air gap and glass cover with high solar
  23394        \memo transmissivity.
  23395    \min-fields 10
