  25536 AirflowNetwork:OccupantVentilationControl,
  25537       \memo This object is used to provide advanced thermal comfort control of window opening and closing
  25538       \memo for both exterior and interior windows.
  25539   A1, \field Name
  25540       \required-field
  25541       \type alpha
  25542       \reference AirflowNetworkOccupantVentilationControlNames
  25543       \note Enter the name where the advanced thermal comfort control is required.
  25544   N1, \field Minimum Opening Time
  25545       \type real
  25546       \units minutes
  25547       \minimum 0.0
  25548       \default 0.0
  25549   N2, \field Minimum Closing Time
  25550       \type real
  25551       \units minutes
  25552       \minimum 0.0
  25553       \default 0.0
  25554   A2, \field Thermal Comfort Low Temperature Curve Name
  25555       \type object-list
  25556       \object-list UnivariateFunctions
  25557       \note Enter a curve name that represents thermal comfort temperature as a
  25558       \note function of outdoor dry-bulb temperature. Up to two curves are allowed if the
  25559       \note performance cannot be represented by a single curve.
  25560       \note The following two fields are used if two curves are required.
  25561   N3, \field Thermal Comfort Temperature Boundary Point
  25562       \type real
  25563       \units C
  25564       \minimum 0.0
  25565       \default 10.0
  25566       \note This point is used to allow separate low and high thermal comfort temperature
  25567       \note curves. If a single performance curve is used, leave this field blank.
  25568   A3, \field Thermal Comfort High Temperature Curve Name
  25569       \type object-list
  25570       \object-list UnivariateFunctions
  25571       \note Enter a curve name that represents thermal comfort temperature as a
  25572       \note function of outdoor dry-bulb temperature. Up to two curves are allowed if the
  25573       \note performance cannot be represented by a single curve.
  25574       \note If a single performance curve is used, leave this field blank.
  25575   N4, \field Maximum Threshold for Persons Dissatisfied PPD
  25576       \type real
  25577       \units percent
  25578       \minimum 0
  25579       \maximum 100
  25580       \default 10.0
  25581   A4, \field Occupancy Check
  25582       \note If Yes, occupancy check will be performed as part of the opening probability check.
  25583       \type choice
  25584       \key Yes
  25585       \key No
  25586       \default No
  25587   A5, \field Opening Probability Schedule Name
  25588       \type object-list
  25589       \object-list ScheduleNames
  25590       \note If this field is blank, the opening probability check is bypassed and opening is true.
  25591   A6; \field Closing Probability Schedule Name
  25592       \type object-list
  25593       \object-list ScheduleNames
  25594       \note If this field is blank, the closing probability check is bypassed and closing is true.
  25595 
