  27122 HVACTemplate:Zone:VRF,
  27123       \memo Zone terminal unit with variable refrigerant flow (VRF) DX cooling and heating coils
  27124       \memo (air-to-air or water-to-air heat pump). The VRF terminal units are served by an
  27125       \memo HVACTemplate:System:VRF system.
  27126       \min-fields 44
  27127   A1, \field Zone Name
  27128       \required-field
  27129       \note Zone name must match a building zone name
  27130       \type object-list
  27131       \object-list ZoneNames
  27132   A2, \field Template VRF System Name
  27133       \required-field
  27134       \note Name of a HVACTemplate:System:VRF object serving this zone
  27135       \type object-list
  27136       \object-list CompactHVACSystemVRF
  27137   A3, \field Template Thermostat Name
  27138       \note Enter the name of a HVACTemplate:Thermostat object.
  27139       \note If blank, then it is assumed that standard thermostat objects
  27140       \note have been defined for this zone.
  27141       \type object-list
  27142       \object-list CompactHVACThermostats
  27143   N1, \field Zone Heating Sizing Factor
  27144       \note If blank, value from Sizing:Parameters will be used.
  27145       \minimum 0
  27146   N2, \field Zone Cooling Sizing Factor
  27147       \note If blank, value from Sizing:Parameters will be used.
  27148       \minimum 0
  27149   N3, \field Rated Total Heating Capacity Sizing Ratio
  27150       \type real
  27151       \units W/W
  27152       \minimum 1.0
  27153       \default 1.0
  27154       \note If this terminal unit's heating coil is autosized, the heating capacity is sized
  27155       \note to be equal to the cooling capacity multiplied by this sizing ratio.
  27156       \note This input applies to the terminal unit heating coil and overrides the sizing
  27157       \note ratio entered in the HVACTemplate:System:VRF object.
  27158   N4, \field Cooling Supply Air Flow Rate
  27159       \note This field may be set to "autosize".  If a value is entered, it will be
  27160       \note multiplied by the Supply Air Sizing Factor and by zone multipliers.
  27161       \type real
  27162       \units m3/s
  27163       \minimum> 0.0
  27164       \autosizable
  27165       \default autosize
  27166   N5, \field No Cooling Supply Air Flow Rate
  27167       \note This flow rate is used when the terminal is not cooling and the previous mode was cooling.
  27168       \note This field may be set to "autosize".  If a value is entered, it will be
  27169       \note multiplied by the Supply Air Sizing Factor and by zone multipliers.
  27170       \type real
  27171       \units m3/s
  27172       \minimum 0.0
  27173       \autosizable
  27174       \default autosize
  27175   N6, \field Heating Supply Air Flow Rate
  27176       \note This field may be set to "autosize".  If a value is entered, it will be
  27177       \note multiplied by the Supply Air Sizing Factor and by zone multipliers.
  27178       \type real
  27179       \units m3/s
  27180       \minimum> 0.0
  27181       \autosizable
  27182       \default autosize
  27183   N7, \field No Heating Supply Air Flow Rate
  27184       \note This flow rate is used when the terminal is not heating and the previous mode was heating.
  27185       \note This field may be set to "autosize".  If a value is entered, it will be
  27186       \note multiplied by the Supply Air Sizing Factor and by zone multipliers.
  27187       \type real
  27188       \units m3/s
  27189       \minimum 0.0
  27190       \autosizable
  27191       \default autosize
  27192   N8, \field Cooling Outdoor Air Flow Rate
  27193       \note If this field is set to autosize it will be sized based on the outdoor air inputs below,
  27194       \note unless a dedicated outdoor air system is specified for this zone and then it will be
  27195       \note set to zero.
  27196       \type real
  27197       \units m3/s
  27198       \minimum 0.0
  27199       \autosizable
  27200       \default autosize
  27201   N9, \field Heating Outdoor Air Flow Rate
  27202       \note If this field is set to autosize it will be sized based on the outdoor air inputs below,
  27203       \note unless a dedicated outdoor air system is specified for this zone and then it will be
  27204       \note set to zero.
  27205       \type real
  27206       \units m3/s
  27207       \minimum 0.0
  27208       \autosizable
  27209       \default autosize
  27210  N10, \field No Load Outdoor Air Flow Rate
  27211       \note If this field is set to autosize it will be sized based on the outdoor air inputs below,
  27212       \note unless a dedicated outdoor air system is specified for this zone and then it will be
  27213       \note set to zero.
  27214       \type real
  27215       \units m3/s
  27216       \minimum 0.0
  27217       \autosizable
  27218       \default autosize
  27219   A4, \field Outdoor Air Method
  27220       \note Flow/Person, Flow/Zone, Flow/Area, Sum, and Maximum use the values in the next three
  27221       \note fields: Outdoor Air Flow Rate per Person, Outdoor Air Flow Rate per Zone Floor Area,
  27222       \note and Outdoor Air Flow Rate per Zone.
  27223       \note DetailedSpecification ignores these three Outdoor Air Flow Rate fields and instead
  27224       \note references design specification objects named in the fields
  27225       \note Design Specification Outdoor Air Object Name and Design Specification Zone Air
  27226       \note Distribution Object Name.
  27227       \type choice
  27228       \key Flow/Person
  27229       \key Flow/Zone
  27230       \key Flow/Area
  27231       \key Sum
  27232       \key Maximum
  27233       \key DetailedSpecification
  27234       \default Flow/Person
  27235  N11, \field Outdoor Air Flow Rate per Person
  27236       \units m3/s
  27237       \note Default 0.00944 is 20 cfm per person
  27238       \note This input is used if the field Outdoor Air Method is
  27239       \note Flow/Person, Sum, or Maximum
  27240       \default 0.00944
  27241  N12, \field Outdoor Air Flow Rate per Zone Floor Area
  27242       \units m3/s-m2
  27243       \default 0.0
  27244       \note This input is used if the field Outdoor Air Method is
