  33183 Sizing:Plant,
  33184       \memo Specifies the input needed to autosize plant loop flow rates and equipment capacities.
  33185       \memo This information is initially used by components that use water for heating or cooling
  33186       \memo such as hot or chilled water coils to calculate their maximum water flow rates. These
  33187       \memo flow rates are then summed for use in calculating the Plant Loop flow rates.
  33188   \min-fields 4
  33189   A1, \field Plant or Condenser Loop Name
  33190       \note Enter the name of a PlantLoop or a CondenserLoop object
  33191       \required-field
  33192       \type object-list
  33193       \object-list PlantLoops
  33194   A2, \field Loop Type
  33195       \required-field
  33196       \type choice
  33197       \key Heating
  33198       \key Cooling
  33199       \key Condenser
  33200       \key Steam
  33201   N1, \field Design Loop Exit Temperature
  33202       \required-field
  33203       \type real
  33204       \units C
  33205   N2, \field Loop Design Temperature Difference
  33206       \required-field
  33207       \type real
  33208       \units deltaC
  33209       \minimum> 0.0
  33210   A3, \field Sizing Option
  33211       \note if Coincident is chosen, then sizing is based on HVAC Sizing Simulations and
  33212       \note the input field called Do HVAC Sizing Simulation for Sizing Periods in SimulationControl must be set to Yes
  33213       \type choice
  33214       \key Coincident
  33215       \key NonCoincident
  33216       \default NonCoincident
  33217   N3, \field Zone Timesteps in Averaging Window
  33218       \note this is used in the coincident sizing algorithm to apply a running average to peak flow rates
  33219       \note that occur during HVAC Sizing Simulations
  33220       \type integer
  33221       \minimum 1
  33222       \default 1
  33223   A4; \field Coincident Sizing Factor Mode
  33224       \note this is used to adjust the result for coincident sizing by applying a sizing factor
  33225       \type choice
  33226       \key None
  33227       \key GlobalHeatingSizingFactor
  33228       \key GlobalCoolingSizingFactor
  33229       \key LoopComponentSizingFactor
  33230 
  33231 OutputControl:Sizing:Style,
  33232        \memo Default style for the Sizing output files is comma -- this works well for
  33233        \memo importing into spreadsheet programs such as Excel(tm) but not so well for word
  33234        \memo processing programs -- there tab may be a better choice.  Fixed puts spaces between
  33235        \memo the "columns"
  33236        \unique-object
  33237    A1; \field Column Separator
  33238        \required-field
  33239        \type choice
  33240        \key Comma
  33241        \key Tab
  33242        \key Fixed
  33243 
  33244 \group Zone HVAC Controls and Thermostats
  33245 
  33246 ZoneControl:Humidistat,
