  33465 ZoneControl:Thermostat:TemperatureAndHumidity,
  33466        \min-fields 2
  33467        \memo This object modifies a ZoneControl:Thermostat object to effect temperature control based on
  33468        \memo zone air humidity conditions.
  33469   A1,  \field Thermostat Name
  33470        \required-field
  33471        \type object-list
  33472        \object-list ZoneControlThermostaticNames
  33473        \note Enter the name of a ZoneControl:Thermostat object whose operation is to be modified to
  33474        \note effect temperature control based on zone air humidity conditions. If the ZoneControl:
  33475        \note Thermostat object references a ZoneList, simply enter the name of the ZoneControl:Thermostat
  33476        \note object and this temperature and humidity thermostat control will be applied to all zones
  33477        \note in the ZoneList. If the ZoneControl:Thermostat object references a ZoneList but it is
  33478        \note desired that only a single zone within the ZoneList be controlled based on temperature and
  33479        \note humidity control, then the name to be put here is <Zone Name> <Thermostat Name> where the
  33480        \note Thermostat Name is the the name of the ZoneControl:Thermostat object.
  33481   A2 , \field Dehumidifying Relative Humidity Setpoint Schedule Name
  33482        \required-field
  33483        \type object-list
  33484        \object-list ScheduleNames
  33485        \note Schedule values should be in Relative Humidity (percent)
  33486   A3,  \field Dehumidification Control Type
  33487        \type choice
  33488        \key Overcool
  33489        \key None
  33490        \default Overcool
  33491   A4,  \field Overcool Range Input Method
  33492        \type choice
  33493        \key Constant
  33494        \key Scheduled
  33495        \default Constant
  33496   N1,  \field Overcool Constant Range
  33497        \type real
  33498        \units deltaC
  33499        \minimum 0.0
  33500        \maximum 3.0
  33501        \default 1.7
  33502        \note Maximum Overcool temperature range for cooling setpoint reduction.
  33503        \note Used with Dehumidification Control Type = Overcool.
  33504        \note A value of 0.0 indicates no zone temperature overcooling will be provided to
  33505        \note gain additional dehumidification.
  33506   A5,  \field Overcool Range Schedule Name
  33507        \note Schedule values of 0.0 indicates no zone temperature overcooling will be
  33508        \note provided to gain additional dehumidification.
  33509        \note Schedule values should be >= 0 and <= 3 (deltaC).
  33510        \type object-list
  33511        \object-list ScheduleNames
  33512   N2;  \field Overcool Control Ratio
  33513        \type real
  33514        \units percent/K
  33515        \minimum 0.0
  33516        \default 3.6
  33517        \note The value of this input field is used to adjust the cooling setpoint temperature
  33518        \note (established by the associated ZoneControl:Thermostat object) downward based on the
  33519        \note difference between the zone air relative humidity level and the dehumidifying
  33520        \note relative humidity setpoint.
