  33632 ZoneControl:Thermostat:StagedDualSetpoint,
  33633    \memo Define the Thermostat StagedDualSetpoint settings for a zone or list of zones.
  33634    \memo If you use a ZoneList in the Zone or ZoneList name field then this definition applies
  33635    \memo to all the zones in the ZoneList.
  33636   A1 , \field Name
  33637        \required-field
  33638        \reference ZoneControlThermostaticNames
  33639   A2 , \field Zone or ZoneList Name
  33640        \required-field
  33641        \type object-list
  33642        \object-list ZoneAndZoneListNames
  33643   N1 , \field Number of Heating Stages
  33644        \required-field
  33645        \type integer
  33646        \minimum 1
  33647        \maximum 4
  33648        \note Enter the number of the following sets of data for heating temperature offset
  33649   A3 , \field Heating Temperature Setpoint Schedule Name
  33650        \type object-list
  33651        \object-list ScheduleNames
  33652   N2 , \field Heating Throttling Temperature Range
  33653        \units deltaC
  33654        \minimum 0.0
  33655        \default 1.1
  33656   N3 , \field Stage 1 Heating Temperature Offset
  33657        \required-field
  33658        \type real
  33659        \units deltaC
  33660        \maximum 0.0
  33661        \note The heating temperature offset is used to determine heating stage number for
  33662        \note multi stage equipment.
  33663        \note When the temperature difference of the heating setpoint and the controlled zone
  33664        \note temperature at previous time step is less than Stage 1 value and greater than
  33665        \note Stage 2 value, the stage number is 1.
  33666   N4 , \field Stage 2 Heating Temperature Offset
  33667        \type real
  33668        \units deltaC
  33669        \maximum 0.0
  33670        \note The heating temperature offset is used to determine heating stage number for
  33671        \note multi stage equipment.
  33672        \note When the temperature difference of the heating setpoint and the controlled zone
  33673        \note temperature at previous time step is less than Stage 2 value and greater than
  33674        \note Stage 3 value, the stage number is 2.
  33675        \note The value of this field has to be less the value at the previous field.
  33676   N5 , \field Stage 3 Heating Temperature Offset
  33677        \type real
  33678        \units deltaC
  33679        \maximum 0.0
  33680        \note The heating temperature offset is used to determine heating stage number for
  33681        \note multi stage equipment.
  33682        \note When the temperature difference of the heating setpoint and the controlled zone
  33683        \note temperature at previous time step is less than Stage 3 value and greater than
  33684        \note Stage 4 value, the stage number is 3.
  33685        \note The value of this field has to be less the value at the previous field.
  33686   N6 , \field Stage 4 Heating Temperature Offset
  33687        \type real
  33688        \units deltaC
  33689        \maximum 0.0
  33690        \note The heating temperature offset is used to determine heating stage number for
  33691        \note multi stage equipment.
  33692        \note When the temperature difference of the heating setpoint and the controlled zone
  33693        \note temperature at previous time step is less than Stage 4 value, the stage number is 4.
  33694        \note The value of this field has to be less the value at the previous field.
  33695   N7 , \field Number of Cooling Stages
  33696        \required-field
  33697        \type integer
  33698        \minimum 1
  33699        \maximum 4
  33700        \note Enter the number of the following sets of data for cooling temperature offset
  33701   A4 , \field Cooling Temperature Setpoint Base Schedule Name
  33702        \type object-list
  33703        \object-list ScheduleNames
  33704   N8 , \field Cooling Throttling Temperature Range
  33705        \units deltaC
  33706        \minimum 0.0
  33707        \default 1.1
  33708   N9 , \field Stage 1 Cooling Temperature Offset
  33709        \required-field
  33710        \type real
  33711        \units deltaC
  33712        \minimum 0.0
  33713        \note The cooling temperature offset is used to determine cooling stage number for
  33714        \note multi stage equipment.
  33715        \note When the temperature difference of the cooling setpoint and the controlled zone
  33716        \note temperature at previous time step is greater than Stage 1 value and less than
  33717        \note Stage 2 value, the stage number is 1.
  33718   N10, \field Stage 2 Cooling Temperature Offset
  33719        \type real
  33720        \units deltaC
  33721        \minimum 0.0
  33722        \note The cooling temperature offset is used to determine cooling stage number for
  33723        \note multi stage equipment.
  33724        \note When the temperature difference of the cooling setpoint and the controlled zone
  33725        \note temperature at previous time step is greater than Stage 2 value and less than
  33726        \note Stage 3 value, the stage number is 2.
  33727        \note The value of this field has to be greater than the value at the previous field.
  33728   N11, \field Stage 3 Cooling Temperature Offset
  33729        \type real
  33730        \units deltaC
  33731        \minimum 0.0
  33732        \note The cooling temperature offset is used to determine cooling stage number for
  33733        \note multi stage equipment.
  33734        \note When the temperature difference of the cooling setpoint and the controlled zone
  33735        \note temperature at previous time step is greater than Stage 3 value and less than
  33736        \note Stage 4 value, the stage number is 3.
  33737        \note The value of this field has to be greater than the value at the previous field.
  33738   N12; \field Stage 4 Cooling Temperature Offset
  33739        \type real
  33740        \units deltaC
  33741        \minimum 0.0
  33742        \note The cooling temperature offset is used to determine cooling stage number for
  33743        \note multi stage equipment.
  33744        \note When the temperature difference of the cooling setpoint and the controlled zone
  33745        \note temperature at previous time step is greater than Stage 4 value, the stage number is 4.
  33746        \note The value of this field has to be greater than the value at the previous field.
