  33797 \group Zone HVAC Forced Air Units
  33798 
  33799 ZoneHVAC:IdealLoadsAirSystem,
  33800        \memo Ideal system used to calculate loads without modeling a full HVAC system. All that is
  33801        \memo required for the ideal system are zone controls, zone equipment configurations, and
  33802        \memo the ideal loads system component. This component can be thought of as an ideal unit
  33803        \memo that mixes zone air with the specified amount of outdoor air and then adds or removes
  33804        \memo heat and moisture at 100% efficiency in order to meet the specified controls. Energy
  33805        \memo use is reported as DistrictHeating and DistrictCooling.
  33806        \min-fields 27
  33807   A1 , \field Name
  33808        \required-field
  33809        \reference ZoneEquipmentNames
  33810   A2 , \field Availability Schedule Name
  33811        \note Availability schedule name for this system. Schedule value > 0 means the system is available.
  33812        \note If this field is blank, the system is always available.
  33813        \type object-list
  33814        \object-list ScheduleNames
  33815   A3 , \field Zone Supply Air Node Name
  33816        \note Must match a zone air inlet node name.
  33817        \required-field
  33818        \type node
  33819   A4 , \field Zone Exhaust Air Node Name
  33820        \note Should match a zone air exhaust node name.
  33821        \note This field is optional, but is required if this
  33822        \note this object is used with other forced air equipment.
  33823        \type node
  33824   A5 , \field System Inlet Air Node Name
  33825        \note This field is only required when the Ideal Loads Air System is connected to an
  33826        \note AirloopHVAC:ZoneReturnPlenum, otherwise leave this field blank. When connected to a plenum
  33827        \note the return plenum Outlet Node Name (or Induced Air Outlet Node Name when connecting multiple
  33828        \note ideal loads air sytems) is entered here. The two ideal loads air system node name fields described above,
  33829        \note the Zone Supply Air Node Name and the Zone Exhaust Air Node Name must also be entered.
  33830        \note The Zone Supply Air Node Name must match a zone inlet air node name for the zone where this
  33831        \note Ideal Loads Air System is connected. The Zone Exhaust Air Node Name must match an inlet air
  33832        \note node name of an AirloopHVAC:ReturnAirPlenum object.
  33833        \type node
  33834   N1 , \field Maximum Heating Supply Air Temperature
  33835        \units C
  33836        \minimum> 0
  33837        \maximum< 100
  33838        \default 50
  33839   N2 , \field Minimum Cooling Supply Air Temperature
  33840        \units C
  33841        \minimum> -100
  33842        \maximum< 50
  33843        \default 13
  33844   N3 , \field Maximum Heating Supply Air Humidity Ratio
  33845        \units kgWater/kgDryAir
  33846        \minimum> 0
  33847        \default 0.0156
  33848   N4 , \field Minimum Cooling Supply Air Humidity Ratio
  33849        \units kgWater/kgDryAir
  33850        \minimum> 0
  33851        \default 0.0077
  33852   A6 , \field Heating Limit
  33853        \type choice
  33854        \key NoLimit
  33855        \key LimitFlowRate
  33856        \key LimitCapacity
  33857        \key LimitFlowRateAndCapacity
  33858        \default NoLimit
  33859   N5 , \field Maximum Heating Air Flow Rate
  33860        \note This field is ignored if Heating Limit = NoLimit
  33861        \note If this field is blank, there is no limit.
  33862        \units m3/s
  33863        \minimum 0.0
  33864        \autosizable
  33865   N6 , \field Maximum Sensible Heating Capacity
  33866        \note This field is ignored if Heating Limit = NoLimit
  33867        \note If this field is blank, there is no limit.
  33868        \units W
  33869        \minimum 0.0
  33870        \autosizable
  33871   A7 , \field Cooling Limit
  33872        \type choice
  33873        \key NoLimit
  33874        \key LimitFlowRate
  33875        \key LimitCapacity
  33876        \key LimitFlowRateAndCapacity
  33877        \default NoLimit
  33878   N7 , \field Maximum Cooling Air Flow Rate
  33879        \note This field is ignored if Cooling Limit = NoLimit
  33880        \note This field is required if Outdoor Air Economizer Type is anything other than NoEconomizer.
  33881        \units m3/s
  33882        \minimum 0.0
  33883        \autosizable
  33884   N8 , \field Maximum Total Cooling Capacity
  33885        \note This field is ignored if Cooling Limit = NoLimit
  33886        \units W
  33887        \minimum 0.0
  33888        \autosizable
  33889   A8 , \field Heating Availability Schedule Name
  33890        \note If blank, heating is always available.
  33891        \type object-list
  33892        \object-list ScheduleNames
  33893   A9 , \field Cooling Availability Schedule Name
  33894        \note If blank, cooling is always available.
  33895        \type object-list
  33896        \object-list ScheduleNames
  33897   A10, \field Dehumidification Control Type
  33898        \note ConstantSensibleHeatRatio means that the ideal loads system
  33899        \note will be controlled to meet the sensible cooling load, and the
  33900        \note latent cooling rate will be computed using a constant
  33901        \note sensible heat ratio (SHR)
  33902        \note Humidistat means that there is a ZoneControl:Humidistat for this
  33903        \note zone and the ideal loads system will attempt to satisfy the humidistat.
  33904        \note None means that there is no dehumidification.
  33905        \note ConstantSupplyHumidityRatio means that during cooling the supply air
  33906        \note will always be at the Minimum Cooling Supply Humidity Ratio.
  33907        \type choice
  33908        \key ConstantSensibleHeatRatio
  33909        \key Humidistat
  33910        \key None
  33911        \key ConstantSupplyHumidityRatio
  33912        \default ConstantSensibleHeatRatio
  33913   N9 , \field Cooling Sensible Heat Ratio
  33914        \note This field is applicable only when Dehumidification Control Type is ConstantSensibleHeatRatio
  33915        \units dimensionless
  33916        \minimum> 0.0
  33917        \maximum 1.0
  33918        \default 0.7
  33919   A11, \field Humidification Control Type
  33920        \note None means that there is no humidification.
  33921        \note Humidistat means that there is a ZoneControl:Humidistat for this
  33922        \note zone and the ideal loads system will attempt to satisfy the humidistat.
  33923        \note ConstantSupplyHumidityRatio means that during heating the supply air
  33924        \note will always be at the Maximum Heating Supply Humidity Ratio.
  33925        \type choice
  33926        \key None
  33927        \key Humidistat
  33928        \key ConstantSupplyHumidityRatio
  33929        \default None
  33930   A12, \field Design Specification Outdoor Air Object Name
  33931        \type object-list
  33932        \object-list DesignSpecificationOutdoorAirNames
  33933        \note When the name of a DesignSpecification:OutdoorAir object is entered, the minimum
  33934        \note outdoor air flow rate will be computed using these specifications. The outdoor air
  33935        \note flow rate will also be affected by the next two fields.
  33936        \note If this field is blank, there will be no outdoor air and the remaining fields will
  33937        \note be ignored.
  33938   A13, \field Outdoor Air Inlet Node Name
  33939        \type node
  33940        \note This field is required if the system provides outdoor air
  33941        \note Enter the name of an outdoor air node. This node name is also specified in
  33942        \note an OutdoorAir:Node or OutdoorAir:NodeList object.
  33943   A14, \field Demand Controlled Ventilation Type
  33944        \note This field controls how the minimum outdoor air flow rate is calculated.
  33945        \note None means that design occupancy will be used to compute the minimum outdoor air flow rate
  33946        \note OccupancySchedule means that current occupancy level will be used.
  33947        \note CO2Setpoint means that the design occupancy will be used to compute the minimum outdoor air flow
  33948        \note rate and the outdoor air flow rate may be increased if necessary to maintain the indoor air carbon
  33949        \note dioxide setpoint defined in a ZoneControl:ContaminantController object.
  33950        \type choice
  33951        \key None
  33952        \key OccupancySchedule
  33953        \key CO2Setpoint
  33954        \default None
  33955   A15, \field Outdoor Air Economizer Type
  33956        \note DifferentialDryBulb and DifferentialEnthalpy will increase the outdoor air flow rate
  33957        \note when there is a cooling load and the outdoor air temperature or enthalpy
  33958        \note is below the zone exhaust air temperature or enthalpy.
  33959        \type choice
  33960        \key NoEconomizer
  33961        \key DifferentialDryBulb
  33962        \key DifferentialEnthalpy
  33963        \default NoEconomizer
  33964   A16, \field Heat Recovery Type
  33965        \type choice
  33966        \key None
  33967        \key Sensible
  33968        \key Enthalpy
  33969        \default None
  33970   N10, \field Sensible Heat Recovery Effectiveness
  33971        \units dimensionless
  33972        \minimum 0.0
  33973        \maximum 1.0
  33974        \default 0.70
  33975   N11, \field Latent Heat Recovery Effectiveness
  33976        \note Applicable only if Heat Recovery Type is Enthalpy.
  33977        \units dimensionless
  33978        \minimum 0.0
  33979        \maximum 1.0
  33980        \default 0.65
  33981   A17; \field Design Specification ZoneHVAC Sizing Object Name
  33982        \note Enter the name of a DesignSpecificationZoneHVACSizing object.
  33983        \type object-list
  33984        \object-list DesignSpecificationZoneHVACSizingName
  33985 
