  35405 ZoneHVAC:HybridUnitaryHVAC,
  35406         \memo Hybrid Unitary HVAC. A black box model for multi-mode packaged forced air equipment. Independent variables include outdoor air conditions and indoor air conditions. Controlled inputs include operating mode, supply air flow rate, and outdoor air faction. Emperical lookup tables are required to map supply air temperature supply air humidity, electricity use, fuel uses, water use, fan electricity use, and external static pressure as a function of each indpednent varaible and each cont
  35407         \extensible:25 repeat last twentyfive fields remembering to move the semi-colon to the last value
  35408     A1, \field Name
  35409         \required-field
  35410         \type alpha
  35411         \retaincase
  35412         \reference ZoneEquipmentNames
  35413     A2, \field Availability Schedule Name
  35414         \note Enter the availability schedule name for this system. Schedule value > 0 means the system is available. If this field is blank, the system is always available.
  35415         \type object-list
  35416         \object-list ScheduleNames
  35417     A3, \field Availability Manager List Name
  35418         \note Enter the name of an AvailabilityManagerAssignmentList object.
  35419         \type object-list
  35420         \object-list SystemAvailabilityManagerLists
  35421     A4, \field Minimum Supply Air Temperature Schedule Name
  35422         \note Values in this schedule are used as a constraint in choosing the feasible settings for supply air flow rate and ouside air fraction in each operating mode. If this field is blank, no minimum is imposed.
  35423         \type object-list
  35424         \object-list ScheduleNames
  35425     A5, \field Maximum Supply Air Temperature Schedule Name
  35426         \note Values in this schedule are used as a constraint in choosing the feasible settings for supply air flow rate and outdoor air fraction in each operating mode. If this field is blank, no maximum is imposed.
  35427         \type object-list
  35428         \object-list ScheduleNames
  35429     A6, \field Minimum Supply Air Humidity Ratio Schedule Name
  35430         \note Values in this schedule are used as a constraint in choosing the feasible settings for supply air flow rate and outdoor air fraction in each operating mode. If this field is blank, no minimum is imposed.
  35431         \type object-list
  35432         \object-list ScheduleNames
  35433     A7, \field Maximum Supply Air Humidity Ratio Schedule Name
  35434         \note Values in this schedule are used as a constraint in choosing the feasible settings for supply air flow rate and outdoor air fraction in each operating mode. If this field is blank, no maximum is imposed.
  35435         \type object-list
  35436         \object-list ScheduleNames
  35437     A8, \field Method to Choose Controlled Inputs and Part Runtime Fraction
  35438         \note Select the method that will be used to choose operating mode(s), supply air flow rate(s), outdoor air fraction(s) and part runtime fraction(s) in each time step. "Automatic" = chooses controlled inputs and part runtime fraction(s) to minimize resource use within each time step while best satisfying requested sensible cooling, dehumidification and ventilation, and subject to constraints. "User Defined" = EMS will be used to choose controlled inputs and part runtime fraction(s) in ea
  35439         \type choice
  35440         \key Automatic
  35441         \key User Defined
  35442         \default Automatic
  35443     A9, \field Return Air Node Name
  35444         \required-field
  35445         \type node
  35446         \note Return air node for the hybrid unit must be a zone exhaust node.
  35447    A10, \field Outdoor Air Node Name
  35448         \required-field
  35449         \type node
  35450         \note Outdoor air node for the hybrid unit must be an outdoor air node.
  35451    A11, \field Supply Air Node Name
  35452         \required-field
  35453         \type node
  35454         \note Supply air node for the hybrid unit must be a zone air inlet node.
  35455    A12, \field Relief Node Name
  35456         \type node
  35457         \note Relief node for the hybrid unit must be a zone exhaust node, unless flow is being balanced elsewhere.
  35458     N1, \field System Maximum Supply Air Flow Rate
  35459         \type real
  35460         \minimum> 0
  35461         \note The value in this field represents the maximum supply air volume flow rate among all operating modes. Values of extensive variables in lookup tables are normalized by the system maximum supply air mass flow rate that was used to build performance curves. The value in this field is used to rescale the output from exenstive variables to a desired system size.
  35462         \units m3/s
  35463     N2, \field External Static Pressure at System Maximum Supply Air Flow Rate
  35464         \type real
  35465         \minimum> 0
  35466         \note Input the external static pressure when the system operates at maximum supply air flow rate. Fan affinity laws are used to scale supply fan power from the values tabulated in lookup tables, to values that match the external static pressure input to this field. If this field is blank, the supply fan power is not scaled from the values tabulated in lookup tables.
  35467         \units Pa
  35468    A13, \field Fan Heat Included in Lookup Tables
  35469         \type choice
  35470         \key No
  35471         \key Yes
  35472         \default No
  35473         \note This field specifies if the fan heat is accounted for in the lookup tables.
  35474    A14, \field Fan Heat Gain Location
  35475         \type choice
  35476         \key MixedAirStream
  35477         \key SupplyAirStream
  35478         \default SupplyAirStream
  35479         \note This field specifies where to add the fan heat in the air stream.
  35480     N3, \field Fan Heat In Air Stream Fraction
  35481         \note 0.0 means no fan heat is added to the air stream, 1.0 means all fan heat is added to the air stream.
  35482         \type real
  35483         \default 1.0
  35484         \minimum 0.0
  35485         \maximum 1.0
  35486     N4, \field Scaling Factor
  35487         \type real
  35488         \minimum> 0
  35489         \note The value in this field scales all extensive performance variables including: supply air mass flow rate, fuel uses, and water use. If this field is blank, the default scaling factor is 1.
  35490         \default 1
  35491     N5, \field Minimum Time Between Mode Change
  35492         \type real
  35493         \minimum 1
  35494         \note Any mode selected will not operate for less time than the value input in this field. If the value in this field is larger than each timestep, the mode selected in one time step will persist in later time steps until the minimum time between mode change is satisfied. Supply air mass flow rate and outdoor air fraction within a mode are not subject to minimum runtime and may change in every time step. Mode 0 does not have a minimum time. If this field is blank, the default minimum tim
  35495         \units minutes
  35496         \default 10
  35497    A15, \field First Fuel Type
  35498         \type choice
  35499         \key None
  35500         \key Electricity
  35501         \key NaturalGas
  35502         \key Propane
  35503         \key FuelOilNo1
  35504         \key FuelOilNo2
  35505         \key Diesel
  35506         \key Gasoline
  35507         \key Coal
  35508         \key OtherFuel1
  35509         \key OtherFuel2
  35510         \key Steam
  35511         \key DistrictHeating
  35512         \key DistrictCooling
  35513         \note Select the fuel type associated with field: "System Electric Power Lookup Table" in each mode.
  35514         \note If this field is blank, default first fuel type = Electricity.
  35515         \default Electricity
  35516    A16, \field Second Fuel Type
  35517         \type choice
  35518         \key None
  35519         \key Electricity
  35520         \key NaturalGas
  35521         \key Propane
  35522         \key FuelOilNo1
  35523         \key FuelOilNo2
  35524         \key Diesel
  35525         \key Gasoline
  35526         \key Coal
  35527         \key OtherFuel1
  35528         \key OtherFuel2
  35529         \key Steam
  35530         \key DistrictHeating
  35531         \key DistrictCooling
  35532         \note Select the fuel type associated with field: "System Second Fuel Consumption Lookup Table" in each mode.
  35533         \note If this field is blank, default second fuel type = None.
  35534         \default None
  35535    A17, \field Third Fuel Type
  35536         \type choice
  35537         \key None
  35538         \key Electricity
  35539         \key NaturalGas
  35540         \key Propane
  35541         \key FuelOilNo1
  35542         \key FuelOilNo2
  35543         \key Diesel
  35544         \key Gasoline
  35545         \key Coal
  35546         \key OtherFuel1
  35547         \key OtherFuel2
  35548         \key Steam
  35549         \key DistrictHeating
  35550         \key DistrictCooling
  35551         \note Select the fuel type associated with field: "System Third Fuel Consumption Lookup Table" in each mode.
  35552         \note If this field is blank, default third fuel type = None.
  35553         \default None
  35554    A18, \field Objective Function to Minimize
  35555         \type choice
  35556         \key Electricity Use
  35557         \key Second Fuel Use
  35558         \key Third Fuel Use
  35559         \key Water Use
  35560         \note In each time step, controlled variables will be chosen to minimize the selection in this field, subject to constraints.
  35561         \note If this field is blank, the objective function will minimize electricity use.
  35562         \default Electricity Use
  35563    A19, \field Design Specification Outdoor Air Object Name
  35564         \type object-list
  35565         \object-list DesignSpecificationOutdoorAirNames
  35566         \note Enter the name of a DesignSpecification:OutdoorAir object. Information in that object will be used to compute the minimum outdoor air flow rate in each time step.
  35567         \note If this field is blank, the system may still supply outdoor air, if it is capable as described by lookup tables, when doing so is the most efficient way to satisfy other constraints.
  35568    A20, \field Mode 0 Name
  35569         \type alpha
  35570         \retaincase
  35571         \note Enter a name for Mode 0.
  35572         \note Mode 0 describes equipment performance in standby.  Mode 0 is usually characterized by electricity use for controls and crankcase heaters, or other standby resouce consumption. Mode 0 will be chosen for any timestep, or portion of timestep, when no ventilation, cooling, humidification, or dehumidification is required.  Mode 0 is available at any environmental condition.
  35573    A21, \field Mode 0 Supply Air Temperature Lookup Table Name
  35574         \type object-list
  35575         \object-list MultivariateFunctions
  35576         \note Enter the name of the Supply Air Temperature Lookup Table for Mode 0.
  35577         \note Units for lookup table values should be in C.
  35578         \note If this field is blank, Mode 0 will not be considered for any period that requires ventilation, heating, cooling, humidification, or dehumidification. If this field is blank, when Mode 0 is chosen (during standby periods) the supply air temperature will equal the return air temperature.
  35579    A22, \field Mode 0 Supply Air Humidity Ratio Lookup Table Name
  35580         \type object-list
  35581         \object-list MultivariateFunctions
  35582         \note Enter the name of the Supply Air Humidity Ratio Lookup Table for Mode 0.
  35583         \note Units for lookup table values should be in kgWater/kgDryAir.
  35584         \note If this field is blank, Mode 0 will not be considered for any period that requires ventilation, heating, cooling, humidification, or dehumidification. If this field is blank, when Mode 0 is chosen (during standby periods) the supply air humidty ratio will equal the return air humidity ratio.
  35585    A23, \field Mode 0 System Electric Power Lookup Table Name
  35586         \type object-list
  35587         \object-list MultivariateFunctions
  35588         \note Enter the name of the Electric Power Lookup Table for Mode 0.
  35589         \note Units for lookup table values should be in W.
  35590         \note If this field is blank, Mode 0 does not consume electricity.
  35591    A24, \field Mode 0 Supply Fan Electric Power Lookup Table Name
  35592         \type object-list
  35593         \object-list MultivariateFunctions
  35594         \note Enter the name of the Supply Fan Electric Power Lookup Table for Mode 0.
  35595         \note Units for lookup table values should be in W.
  35596         \note If this field is blank, Mode 0 does not consume electricity for supply fan.
  35597    A25, \field Mode 0 External Static Pressure Lookup Table Name
  35598         \type object-list
  35599         \object-list MultivariateFunctions
  35600         \note Enter the name of the External Static Pressure Lookup Table for Mode 0.
  35601         \note Units for lookup table values should be in Pa.
  35602         \note If this field is blank, external static pressure will not be reported.
  35603    A26, \field Mode 0 System Second Fuel Consumption Lookup Table Name
  35604         \type object-list
  35605         \object-list MultivariateFunctions
  35606         \note Enter the name of the System Second Fuel Consumption Lookup Table for Mode 0.
  35607         \note Units for lookup table values should be in W.
  35608         \note If this field is blank, Mode 0 does not consume a second fuel.
  35609    A27, \field Mode 0 System Third Fuel Consumption Lookup Table Name
  35610         \type object-list
  35611         \object-list MultivariateFunctions
  35612         \note Enter the name of the System Third Fuel Consumption Lookup Table for Mode 0.
  35613         \note Units for lookup table values should be in W.
  35614         \note If this field is blank, Mode 0 does not consume a third fuel.
  35615    A28, \field Mode 0 System Water Use Lookup Table Name
  35616         \type object-list
  35617         \object-list MultivariateFunctions
  35618         \note Enter the name of the System Water Use Lookup Table for Mode 0.
  35619         \note Units for lookup table values should be in kg/s.
  35620         \note If this field is blank, Mode 0 does not consume water.
  35621     N6, \field Mode 0 Outdoor Air Fraction
  35622         \type real
  35623         \minimum 0.00
  35624         \maximum 1.00
  35625         \note Enter the outdoor air fraction for Mode 0.
  35626         \note If this field is blank, the outdoor air fraction for Mode 0 will be 0.00.
  35627         \default 0.00
  35628     N7, \field Mode 0 Supply Air Mass Flow Rate Ratio
  35629         \type real
  35630         \minimum 0.00
  35631         \maximum 1.00
  35632         \note Enter the supply air mass flow rate ratio for Mode 0. The value in this field will be used to determine the supply air mass flow rate in Mode 0.
  35633         \note Supply air mass flow rate ratio describes supply air mass flow rate as a fraction of mass flow rate associated with the value in field: "System Maximum Supply Air Flow Rate".
  35634         \note If this field is blank, the supply air mass flow rate ratio for Mode 0 will be 0.
  35635         \default 0.00
