  40723 \group Zone HVAC Radiative/Convective Units
  40724 
  40725 ZoneHVAC:Baseboard:RadiantConvective:Water,
  40726        \extensible:2 - repeat last two fields, remembering to remove ; from "inner" fields.
  40727        \memo The number of surfaces can be expanded beyond 100, if necessary, by adding more
  40728        \memo groups to the end of the list
  40729        \min-fields 12
  40730   A1,  \field Name
  40731        \required-field
  40732        \reference-class-name validBranchEquipmentTypes
  40733        \reference validBranchEquipmentNames
  40734        \reference ZoneEquipmentNames
  40735   A2,  \field Availability Schedule Name
  40736        \note Availability schedule name for this system. Schedule value > 0 means the system is available.
  40737        \note If this field is blank, the system is always available.
  40738        \type object-list
  40739        \object-list ScheduleNames
  40740   A3,  \field Inlet Node Name
  40741        \required-field
  40742        \type node
  40743   A4,  \field Outlet Node Name
  40744        \required-field
  40745        \type node
  40746   N1,  \field Rated Average Water Temperature
  40747        \note Rated average water temperature is the average of the inlet and outlet water temperatures
  40748        \note at rated conditions.
  40749        \type real
  40750        \maximum 150.0
  40751        \minimum 20.0
  40752        \units C
  40753        \default 87.78
  40754   N2,  \field Rated Water Mass Flow Rate
  40755        \note Standard is I=B=R Rating document where all baseboards are rated at either 0.063 kg/s (1 gpm)
  40756        \note or 0.252 kg/s (4 gpm).  It is recommended that users find data for the baseboard heater that
  40757        \note corresponds to performance at 0.063 kg/s unless the flow rate is expected to be above 0.252 kg/s.
  40758        \note If the flow rate is expected to be above 0.252 kg/s, this field should be 0.252 kg/s.
  40759        \type real
  40760        \maximum 10.0
  40761        \minimum> 0.0
  40762        \units kg/s
  40763        \default 0.063
  40764   A5,  \field Heating Design Capacity Method
  40765        \type choice
  40766        \key HeatingDesignCapacity
  40767        \key CapacityPerFloorArea
  40768        \key FractionOfAutosizedHeatingCapacity
  40769        \default HeatingDesignCapacity
  40770        \note Enter the method used to determine the heating design capacity.
  40771        \note HeatingDesignCapacity = > selected when the design heating capacity value or autosize
  40772        \note is specified. CapacityPerFloorArea = > selected when the design heating capacity is
  40773        \note determine from user specified heating capacity per floor area and zone floor area.
  40774        \note FractionOfAutosizedHeatingCapacity = > is selected when the design heating capacity is
  40775        \note determined from a user specified fraction and the auto-sized design heating capacity.
  40776   N3 , \field Heating Design Capacity
  40777        \type real
  40778        \units W
  40779        \minimum 0.0
  40780        \autosizable
  40781        \ip-units W
  40782        \default autosize
  40783        \note Enter the design heating capacity. Required field when the heating design capacity method
  40784        \note HeatingDesignCapacity. This input field is rated heating capacity. Users must multiply the
  40785        \note actual finned length published in the literature to determine the rated capacity. Rated
  40786        \note Capacity is for an inlet air dry-bulb temperature of 18.0C, the Rated Water Mass Flow Rate
  40787        \note of 0.063kg/s or 0.252kg/s, and the Rated Average Water Temperature between 32.2C and 115.6C.
  40788   N4 , \field Heating Design Capacity Per Floor Area
  40789        \type real
  40790        \units W/m2
  40791        \minimum 0.0
  40792        \note Enter the heating design capacity per zone floor area.Required field when the heating design
  40793        \note capacity method field is CapacityPerFloorArea.
  40794   N5 , \field Fraction of Autosized Heating Design Capacity
  40795        \type real
  40796        \minimum 0.0
  40797        \default 1.0
  40798        \note Enter the fraction of auto - sized heating design capacity.Required field when capacity the
  40799        \note heating design capacity method field is FractionOfAutosizedHeatingCapacity.
  40800   N6,  \field Maximum Water Flow Rate
  40801        \required-field
  40802        \autosizable
  40803        \type real
  40804        \units m3/s
  40805        \ip-units gal/min
  40806   N7,  \field Convergence Tolerance
  40807        \type real
  40808        \minimum> 0.0
  40809        \default 0.001
  40810   N8,  \field Fraction Radiant
  40811        \required-field
  40812        \type real
  40813        \minimum 0
  40814        \maximum 1
  40815   N9,  \field Fraction of Radiant Energy Incident on People
  40816        \type real
  40817        \minimum 0
  40818        \maximum 1
