  43989 ZoneHVAC:LowTemperatureRadiant:VariableFlow,
  43990         \memo Low temperature hydronic radiant heating and/or cooling system embedded in a building
  43991         \memo surface (wall, ceiling, or floor). Controlled by varying the hot or chilled water
  43992         \memo flow to the unit.
  43993         \min-fields 33
  43994    A1 , \field Name
  43995         \required-field
  43996         \reference-class-name validBranchEquipmentTypes
  43997         \reference validBranchEquipmentNames
  43998         \reference ZoneEquipmentNames
  43999    A2 , \field Availability Schedule Name
  44000         \note Availability schedule name for this system. Schedule value > 0 means the system is available.
  44001         \note If this field is blank, the system is always available.
  44002         \type object-list
  44003         \object-list ScheduleNames
  44004    A3 , \field Zone Name
  44005         \note Name of zone system is serving
  44006         \type object-list
  44007         \object-list ZoneNames
  44008    A4 , \field Surface Name or Radiant Surface Group Name
  44009         \note Identifies surfaces that radiant system is embedded in.
  44010         \note For a system with multiple surfaces, enter the name of
  44011         \note a ZoneHVAC:LowTemperatureRadiant:SurfaceGroup object.
  44012         \type object-list
  44013         \object-list RadiantSurfaceNames
  44014         \object-list RadiantGroupNames
  44015    A5 , \field Fluid to Radiant Surface Heat Transfer Model
  44016         \note This parameter identifies how the heat transfer between
  44017         \note fluid being circulated through the radiant system and
  44018         \note the radiant system (slab) is modeled.  ConvectionOnly
  44019         \note means that only convection between the fluid and the
  44020         \note inside surface of the pipe is modeled using a conventional
  44021         \note equation for flow inside a pipe.  ISOStandard models
  44022         \note convection between the fluid and the inside of
  44023         \note of the pipe and conduction through the pipe material using
  44024         \note equations specific to ISO Standard 11855-2.
  44025         \type choice
  44026         \key ConvectionOnly
  44027         \key ISOStandard
  44028         \default ConvectionOnly
  44029    N1 , \field Hydronic Tubing Inside Diameter
  44030         \units m
  44031         \minimum> 0
  44032         \default 0.013
  44033         \ip-units in
  44034    N2 , \field Hydronic Tubing Outside Diameter
  44035         \units m
  44036         \minimum> 0
  44037         \default 0.016
  44038         \ip-units in
  44039    N3 , \field Hydronic Tubing Length
  44040         \note (total length of pipe embedded in surface)
  44041         \units m
  44042         \minimum> 0
  44043         \autosizable
  44044         \default autosize
  44045    N4 , \field Hydronic Tubing Conductivity
  44046         \note Conductivity of the tubing/piping material
  44047         \units W/m-K
  44048         \minimum> 0
  44049         \default 0.35
  44050    A6 , \field Temperature Control Type
  44051         \note (Temperature on which unit is controlled)
  44052         \type choice
  44053         \key MeanAirTemperature
  44054         \key MeanRadiantTemperature
  44055         \key OperativeTemperature
  44056         \key OutdoorDryBulbTemperature
  44057         \key OutdoorWetBulbTemperature
  44058         \key SurfaceFaceTemperature
  44059         \key SurfaceInteriorTemperature
  44060         \default MeanAirTemperature
  44061    A7,  \field Setpoint Control Type
  44062         \note How setpoint temperature is defined
  44063         \type choice
  44064         \key HalfFlowPower
  44065         \key ZeroFlowPower
  44066         \default HalfFlowPower
  44067    A8 , \field Heating Design Capacity Method
  44068         \type choice
  44069         \key HeatingDesignCapacity
  44070         \key CapacityPerFloorArea
  44071         \key FractionOfAutosizedHeatingCapacity
  44072         \default HeatingDesignCapacity
  44073         \note Enter the method used to determine the heating design capacity.
  44074         \note HeatingDesignCapacity = > selected when the design heating capacity value or autosize
  44075         \note is specified. CapacityPerFloorArea = > selected when the design heating capacity is
  44076         \note determine from user specified heating capacity per floor area and zone floor area.
  44077         \note FractionOfAutosizedHeatingCapacity = > is selected when the design heating capacity is
  44078         \note determined from a user specified fraction and the auto-sized design heating capacity.
  44079    N5 , \field Heating Design Capacity
  44080         \type real
  44081         \units W
  44082         \minimum 0.0
  44083         \autosizable
  44084         \ip-units W
  44085         \default autosize
  44086         \note Enter the design heating capacity.Required field when the heating design capacity method
  44087         \note HeatingDesignCapacity.
  44088    N6 , \field Heating Design Capacity Per Floor Area
  44089         \type real
  44090         \units W/m2
  44091         \minimum 0.0
  44092         \note Enter the heating design capacity per zone floor area.Required field when the heating design
  44093         \note capacity method field is CapacityPerFloorArea.
  44094    N7 , \field Fraction of Autosized Heating Design Capacity
  44095         \type real
  44096         \minimum 0.0
  44097         \default 1.0
  44098         \note Enter the fraction of auto - sized heating design capacity.Required field when capacity the
  44099         \note heating design capacity method field is FractionOfAutosizedHeatingCapacity.
  44100    N8 , \field Maximum Hot Water Flow
  44101         \units m3/s
  44102         \minimum 0
  44103         \autosizable
  44104         \ip-units gal/min
