  44188 ZoneHVAC:LowTemperatureRadiant:ConstantFlow,
  44189         \memo Low temperature hydronic radiant heating and/or cooling system embedded in a building
  44190         \memo surface (wall, ceiling, or floor). Controlled by varying the hot or chilled water
  44191         \memo temperature circulating through the unit.
  44192         \min-fields 33
  44193    A1 , \field Name
  44194         \required-field
  44195         \reference-class-name validBranchEquipmentTypes
  44196         \reference validBranchEquipmentNames
  44197         \reference ZoneEquipmentNames
  44198    A2 , \field Availability Schedule Name
  44199         \note Availability schedule name for this system. Schedule value > 0 means the system is available.
  44200         \note If this field is blank, the system is always available.
  44201         \type object-list
  44202         \object-list ScheduleNames
  44203    A3 , \field Zone Name
  44204         \note Name of zone system is serving
  44205         \type object-list
  44206         \object-list ZoneNames
  44207    A4 , \field Surface Name or Radiant Surface Group Name
  44208         \note Identifies surfaces that radiant system is embedded in.
  44209         \note For a system with multiple surfaces, enter the name of
  44210         \note a ZoneHVAC:LowTemperatureRadiant:SurfaceGroup object.
  44211         \type object-list
  44212         \object-list RadiantSurfaceNames
  44213         \object-list RadiantGroupNames
  44214    A5 , \field Fluid to Radiant Surface Heat Transfer Model
  44215         \note This parameter identifies how the heat transfer between
  44216         \note fluid being circulated through the radiant system and
  44217         \note the radiant system (slab) is modeled.  ConvectionOnly
  44218         \note means that only convection between the fluid and the
  44219         \note inside surface of the pipe is modeled using a conventional
  44220         \note equation for flow inside a pipe.  ISOStandard models
  44221         \note convection between the fluid and the inside of
  44222         \note of the pipe and conduction through the pipe material using
  44223         \note equations specific to ISO Standard 11855-2.
  44224         \type choice
  44225         \key ConvectionOnly
  44226         \key ISOStandard
  44227         \default ConvectionOnly
  44228    N1 , \field Hydronic Tubing Inside Diameter
  44229         \units m
  44230         \minimum> 0
  44231         \default 0.013
  44232         \ip-units in
  44233    N2 , \field Hydronic Tubing Outside Diameter
  44234         \units m
  44235         \minimum> 0
  44236         \default 0.016
  44237         \ip-units in
  44238    N3 , \field Hydronic Tubing Length
  44239         \note (total length of pipe embedded in surface)
  44240         \units m
  44241         \minimum> 0
  44242         \autosizable
  44243         \default autosize
  44244    N4 , \field Hydronic Tubing Conductivity
  44245         \note Conductivity of the tubing/piping material
  44246         \units W/m-K
  44247         \minimum> 0
  44248         \default 0.35
  44249    A6 , \field Temperature Control Type
  44250         \note Temperature used to control system
  44251         \type choice
  44252         \key MeanAirTemperature
  44253         \key MeanRadiantTemperature
  44254         \key OperativeTemperature
  44255         \key OutdoorDryBulbTemperature
  44256         \key OutdoorWetBulbTemperature
  44257         \key SurfaceFaceTemperature
  44258         \key SurfaceInteriorTemperature
  44259         \key RunningMeanOutdoorDryBulbTemperature
  44260         \default MeanAirTemperature
  44261    N5 , \field Running Mean Outdoor Dry-Bulb Temperature Weighting Factor
  44262         \note this is the weighting factor in the equation that calculate the running mean outdoor dry-bulb temperature
  44263         \note as a weighted average of the previous day’s running mean outdoor dry-bulb temperature and the previous day’s
  44264         \note average outdoor dry-bulb temperature this value is only used by EnergyPlus when the user elects to use the
  44265         \note RunningMeanOutdoorDryBulbTemperature control type
  44266         \minimum 0.0
  44267         \maximum 1.0
  44268         \default 0.8
  44269    N6 , \field Rated Flow Rate
  44270         \units m3/s
  44271         \ip-units gal/min
  44272         \autosizable
  44273    A7 , \field Pump Flow Rate Schedule Name
  44274         \note Modifies the Rated Flow Rate of the pump on a time basis
  44275         \note the default is that the pump is ON and runs according to its other
  44276         \note operational requirements specified above.  The schedule is for special
  44277         \note pump operations. Values here are between 0 and 1 and are multipliers
  44278         \note on the previous field (Rated Flow Rate).
  44279         \type object-list
  44280         \object-list ScheduleNames
  44281    N7 , \field Rated Pump Head
  44282         \units Pa
  44283         \default 179352
  44284         \note default head is 60 feet
  44285    N8 , \field Rated Power Consumption
  44286         \units W
  44287    N9 , \field Motor Efficiency
  44288         \type real
  44289         \minimum 0.0
  44290         \maximum 1.0
  44291         \default 0.9
  44292    N10, \field Fraction of Motor Inefficiencies to Fluid Stream
  44293         \minimum 0.0
  44294         \maximum 1.0
  44295         \default 0.0
  44296    A8 , \field Heating Water Inlet Node Name
  44297         \type node
  44298    A9 , \field Heating Water Outlet Node Name
  44299         \type node
  44300    A10, \field Heating High Water Temperature Schedule Name
  44301         \note Water and control temperatures for heating work together to provide
  44302         \note a linear function that determines the water temperature sent to the
  44303         \note radiant system.  The current control temperature (see Temperature Control Type above) is
  44304         \note compared to the high and low control temperatures at the current time.
  44305         \note If the control temperature is above the high temperature, then the
  44306         \note inlet water temperature is set to the low water temperature.  If the
  44307         \note control temperature is below the low temperature, then the inlet
  44308         \note water temperature is set to the high water temperature.  If the control
  44309         \note temperature is between the high and low value, then the inlet water
  44310         \note temperature is linearly interpolated between the low and high water
  44311         \note temperature values.
  44312         \type object-list
  44313         \object-list ScheduleNames
  44314    A11, \field Heating Low Water Temperature Schedule Name
  44315         \type object-list
  44316         \object-list ScheduleNames
  44317    A12, \field Heating High Control Temperature Schedule Name
  44318         \type object-list
  44319         \object-list ScheduleNames
  44320    A13, \field Heating Low Control Temperature Schedule Name
  44321         \type object-list
  44322         \object-list ScheduleNames
  44323    A14, \field Cooling Water Inlet Node Name
  44324         \type node
  44325    A15, \field Cooling Water Outlet Node Name
  44326         \type node
  44327    A16, \field Cooling High Water Temperature Schedule Name
  44328         \note See note for Heating High Water Temperature Schedule above for
  44329         \note interpretation information (or see the Input/Output Reference).
  44330         \type object-list
  44331         \object-list ScheduleNames
  44332    A17, \field Cooling Low Water Temperature Schedule Name
  44333         \type object-list
  44334         \object-list ScheduleNames
  44335    A18, \field Cooling High Control Temperature Schedule Name
  44336         \type object-list
  44337         \object-list ScheduleNames
  44338    A19, \field Cooling Low Control Temperature Schedule Name
  44339         \type object-list
  44340         \object-list ScheduleNames
  44341    A20, \field Condensation Control Type
  44342         \type choice
  44343         \key Off
  44344         \key SimpleOff
  44345         \key VariableOff
  44346         \default SimpleOff
  44347    N11, \field Condensation Control Dewpoint Offset
  44348         \units C
  44349         \default 1.0
