  46082 \group Zone HVAC Air Loop Terminal Units
  46083 
  46084 AirTerminal:SingleDuct:ConstantVolume:Reheat,
  46085        \memo Central air system terminal unit, single duct, constant volume, with reheat coil (hot
  46086        \memo water, electric, gas, or steam).
  46087   A1 , \field Name
  46088        \required-field
  46089        \reference AirTerminalUnitNames
  46090        \reference AFNTerminalUnitNames
  46091   A2 , \field Availability Schedule Name
  46092        \note Availability schedule name for this system. Schedule value > 0 means the system is available.
  46093        \note If this field is blank, the system is always available.
  46094        \type object-list
  46095        \object-list ScheduleNames
  46096   A3,  \field Air Outlet Node Name
  46097        \required-field
  46098        \type node
  46099   A4,  \field Air Inlet Node Name
  46100        \required-field
  46101        \type node
  46102   N1,  \field Maximum Air Flow Rate
  46103        \required-field
  46104        \units m3/s
  46105        \minimum 0.0
  46106        \autosizable
  46107   A5,  \field Reheat Coil Object Type
  46108        \required-field
  46109        \type choice
  46110        \key Coil:Heating:Water
  46111        \key Coil:Heating:Electric
  46112        \key Coil:Heating:Fuel
  46113        \key Coil:Heating:Steam
  46114   A6,  \field Reheat Coil Name
  46115        \required-field
  46116        \type object-list
  46117        \object-list HeatingCoilName
  46118   N2,  \field Maximum Hot Water or Steam Flow Rate
  46119        \note Not used when reheat coil type is gas or electric
  46120        \units m3/s
  46121        \minimum 0.0
  46122        \autosizable
  46123        \ip-units gal/min
  46124   N3,  \field Minimum Hot Water or Steam Flow Rate
  46125        \note Not used when reheat coil type is gas or electric
  46126        \units m3/s
  46127        \minimum 0.0
  46128        \default 0.0
  46129        \ip-units gal/min
  46130   N4,  \field Convergence Tolerance
  46131        \type real
  46132        \minimum> 0.0
  46133        \default 0.001
  46134   N5; \field Maximum Reheat Air Temperature
  46135       \note Specifies the maximum allowable supply air temperature leaving the reheat coil.
  46136       \note If left blank, there is no limit and no default. If unknown, 35C (95F) is recommended.
  46137       \type real
  46138       \units C
  46139       \minimum> 0.0
  46140 
  46141 AirTerminal:SingleDuct:ConstantVolume:NoReheat,
  46142        \memo Central air system terminal unit, single duct, constant volume, without reheat coil
  46143        \min-fields 5
  46144   A1 , \field Name
  46145        \required-field
  46146        \reference AirTerminalUnitNames
  46147        \reference AFNTerminalUnitNames
  46148   A2 , \field Availability Schedule Name
  46149        \note Availability schedule name for this system. Schedule value > 0 means the system is available.
  46150        \note If this field is blank, the system is always available.
  46151        \type object-list
  46152        \object-list ScheduleNames
  46153   A3,  \field Air Inlet Node Name
  46154        \required-field
  46155        \type node
  46156        \note The air-inlet node name that connects the air splitter to the individual zone air distribution
  46157        \note unit. This node should also be one of the outlet air node of an AirLoopHVAC:ZoneSplitter or
  46158        \note AirLoopHVAC:SupplyPlenum component.
  46159   A4,  \field Air Outlet Node Name
  46160        \required-field
  46161        \type node
  46162        \note This is an air outlet node from the air distribution unit. This node name should be one of the
  46163        \note supply air inlet node names of a zone served by this component.
  46164   N1,  \field Maximum Air Flow Rate
  46165        \required-field
  46166        \units m3/s
  46167        \minimum 0.0
  46168        \autosizable
  46169    A5, \field Design Specification Outdoor Air Object Name
  46170        \type object-list
  46171        \object-list DesignSpecificationOutdoorAirNames
  46172        \note This field is used to modulate the terminal unit flow rate based on the specified outdoor air
  46173        \note requirement. When the name of a DesignSpecification:OutdoorAir object is entered, the terminal unit will
  46174        \note adjust flow to meet this outdoor air requirement and no more. There is no control for zone load.
  46175        \note If Outdoor Air Flow per Person is non-zero, then the outdoor air requirement will be computed based
  46176        \note on either the current or design occupancy as specified in the Per Person Ventilation Rate Mode field.
  46177        \note At no time will the supply air flow rate exceed the value for Maximum Air Flow Rate. The requested flow
  46178        \note rate may not be fully met if the system is operating with cycling fan. If this field is blank, then
  46179        \note the terminal unit will not be controlled for outdoor air flow. This field is optional.
  46180    A6; \field Per Person Ventilation Rate Mode
  46181        \type choice
  46182        \key CurrentOccupancy
  46183        \key DesignOccupancy
  46184        \default CurrentOccupancy
  46185        \note CurrentOccupancy uses current number of people in the zone which may vary
  46186        \note DesignOccupancy uses the total number of people in the zone and is constant
  46187 
  46188 AirTerminal:SingleDuct:VAV:NoReheat,
  46189        \memo Central air system terminal unit, single duct, variable volume, with no reheat coil.
  46190   A1,  \field Name
  46191        \required-field
  46192        \reference AirTerminalUnitNames
  46193   A2,  \field Availability Schedule Name
  46194        \note Availability schedule name for this system. Schedule value > 0 means the system is available.
  46195        \note If this field is blank, the system is always available.
  46196        \type object-list
  46197        \object-list ScheduleNames
  46198   A3,  \field Air Outlet Node Name
  46199        \required-field
  46200        \type node
  46201   A4,  \field Air Inlet Node Name
  46202        \required-field
  46203        \type node
  46204   N1,  \field Maximum Air Flow Rate
  46205        \required-field
  46206        \units m3/s
  46207        \minimum 0.0
  46208        \autosizable
  46209   A5 , \field Zone Minimum Air Flow Input Method
  46210        \type choice
  46211        \key Constant
  46212        \key FixedFlowRate
  46213        \key Scheduled
  46214        \default Constant
  46215        \note Constant = Constant Minimum Air Flow Fraction (a fraction of Maximum Air Flow Rate)
  46216        \note FixedFlowRate = Fixed Minimum Air Flow Rate (a fixed minimum air volume flow rate)
  46217        \note Scheduled = Scheduled Minimum Air Flow Fraction (a fraction of Maximum Air Flow
  46218   N2 , \field Constant Minimum Air Flow Fraction
  46219        \type real
  46220        \autosizable
  46221        \default autosize
  46222        \note This field is used if the field Zone Minimum Air Flow Input Method is Constant
  46223        \note If the field Zone Minimum Air Flow Input Method is Scheduled, then this field
  46224        \note is optional; if a value is entered, then it is used for sizing normal-action reheat coils.
  46225        \note If both this field and the following field are entered, the larger result is used.
  46226        \note The values for autosizing are picked up from the Sizing:Zone input fields
  46227        \note "Cooling Minimum Air Flow per Zone Floor Area", "Cooling Minimum Air Flow", and
  46228        \note "Cooling Minimum Air Flow Fraction". If there is no sizing calculation a default of
  46229        \note 0.000762 m3/s-m2 (0.15 cfm/ft2) is used.
  46230   N3 , \field Fixed Minimum Air Flow Rate
  46231        \type real
  46232        \units m3/s
  46233        \autosizable
  46234        \default autosize
  46235        \note This field is used if the field Zone Minimum Air Flow Input Method is FixedFlowRate.
  46236        \note If the field Zone Minimum Air Flow Input Method is Scheduled, then this field
  46237        \note is optional; if a value is entered, then it is used for sizing normal-action reheat coils.
  46238        \note If both this field and the previous field are entered, the larger result is used.
  46239        \note The values for autosizing are picked up from the Sizing:Zone input fields
  46240        \note "Cooling Minimum Air Flow per Zone Floor Area", "Cooling Minimum Air Flow", and
  46241        \note "Cooling Minimum Air Flow Fraction". If there is no sizing calculation a default of
  46242        \note 0.000762 m3/s-m2 (0.15 cfm/ft2) is used.
  46243   A6 , \field Minimum Air Flow Fraction Schedule Name
  46244        \type object-list
  46245        \object-list ScheduleNames
  46246        \note This field is used if the field Zone Minimum Air Flow Input Method is Scheduled
  46247        \note Schedule values are fractions, 0.0 to 1.0.
  46248        \note If the field Constant Minimum Air Flow Fraction is blank, then the average of the
  46249        \note minimum and maximum schedule values is used for sizing normal-action reheat coils.
  46250   A7 , \field Design Specification Outdoor Air Object Name
  46251        \type object-list
  46252        \object-list DesignSpecificationOutdoorAirNames
  46253        \note When the name of a DesignSpecification:OutdoorAir object is entered, the terminal
  46254        \note unit will increase flow as needed to meet this outdoor air requirement.
  46255        \note If Outdoor Air Flow per Person is non-zero, then the outdoor air requirement will
  46256        \note be computed based on the current number of occupants in the zone.
  46257        \note At no time will the supply air flow rate exceed the value for Maximum Air Flow Rate.
  46258        \note If this field is blank, then the terminal unit will not be controlled for outdoor air flow.
  46259   A8 ; \field Minimum Air Flow Turndown Schedule Name
  46260        \type object-list
  46261        \object-list ScheduleNames
  46262        \note This field adjusts the design minimum flow rate by multiplying it using this schedule of fraction
  46263        \note values. This field can be used with any of the three "Zone Minimum Air Flow Input Method".
  46264        \note Schedule values are fractions, 0.0 to 1.0. This field adjusts the minimum airflow turndown
  46265        \note below the design minimum air flow and is intended for use with ASHRAE Standard 170.
  46266        \note If this field is left blank, then the turndown minimum air flow fraction value is set to 1.
  46267 
  46268 AirTerminal:SingleDuct:VAV:Reheat,
  46269        \memo Central air system terminal unit, single duct, variable volume, with reheat coil (hot
  46270        \memo water, electric, gas, or steam).
  46271        \min-fields 18
  46272   A1 , \field Name
  46273        \required-field
  46274        \reference AirTerminalUnitNames
  46275        \reference AFNTerminalUnitNames
  46276   A2 , \field Availability Schedule Name
  46277        \note Availability schedule name for this system. Schedule value > 0 means the system is available.
  46278        \note If this field is blank, the system is always available.
  46279        \type object-list
  46280        \object-list ScheduleNames
  46281   A3 , \field Damper Air Outlet Node Name
  46282        \note the outlet node of the damper and the inlet node of the reheat coil
  46283        \note this is an internal node to the terminal unit and connects the damper and reheat coil
  46284        \required-field
  46285        \type node
  46286   A4 , \field Air Inlet Node Name
  46287        \note the inlet node to the terminal unit and the damper
  46288        \required-field
  46289        \type node
  46290   N1 , \field Maximum Air Flow Rate
  46291        \required-field
  46292        \units m3/s
  46293        \minimum 0.0
  46294        \autosizable
  46295   A5 , \field Zone Minimum Air Flow Input Method
  46296        \type choice
  46297        \key Constant
  46298        \key FixedFlowRate
  46299        \key Scheduled
  46300        \default Constant
  46301        \note Constant = Constant Minimum Air Flow Fraction (a fraction of Maximum Air Flow Rate)
  46302        \note FixedFlowRate = Fixed Minimum Air Flow Rate (a fixed minimum air volume flow rate)
  46303        \note Scheduled = Scheduled Minimum Air Flow Fraction (a fraction of Maximum Air Flow
  46304   N2 , \field Constant Minimum Air Flow Fraction
  46305        \type real
  46306        \autosizable
  46307        \default autosize
  46308        \note This field is used if the field Zone Minimum Air Flow Input Method is Constant
  46309        \note If the field Zone Minimum Air Flow Input Method is Scheduled, then this field
  46310        \note is optional; if a value is entered, then it is used for sizing normal-action reheat coils.
  46311        \note If both this field and the following field are entered, the larger result is used.
  46312        \note The values for autosizing are picked up from the Sizing:Zone input fields
  46313        \note "Cooling Minimum Air Flow per Zone Floor Area", "Cooling Minimum Air Flow", and
  46314        \note "Cooling Minimum Air Flow Fraction". If there is no sizing calculation a default of
  46315        \note 0.000762 m3/s-m2 (0.15 cfm/ft2) is used.
  46316   N3 , \field Fixed Minimum Air Flow Rate
  46317        \type real
  46318        \units m3/s
  46319        \autosizable
  46320        \default autosize
  46321        \note This field is used if the field Zone Minimum Air Flow Input Method is FixedFlowRate.
  46322        \note If the field Zone Minimum Air Flow Input Method is Scheduled, then this field
  46323        \note is optional; if a value is entered, then it is used for sizing normal-action reheat coils.
  46324        \note If both this field and the previous field are entered, the larger result is used.
  46325        \note The values for autosizing are picked up from the Sizing:Zone input fields
  46326        \note "Cooling Minimum Air Flow per Zone Floor Area", "Cooling Minimum Air Flow", and
  46327        \note "Cooling Minimum Air Flow Fraction". If there is no sizing calculation a default of
  46328        \note 0.000762 m3/s-m2 (0.15 cfm/ft2) is used.
  46329   A6 , \field Minimum Air Flow Fraction Schedule Name
  46330        \type object-list
  46331        \object-list ScheduleNames
  46332        \note This field is used if the field Zone Minimum Air Flow Input Method is Scheduled
  46333        \note Schedule values are fractions, 0.0 to 1.0.
  46334        \note If the field Constant Minimum Air Flow Fraction is blank, then the average of the
  46335        \note minimum and maximum schedule values is used for sizing normal-action reheat coils.
  46336   A7 , \field Reheat Coil Object Type
  46337        \required-field
  46338        \type choice
  46339        \key Coil:Heating:Water
  46340        \key Coil:Heating:Electric
  46341        \key Coil:Heating:Fuel
  46342        \key Coil:Heating:Steam
  46343   A8 , \field Reheat Coil Name
  46344        \required-field
  46345        \type object-list
  46346        \object-list HeatingCoilName
  46347   N4 , \field Maximum Hot Water or Steam Flow Rate
  46348        \note Not used when reheat coil type is gas or electric
  46349        \units m3/s
  46350        \minimum 0.0
  46351        \autosizable
  46352        \ip-units gal/min
  46353   N5 , \field Minimum Hot Water or Steam Flow Rate
  46354        \note Not used when reheat coil type is gas or electric
  46355        \units m3/s
  46356        \minimum 0.0
  46357        \default 0.0
  46358        \ip-units gal/min
  46359   A9 , \field Air Outlet Node Name
  46360        \required-field
  46361        \type node
  46362        \note The outlet node of the terminal unit and the reheat coil.
  46363        \note This is also the zone inlet node.
  46364   N6 , \field Convergence Tolerance
  46365        \type real
  46366        \minimum> 0.0
  46367        \default 0.001
  46368   A10, \field Damper Heating Action
  46369        \type choice
  46370        \key Normal
  46371        \key Reverse
  46372        \key ReverseWithLimits
  46373        \default ReverseWithLimits
  46374        \note Normal means the damper is fixed at the minimum position in heating mode
  46375        \note Reverse means the damper can open fully during reheat
  46376        \note ReverseWithLimits means the damper will open partially during reheat
  46377        \note as specified in the following 2 fields
  46378   N7 , \field Maximum Flow per Zone Floor Area During Reheat
  46379        \type real
  46380        \units m3/s-m2
  46381        \autosizable
  46382        \default autosize
  46383        \note Used only when Reheat Coil Object Type = Coil:Heating:Water and Damper Heating Action = ReverseWithLimits
  46384        \note When autocalculating, the maximum flow per zone is set to 0.002032 m3/s-m2 (0.4 cfm/sqft)
  46385        \note This optional field limits the maximum flow allowed in reheat mode.
  46386        \note At no time will the maximum flow rate calculated here exceed the value of
  46387        \note Maximum Air Flow Rate.
  46388   N8 , \field Maximum Flow Fraction During Reheat
  46389        \type real
  46390        \autosizable
  46391        \default autosize
  46392        \note Used only when Reheat Coil Object Type = Coil:Heating:Water and Damper Heating Action = ReverseWithLimits
  46393        \note When autocalculating, the maximum flow fraction is set to the ratio of
  46394        \note 0.002032 m3/s-m2 (0.4 cfm/sqft) multiplied by the zone floor area and the
  46395        \note Maximum Air Flow Rate.
  46396        \note This optional field limits the maximum flow allowed in reheat mode.
  46397        \note At no time will the maximum flow rate calculated here exceed the value of
  46398        \note Maximum Air Flow Rate.
  46399   N9 , \field Maximum Reheat Air Temperature
  46400        \type real
  46401        \units C
  46402        \minimum> 0.0
  46403        \note Specifies the maximum allowable supply air temperature leaving the reheat coil.
  46404        \note If left blank, there is no limit and no default. If unknown, 35C (95F) is recommended.
  46405   A11, \field Design Specification Outdoor Air Object Name
  46406        \type object-list
  46407        \object-list DesignSpecificationOutdoorAirNames
  46408        \note When the name of a DesignSpecification:OutdoorAir object is entered, the terminal
  46409        \note unit will increase flow as needed to meet this outdoor air requirement.
  46410        \note If Outdoor Air Flow per Person is non-zero, then the outdoor air requirement will
  46411        \note be computed based on the current number of occupants in the zone.
  46412        \note At no time will the supply air flow rate exceed the value for Maximum Air Flow Rate.
  46413        \note If this field is blank, then the terminal unit will not be controlled for outdoor air flow.
  46414   A12; \field Minimum Air Flow Turndown Schedule Name
  46415        \type object-list
  46416        \object-list ScheduleNames
  46417        \note This field adjusts the design minimum flow rate by multiplying it using this schedule of fraction
  46418        \note values. This field can be used with any of the three "Zone Minimum Air Flow Input Method".
  46419        \note Schedule values are fractions, 0.0 to 1.0. This field adjusts the minimum airflow turndown
  46420        \note below the design minimum air flow and is intended for use with ASHRAE Standard 170.
  46421        \note If this field is left blank, then the turndown minimum air flow fraction value is set to 1.
  46422 
