  47155 AirTerminal:SingleDuct:Mixer,
  47156        \memo The mixer air terminal unit provides a means of supplying central system
  47157        \memo air to the air inlet or outlet side of a zoneHVAC equipment such as a four
  47158        \memo pipe fan coil unit. Normally the central air would be ventilation air from
  47159        \memo a dedicated outdoor air system (DOAS).
  47160    A1, \field Name
  47161        \required-field
  47162        \reference AirTerminalUnitNames
  47163    A2, \field ZoneHVAC Unit Object Type
  47164        \required-field
  47165        \type choice
  47166        \key ZoneHVAC:FourPipeFanCoil
  47167        \key ZoneHVAC:WaterToAirHeatPump
  47168        \key ZoneHVAC:PackagedTerminalAirConditioner
  47169        \key ZoneHVAC:PackagedTerminalHeatPump
  47170        \key ZoneHVAC:TerminalUnit:VariableRefrigerantFlow
  47171        \key ZoneHVAC:UnitVentilator
  47172        \key AirLoopHVAC:UnitarySystem
  47173        \note The type of ZoneHVAC equipment to which this terminal mixer will be connected.
  47174    A3, \field ZoneHVAC Unit Object Name
  47175        \required-field
  47176        \type object-list
  47177        \object-list DOAToZonalUnit
  47178        \note The name of ZoneHVAC equipment to which this terminal mixer will be connected.
  47179    A4, \field Mixer Outlet Node Name
  47180        \required-field
  47181        \type node
  47182        \note This is the outlet air node name of the mixer. This will be the inlet air node name
  47183        \note of the ZoneHVAC equipment if the connection type in the input field Mixer Connection
  47184        \note Type below is InletSide, else this will be an inlet air node name of the conditioned zone
  47185        \note if the connection type in the input field Mixer Connection Type below is SupplySide.
  47186    A5, \field Mixer Primary Air Inlet Node Name
  47187        \required-field
  47188        \type node
  47189        \note The primary air (treated outdoor air) inlet node name of the mixer. This will be an
  47190        \note outlet air node name of an AirLoopHVAC:ZoneSplitter or AirLoopHVAC:SupplyPlenum providing
  47191        \note the connection to the DOA system.
  47192    A6, \field Mixer Secondary Air Inlet Node Name
  47193        \required-field
  47194        \type node
  47195        \note The secondary air (recirculating air) inlet node name of the mixer. This will be
  47196        \note the outlet air node name of the ZoneHVAC equipment if the connection type in the
  47197        \note input field mixer Connection Type below is SupplySide, or else this will be an exhaust
  47198        \note air node name of the conditioned zone if the connection type in the input field
  47199        \note Mixer Connection Type below is InletSide.
  47200    A7, \field Mixer Connection Type
  47201        \required-field
  47202        \type choice
  47203        \key InletSide
  47204        \key SupplySide
  47205        \note This input field allows user to specify the mixer connection type. Valid choices
  47206        \note are InletSide or SupplySide. This is a required input field. If the mixer connection
  47207        \note type selected is InletSide, then the mixer is connected on the inlet side of the
  47208        \note ZoneHVAC equipment, or else if the mixer connection type selected is SupplySide, then
  47209        \note the mixer is connected at the outlet side of the ZoneHVAC equipment.
  47210    A8, \field Design Specification Outdoor Air Object Name
  47211        \type object-list
  47212        \object-list DesignSpecificationOutdoorAirNames
  47213        \note When the name of a DesignSpecification:OutdoorAir object is entered, the terminal
  47214        \note unit will adjust flow to meet this outdoor air requirement.
  47215        \note If Outdoor Air Flow per Person is non-zero, then the outdoor air requirement will
  47216        \note be computed based on the current number of occupants in the zone, as for demand controlled ventilation.
  47217        \note If this field is blank, then the terminal unit will be controlled using the
  47218        \note DesignSpecification:OutdoorAir objec referenced in the Sizing:Zone object.
  47219    A9; \field Per Person Ventilation Rate Mode
  47220        \type choice
  47221        \key CurrentOccupancy
  47222        \key DesignOccupancy
  47223        \default CurrentOccupancy
  47224        \note CurrentOccupancy models demand controlled ventilation using the current number of people
  47225        \note DesignOccupancy uses the total Number of People in the zone and is constant
  47226 
