  49399 Coil:Cooling:DX,
  49400        \memo New general DX cooling coil supporting on or more speeds and one or or operating  modes.
  49401        \memo Includes DX evaporator coil, compressor, and condenser.
  49402        \memo Object is currently only supported by the AIRLOOPHVAC:UNITARYSYSTEM object.
  49403        \memo Remaining Coil:Cooling:DX* objects will be deprecated at a future date,
  49404        \memo after which, this object will replace all other Coil:Cooling:DX* objects.
  49405        \min-fields 8
  49406    A1, \field Name
  49407        \required-field
  49408        \type alpha
  49409        \reference CoilCoolingDX
  49410        \reference AFNCoilNames
  49411    A2, \field Evaporator Inlet Node Name
  49412        \required-field
  49413        \type node
  49414    A3, \field Evaporator Outlet Node Name
  49415        \required-field
  49416        \type node
  49417    A4, \field Availability Schedule Name
  49418        \note Schedule value > 0 means the coil is available.
  49419        \note If this field is blank, the coil is always available.
  49420        \type object-list
  49421        \object-list ScheduleNames
  49422    A5, \field Condenser Zone Name
  49423        \note This input field is name of a conditioned or unconditioned zone where the secondary
  49424        \note coil (condenser) of a DX system or heat pump is to be placed.  This is an optional
  49425        \note input field specified only when the user desires to reject the condenser heat into a
  49426        \note zone. The heat rejected is modeled as internal sensible heat gain of the zone.
  49427        \type object-list
  49428        \object-list ZoneNames
  49429    A6, \field Condenser Inlet Node Name
  49430        \required-field
  49431        \note This is the name of an air node in the simulation.  This may be an explicitly defined outdoor
  49432        \note air node, or it may be a separate air node.
  49433        \type node
  49434    A7, \field Condenser Outlet Node Name
  49435        \required-field
  49436        \note This is the name of an air node in the simulation.
  49437        \type node
  49438    A8, \field Performance Object Name
  49439        \required-field
  49440        \type object-list
  49441        \object-list DXCoolingPerformanceNames
  49442    A9, \field Condensate Collection Water Storage Tank Name
  49443        \type object-list
  49444        \object-list WaterStorageTankNames
  49445   A10; \field Evaporative Condenser Supply Water Storage Tank Name
  49446        \type object-list
  49447        \object-list WaterStorageTankNames
  49448 
  49449 Coil:Cooling:DX:CurveFit:Performance,
  49450        \memo DX cooling coil performance specification referencing one or more
  49451        \memo operating modes. Mode 1 is always the base design operating mode.
  49452        \memo Additional modes are optional states such as subcool reheat for humidity control.
  49453        \min-fields 11
  49454    A1, \field Name
  49455        \required-field
  49456        \type alpha
  49457        \reference DXCoolingPerformanceNames
  49458    N1, \field Crankcase Heater Capacity
  49459        \type real
  49460        \minimum 0.0
  49461        \default 0.0
  49462        \units W
  49463        \ip-units W
  49464    N2, \field Minimum Outdoor Dry-Bulb Temperature for Compressor Operation
  49465        \type real
  49466        \default -25.0
  49467        \units C
  49468    N3, \field Maximum Outdoor Dry-Bulb Temperature for Crankcase Heater Operation
  49469        \type real
  49470        \minimum 0.0
  49471        \default 10.0
  49472        \units C
  49473    N4, \field Unit Internal Static Air Pressure
  49474        \note Enter pressure drop for the unit containing the coil.
  49475        \note This value is only used to calculate Energy Efficiency Ratio
  49476        \note (EER), Integrated Energy Efficiency Ratio (IEER), and the
  49477        \note Standard Rating (Net) Cooling Capacity. This value is not
  49478        \note used for modeling the evaporator fan during simulations.
  49479        \type real
  49480        \units Pa
  49481        \minimum> 0.0
  49482    A2, \field Capacity Control Method
  49483        \type choice
  49484        \key Discrete
  49485        \key Continuous
  49486        \default Discrete
  49487    N5, \field Evaporative Condenser Basin Heater Capacity
  49488        \note This field is only used for Condenser Type = EvaporativelyCooled and for periods
  49489        \note when the basin heater is available (field Basin Heater Operating Schedule Name).
  49490        \note For this situation, the heater maintains the basin water temperature at the basin heater
  49491        \note setpoint temperature when the outdoor air temperature falls below the setpoint temperature.
  49492        \note The basin heater only operates when the DX coil is off.
  49493        \type real
  49494        \units W/K
  49495        \minimum 0.0
  49496        \default 0.0
  49497    N6, \field Evaporative Condenser Basin Heater Setpoint Temperature
  49498        \note This field is only used for Condenser Type = EvaporativelyCooled.
  49499        \note Enter the outdoor dry-bulb temperature when the basin heater turns on.
  49500        \type real
  49501        \units C
  49502        \minimum 2.0
  49503        \default 2.0
  49504    A3, \field Evaporative Condenser Basin Heater Operating Schedule Name
  49505        \note This field is only used for Condenser Type = EvaporativelyCooled.
  49506        \note Schedule values greater than 0 allow the basin heater to operate whenever the outdoor
  49507        \note air dry-bulb temperature is below the basin heater setpoint temperature.
  49508        \note If a schedule name is not entered, the basin heater is allowed to operate
  49509        \note throughout the entire simulation.
  49510        \type object-list
  49511        \object-list ScheduleNames
  49512    A4, \field Compressor Fuel Type
  49513        \type choice
  49514        \key Electricity
  49515        \key NaturalGas
  49516        \key Propane
  49517        \key Diesel
  49518        \key Gasoline
  49519        \key FuelOilNo1
  49520        \key FuelOilNo2
  49521        \key OtherFuel1
  49522        \key OtherFuel2
  49523        \default Electricity
  49524    A5, \field Base Operating Mode
  49525        \note Operating Mode 1 is always used as the base design operating mode.
  49526        \required-field
  49527        \type object-list
  49528        \object-list DXCoolingOperatingModeNames
  49529    A6, \field Alternative Operating Mode 1
  49530        \note The alternative operating mode is used for enhanced dehumidification.
  49531        \note If this is blank, the coil will always operate in the base operating mode.
  49532        \note If an alternate mode is defined here, the coil will use the enhanced mode if
  49533        \note activated by the parent system controls.
  49534        \type object-list
  49535        \object-list DXCoolingOperatingModeNames
  49536    A7; \field Alternative Operating Mode 2
  49537        \note The alternative operating mode is used for enhanced dehumidification.
  49538        \note If this is blank, the coil will always operate in the base operating mode or
  49539        \note Alternative Mode 1. If both Alternative Operating Mode 1 and Mode 2 are defined here,
  49540        \note the coil will perform both Subcool and Reheat modes for enhanced dehumidification.
  49541        \note Alternative Operating Mode 1 is used as Subcool mode, and Alternative Operating Mode 2
  49542        \note is used as Reheat mode.
  49543        \type object-list
  49544        \object-list DXCoolingOperatingModeNames
  49545 
  49546 Coil:Cooling:DX:CurveFit:OperatingMode,
  49547        \memo DX cooling coil performance for a single operating mode which may have one or more speeds.
  49548        \min-fields 13
  49549    A1, \field Name
  49550        \required-field
  49551        \type alpha
  49552        \reference DXCoolingOperatingModeNames
  49553    N1, \field Rated Gross Total Cooling Capacity
  49554        \note Total (sensible+latent) cooling capacity not accounting for the effect of supply air fan heat.
  49555        \note Rating point: air entering the evaporator coil at 26.7 C dry-bulb/19.4 C wet-bulb, and
  49556        \note air entering the condenser coil at 35 C dry-bulb/23.9 C wet-bulb.
  49557        \type real
  49558        \units W
  49559        \minimum> 0.0
  49560        \autosizable
  49561        \default autosize
  49562        \note gross capacity excluding supply air fan heat
  49563    N2, \field Rated Evaporator Air Flow Rate
  49564        \note Flow rate corresponding to rated total cooling capacity, Rated SHR and Rated COP.
  49565        \note Should be between 0.00004027 m3/s and 0.00006041 m3/s per watt of rated total cooling capacity.
  49566        \type real
  49567        \units m3/s
  49568        \minimum> 0.0
  49569        \autosizable
  49570    N3, \field Rated Condenser Air Flow Rate
  49571        \note Used to calculate evaporative condenser water use.
  49572        \type real
  49573        \units m3/s
  49574        \minimum> 0.0
  49575        \autosizable
  49576    N4, \field Maximum Cycling Rate
  49577        \note The maximum on-off cycling Rate for the compressor, which occurs at 50% run time
  49578        \note fraction. Suggested value is 3; zero value means latent degradation model is disabled.
  49579        \type real
  49580        \units cycles/hr
  49581        \minimum 0.0
  49582        \maximum 5.0
  49583        \default 0.0
  49584    N5, \field Ratio of Initial Moisture Evaporation Rate and Steady State Latent Capacity
  49585        \note Ratio of the initial moisture evaporation rate from the cooling coil (when
  49586        \note the compressor first turns off) and the coil's steady state latent capacity
  49587        \note at rated air flow rate and temperature conditions. Suggested value is 1.5; zero value
  49588        \note means latent degradation model is disabled.
  49589        \type real
  49590        \units dimensionless
  49591        \minimum 0.0
  49592        \maximum 5.0
  49593        \default 0.0
  49594    N6, \field Latent Capacity Time Constant
  49595        \note Time constant for the cooling coil's latent capacity to reach steady state after
  49596        \note startup. Suggested value is 45; zero value means latent degradation model is disabled.
  49597        \type real
  49598        \units s
  49599        \minimum 0.0
  49600        \maximum 500.0
  49601        \default 0.0
  49602    N7, \field Nominal Time for Condensate Removal to Begin
  49603        \note The nominal time for condensate to begin leaving the coil's condensate
  49604        \note drain line at the coil's rated air flow rate and temperature conditions.
  49605        \note Nominal time is equal to the ratio of the energy of the coil's maximum
  49606        \note condensate holding capacity (J) to the coil's steady state latent capacity (W).
  49607        \note Suggested value is 1000; zero value means latent degradation model is disabled.
  49608        \type real
  49609        \units s
  49610        \minimum 0.0
  49611        \maximum 3000.0
  49612        \default 0.0
  49613    A2, \field Apply Latent Degradation to Speeds Greater than 1
  49614        \type choice
  49615        \key Yes
  49616        \key No
  49617        \default No
  49618    A3, \field Condenser Type
  49619        \type choice
  49620        \key AirCooled
  49621        \key EvaporativelyCooled
  49622        \default AirCooled
  49623    N8, \field Nominal Evaporative Condenser Pump Power
  49624        \note Rated power consumed by the evaporative condenser's water pump
  49625        \type real
  49626        \units W
  49627        \minimum 0.0
  49628        \default 0.0
  49629        \autosizable
  49630    N9, \field Nominal Speed Number
  49631        \note Must be lower than or equal to the highest speed number.
