  51760 CoilPerformance:DX:Cooling,
  51761        \memo Used to specify DX cooling coil performance for one mode of operation for a
  51762        \memo Coil:Cooling:DX:TwoStageWithHumidityControlMode object which may reference one to four
  51763        \memo CoilPerformance:DX:Cooling objects depending on the specified number of stages and
  51764        \memo dehumidification modes. In nearly all cases, the Rated Air Flow Rate will be the same
  51765        \memo for all performance objects associated with a given coil. If bypass is specified,
  51766        \memo the Rated Air Flow Rate includes both the bypassed flow and the flow through the
  51767        \memo active part of the coil.
  51768   \min-fields 11
  51769   A1 , \field Name
  51770        \required-field
  51771        \type alpha
  51772        \reference CoilPerformanceDX
  51773   N1 , \field Gross Rated Total Cooling Capacity
  51774        \note Total cooling capacity not accounting for the effect of supply air fan heat
  51775        \required-field
  51776        \type real
  51777        \units W
  51778        \minimum> 0.0
  51779        \autosizable
  51780        \note gross capacity excluding supply air fan heat
  51781        \note rating point: air entering the cooling coil at 26.7 C dry-bulb/19.4 C wet-bulb, and
  51782        \note air entering the outdoor condenser coil at 35 C dry-bulb/23.9 C wet-bulb
  51783   N2 , \field Gross Rated Sensible Heat Ratio
  51784        \required-field
  51785        \type real
  51786        \minimum 0.5
  51787        \maximum 1.0
  51788        \autosizable
  51789        \note Rated sensible heat ratio (gross sensible capacity/gross total capacity)
  51790        \note sensible and total capacities do not include supply fan heat
  51791   N3 , \field Gross Rated Cooling COP
  51792        \note Gross cooling capacity divided by power input to the compressor and outdoor fan,
  51793        \note does not include supply fan heat or supply fan electrical energy input
  51794        \type real
  51795        \units W/W
  51796        \minimum> 0.0
  51797        \default 3.0
  51798   N4 , \field Rated Air Flow Rate
  51799        \required-field
  51800        \type real
  51801        \units m3/s
  51802        \minimum> 0.0
  51803        \autosizable
  51804        \note Flow rate corresponding to Rated total Cooling capacity, Rated SHR and Rated COP
  51805   N5 , \field Fraction of Air Flow Bypassed Around Coil
  51806        \type real
  51807        \minimum 0.0
  51808        \maximum< 1.0
  51809        \default 0.0
  51810        \note Fraction of Rated Air Flow Rate which bypasses the cooling coil
  51811        \note in this performance mode.  The remaining portion of the flow
  51812        \note should be between 0.00004027 m3/s and .00006041 m3/s per watt of rated total cooling capacity.
  51813        \note This is used to model face-split coils on multi-stage units or bypass dampers.
  51814        \note If total flow rate varies during simulation, the same fraction is bypassed.
  51815   A2 , \field Total Cooling Capacity Function of Temperature Curve Name
  51816        \required-field
  51817        \type object-list
  51818        \object-list BivariateFunctions
  51819        \note curve = a + b*wb + c*wb**2 + d*edb + e*edb**2 + f*wb*edb
  51820        \note wb = entering wet-bulb temperature (C)
  51821        \note edb = dry-bulb temperature seen by the condenser (C)
  51822   A3 , \field Total Cooling Capacity Function of Flow Fraction Curve Name
  51823        \required-field
  51824        \type object-list
  51825        \object-list UnivariateFunctions
  51826        \note quadratic curve = a + b*ff + c*ff**2
  51827        \note cubic curve = a + b*ff + c*ff**2 + d*ff**3
  51828        \note ff = fraction of the full load flow
  51829   A4 , \field Energy Input Ratio Function of Temperature Curve Name
  51830        \required-field
  51831        \type object-list
  51832        \object-list BivariateFunctions
  51833        \note curve = a + b*wb + c*wb**2 + d*edb + e*edb**2 + f*wb*edb
  51834        \note wb = entering wet-bulb temperature (C)
  51835        \note edb = dry-bulb temperature seen by the condenser (C)
  51836   A5 , \field Energy Input Ratio Function of Flow Fraction Curve Name
  51837        \required-field
  51838        \type object-list
  51839        \object-list UnivariateFunctions
  51840        \note quadratic curve = a + b*ff + c*ff**2
  51841        \note cubic curve = a + b*ff + c*ff**2 + d*ff**3
  51842        \note ff = fraction of the full load flow
  51843   A6 , \field Part Load Fraction Correlation Curve Name
  51844        \required-field
  51845        \type object-list
  51846        \object-list UnivariateFunctions
  51847        \note quadratic curve = a + b*PLR + c*PLR**2
  51848        \note cubic curve = a + b*PLR + c*PLR**2 + d*PLR**3
  51849        \note PLR = part load ratio (cooling load/steady state capacity)
  51850   N6 , \field Nominal Time for Condensate Removal to Begin
  51851        \type real
  51852        \units s
  51853        \minimum 0.0
  51854        \maximum 3000.0
  51855        \default 0.0
  51856        \note The nominal time for condensate to begin leaving the coil's condensate
  51857        \note drain line at the coil's rated air flow rate and temperature conditions.
  51858        \note Nominal time is equal to the ratio of the energy of the coil's maximum
  51859        \note condensate holding capacity (J) to the coil's steady state latent capacity (W).
  51860        \note Suggested value is 1000; zero value means latent degradation model is disabled.
  51861   N7 , \field Ratio of Initial Moisture Evaporation Rate and Steady State Latent Capacity
  51862        \type real
  51863        \units dimensionless
  51864        \minimum 0.0
  51865        \maximum 5.0
  51866        \default 0.0
  51867        \note Ratio of the initial moisture evaporation rate from the cooling coil (when
  51868        \note the compressor first turns off) and the coil's steady state latent capacity
  51869        \note at rated air flow rate and temperature conditions. Suggested value is 1.5; zero value
  51870        \note means latent degradation model is disabled.
  51871   N8 , \field Maximum Cycling Rate
  51872        \type real
  51873        \units cycles/hr
  51874        \minimum 0.0
  51875        \maximum 5.0
  51876        \default 0.0
  51877        \note The maximum on-off cycling rate for the compressor, which occurs at 50% run time
  51878        \note fraction. Suggested value is 3; zero value means latent degradation model is disabled.
  51879   N9 , \field Latent Capacity Time Constant
  51880        \type real
  51881        \units s
  51882        \minimum 0.0
  51883        \maximum 500.0
  51884        \default 0.0
  51885        \note Time constant for the cooling coil's latent capacity to reach steady state after
  51886        \note startup. Suggested value is 45; zero value means latent degradation model is disabled.
  51887   A7 , \field Condenser Air Inlet Node Name
  51888        \type node
  51889        \note Enter the name of an outdoor air node. This node name is also specified in
  51890        \note an OutdoorAir:Node or OutdoorAir:NodeList object.
  51891   A8 , \field Condenser Type
  51892        \type choice
  51893        \key AirCooled
  51894        \key EvaporativelyCooled
  51895        \default AirCooled
  51896   N10 , \field Evaporative Condenser Effectiveness
  51897        \type real
  51898        \units dimensionless
  51899        \minimum 0.0
  51900        \maximum 1.0
  51901        \default 0.9
  51902   N11, \field Evaporative Condenser Air Flow Rate
  51903        \type real
  51904        \units m3/s
  51905        \minimum> 0.0
  51906        \autosizable
  51907        \note Used to calculate evaporative condenser water use
  51908   N12, \field Evaporative Condenser Pump Rated Power Consumption
  51909        \type real
  51910        \units W
  51911        \minimum 0.0
  51912        \default 0.0
  51913        \autosizable
  51914        \note Rated power consumed by the evaporative condenser's water pump
  51915   A9,  \field Sensible Heat Ratio Function of Temperature Curve Name
  51916        \type object-list
  51917        \object-list BivariateFunctions
  51918        \note curve = a + b*wb + c*wb**2 + d*db + e*db**2 + f*wb*db
  51919        \note wb = entering wet-bulb temperature seen by the DX cooling coil (C)
  51920        \note db = entering dry-bulb temperature seen by the DX cooling coil (C)
  51921        \note entering temperature can be outside air or pretreated air.
  51922   A10; \field Sensible Heat Ratio Function of Flow Fraction Curve Name
  51923        \type object-list
  51924        \object-list UnivariateFunctions
  51925        \note quadratic curve = a + b*ff + c*ff**2
  51926        \note cubic curve = a + b*ff + c*ff**2 + d*ff**3
  51927        \note ff = fraction of the full load flow
