  52430        \note parasitic electric load associated with the coil operation
  52431        \note such as an inducer fan, etc..  This will be modified by the part load ratio to reflect
  52432        \note the time of operation in a timestep.
  52433        \ip-units W
  52434   A7 , \field Part Load Fraction Correlation Curve Name
  52435        \type object-list
  52436        \object-list UnivariateFunctions
  52437        \note quadratic curve, PLF = a + b*PLR + c*PLR**2
  52438        \note cubic curve, PLF = a + b*PLR + c*PLR**2 + d*PLR**3
  52439        \note PLF = part load fraction
  52440        \note PLR = part load ratio (sensible heating load/steady state heating capacity)
  52441        \note Coil runtime fraction = Part Load Ratio / PLF
  52442        \note This part load degradation is for coil performance & will
  52443        \note increase the fuel consumption of the coil due to transient coil operation.
  52444   N4 ; \field Parasitic Fuel Load
  52445        \units W
  52446        \note parasitic fuel load associated with the coil operation (i.e., standing pilot)
  52447 
