  52783        \type integer
  52784        \minimum 1
  52785        \maximum 6
  52786        \default 4
  52787        \note Standard Region number for which HSPF and other standard ratings are calculated
  52788   A13, \field Evaporator Air Inlet Node Name
  52789        \type node
  52790        \note Enter the name of an outdoor air node. This node name is also specified in
  52791        \note an OutdoorAir:Node or OutdoorAir:NodeList object.
  52792   A14, \field Zone Name for Evaporator Placement
  52793        \note This input field is name of a conditioned or unconditioned zone where the secondary
  52794        \note coil (evaporator) of a heat pump is to be placed.  This is an optional input field
  52795        \note specified only when user desires to extract heat from the zone.  The heat extracted
  52796        \note is modelled as internal gain of the zone. If the primary DX system is a heat pump,
  52797        \note then the zone name should be the same as the zone name specified for placing the
  52798        \note secondary cooling DX coil.
  52799   N13, \field Secondary Coil Air Flow Rate
  52800        \type real
  52801        \units m3/s
  52802        \minimum> 0.0
  52803        \autosizable
  52804        \note This input value is the secondary coil (evaporator) air flow rate when the heat pump
  52805        \note is working in heating mode or the secondary DX coil (condenser) air flow rate when the
  52806        \note heat pump is working in cooling mode.
  52807   N14, \field Secondary Coil Fan Flow Scaling Factor
  52808        \type real
  52809        \units m3/s
  52810        \minimum> 0.0
  52811        \default 1.25
  52812        \note This input field is scaling factor for autosizing the secondary DX coil fan flow rate.
  52813        \note The secondary air flow rate is determined by multiplying the primary DX coil rated air
  52814        \note flow rate by the fan flow scaling factor. Default value is 1.25. If the secondary coil
  52815        \note fan flow rate is not autosized, then the secondary coil fan flow scaling factor is set
  52816        \note to 1.0.
  52817   N15, \field Nominal Sensible Heat Ratio of Secondary Coil
  52818        \type real
  52819        \units m3/s
  52820        \minimum> 0.0
  52821        \maximum 1.0
  52822        \note This input value is the nominal sensible heat ratio used to split the heat extracted by
  52823        \note a secondary DX coil (evaporator) of a heat pump into sensible and latent components.
  52824        \note This is an optional input field.  If this input field is left blank, then pure sensible
  52825        \note internal heat gain is assumed, i.e., sensible heat ratio of 1.0.
  52826   A15, \field Sensible Heat Ratio Modifier Function of Temperature Curve Name
  52827        \type object-list
  52828        \object-list BivariateFunctions
  52829        \note curve = a + b*wb + c*wb**2 + d*db + e*db**2 + f*wb*db
  52830        \note wb = entering wet-bulb temperature seen by the secondary DX coil (C)
  52831        \note db = entering dry-bulb temperature seen by the primary DX coil (C)
  52832        \note This input field is name of sensible heat ratio modifier biquadratic curve.  The value
  52833        \note of this curve modifies the nominal sensible heat ratio for current time step depending
  52834        \note on the secondary zone air node wet-bulb temperature and the heating DX coil entering
  52835        \note air dry-bulb temperature.  This is an optional input field.  If this input field is left
  52836        \note blank, then the nominal sensible heat ratio specified in the field above will be used.
  52837   A16; \field Sensible Heat Ratio Modifier Function of Flow Fraction Curve Name
  52838        \type object-list
  52839        \object-list UnivariateFunctions
  52840        \note quadratic curve = a + b*ff + c*ff**2
  52841        \note cubic curve = a + b*ff + c*ff**2 + d*ff**3
  52842        \note ff = secondary air flow fraction of the full load flow
  52843        \note This input field is name of sensible heat ratio modifier curve.  The value
  52844        \note of this curve modifies the nominal sensible heat ratio for current time step depending
  52845        \note on the secondary coil air flow fraction. This is an optional input field.  If this input
  52846        \note field is left blank, then the nominal sensible heat ratio specified will be used.
  52847 
