  53326   A34, \field Zone Name for Evaporator Placement
  53327        \note This input field is name of a conditioned or unconditioned zone where the secondary
  53328        \note coil (evaporator) of a heat pump is to be placed.  This is an optional input field
  53329        \note specified only when user desires to extract heat from the zone.  The heat extracted
  53330        \note is modeled as internal heat gain of the zone. If the primary DX system is a heat pump,
  53331        \note then the zone name should be the same as the zone name specified for placing the
  53332        \note secondary cooling DX coil.
  53333   N30, \field Speed 1 Secondary Coil Air Flow Rate
  53334        \type real
  53335        \units m3/s
  53336        \minimum> 0.0
  53337        \autosizable
  53338        \note This input value is the secondary coil (evaporator) air flow rate when the heat pump
  53339        \note is working in heating mode or the secondary DX coil (condenser) air flow rate when the
  53340        \note heat pump is working in cooling mode.
  53341   N31, \field Speed 1 Secondary Coil Fan Flow Scaling Factor
  53342        \type real
  53343        \units m3/s
  53344        \minimum> 0.0
  53345        \default 1.25
  53346        \note This input field is scaling factor for autosizing the secondary DX coil fan flow rate.
  53347        \note The secondary air flow rate is determined by multiplying the primary DX coil rated air
  53348        \note flow rate by the fan flow scaling factor. Default value is 1.25. If the secondary coil
  53349        \note fan flow rate is not autosized, then the secondary coil fan flow scaling factor is set
  53350        \note to 1.0.
  53351   N32, \field Speed 1 Nominal Sensible Heat Ratio of Secondary Coil
  53352        \type real
  53353        \units m3/s
  53354        \minimum> 0.0
  53355        \maximum 1.0
  53356        \note This input value is the nominal sensible heat ratio used to split the heat extracted by
  53357        \note a secondary DX coil (evaporator) of a heat pump into sensible and latent components.
  53358        \note This is an optional input field.  If this input field is left blank, then pure sensible
  53359        \note internal heat gain is assumed, i.e., sensible heat ratio of 1.0.
  53360   A35, \field Speed 1 Sensible Heat Ratio Modifier Function of Temperature Curve Name
  53361        \type object-list
  53362        \object-list BivariateFunctions
  53363        \note curve = a + b*wb + c*wb**2 + d*db + e*db**2 + f*wb*db
