  53526 Coil:Heating:DX:VariableSpeed,
  53527         \memo Direct expansion (DX) heating coil (air-to-air heat pump) and compressor unit
  53528         \memo (includes electric compressor and outdoor fan), variable-speed, with defrost
  53529         \memo controls. Requires two to ten sets of performance data and will interpolate between
  53530         \memo speeds.
  53531         \min-fields 25
  53532    A1,  \field Name
  53533         \required-field
  53534         \type alpha
  53535         \reference HeatingCoilsDXVariableSpeed
  53536    A2,  \field Indoor Air Inlet Node Name
  53537         \required-field
  53538         \type node
  53539    A3,  \field Indoor Air Outlet Node Name
  53540         \required-field
  53541         \type node
  53542    N1,  \field Number of Speeds
  53543         \units dimensionless
  53544         \type integer
  53545         \minimum 1
  53546         \maximum 10
  53547         \default 2
  53548    N2,  \field Nominal Speed Level
  53549         \units dimensionless
  53550         \type integer
  53551         \default 2
  53552         \note must be lower than or equal to the highest speed number
  53553    N3,  \field Rated Heating Capacity At Selected Nominal Speed Level
  53554         \units W
  53555         \type real
  53556         \autosizable
  53557         \default autosize
  53558    N4,  \field Rated Air Flow Rate At Selected Nominal Speed Level
  53559         \units m3/s
  53560         \type real
  53561         \autosizable
  53562         \default autosize
  53563    A4,  \field Energy Part Load Fraction Curve Name
  53564         \required-field
  53565         \type object-list
  53566         \object-list UnivariateFunctions
  53567         \note quadratic curve = a + b*PLR + c*PLR**2
  53568         \note cubic curve = a + b*PLR + c*PLR**2 + d*PLR**3
  53569         \note PLR = part load ratio (heating load/steady state capacity)
  53570    A5,  \field Defrost Energy Input Ratio Function of Temperature Curve Name
  53571         \type object-list
  53572         \object-list BivariateFunctions
  53573         \note biquadratic curve = a + b*wb + c*wb**2 + d*oat + e*oat**2 + f*wb*oat
  53574         \note wb = wet-bulb temperature (C) of air entering the indoor coil
  53575         \note oat = outdoor air dry-bulb temperature (C)
  53576         \note only required if ReverseCycle defrost strategy is specified
  53577    N5,  \field Minimum Outdoor Dry-Bulb Temperature for Compressor Operation
  53578         \type real
  53579         \default -8.0
  53580         \units C
  53581    N6,  \field Outdoor Dry-Bulb Temperature to Turn On Compressor
  53582         \type real
  53583         \units C
  53584         \note The outdoor temperature when the compressor is automatically turned back on following an
  53585         \note automatic shut off because of low outdoor dry-bulb temperature. This field is only used
  53586         \note for the calculation of HSPF. If this field is not provided, then outdoor bin temperature
  53587         \note used in the HSPF calculation is always considered to be greater than this temperature and
  53588         \note 'Minimum Outdoor Dry-Bulb Temperature for Compressor Operation' field described above.
  53589         \note This assumption is based on AHRI standard 210/240 (2008) and can introduce significant error
  53590         \note in the final value of HSPF.
  53591    N7,  \field Maximum Outdoor Dry-Bulb Temperature for Defrost Operation
  53592         \type real
  53593         \minimum 0.0
  53594         \maximum 7.22
  53595         \default 5.0
  53596         \units C
