  56139 Coil:WaterHeating:AirToWaterHeatPump:Pumped,
  56140        \memo Heat pump water heater (HPWH) heating coil, air-to-water direct-expansion (DX)
  56141        \memo system which includes a water heating coil, evaporator air coil, evaporator
  56142        \memo fan, electric compressor, and water pump. Part of a WaterHeater:HeatPump:PumpedCondenser system.
  56143        \min-fields 21
  56144   A1 , \field Name
  56145        \required-field
  56146        \type alpha
  56147        \reference HeatPumpWaterHeaterDXCoilsPumped
  56148        \note Unique name for this instance of a heat pump water heater DX coil.
  56149   N1 , \field Rated Heating Capacity
  56150        \required-field
  56151        \type real
  56152        \units W
  56153        \minimum> 0
  56154        \note Heating capacity at the rated inlet air temperatures, rated condenser inlet
  56155        \note water temperature, rated air flow rate, and rated water flow rate.
  56156        \note Can optionally include condenser pump heat.
  56157   N2 , \field Rated COP
  56158        \type real
  56159        \units W/W
  56160        \minimum> 0
  56161        \default 3.2
  56162        \note Heating coefficient of performance at the rated inlet air temperatures,
  56163        \note rated condenser inlet water temperature, rated air flow rate, and rated water flow rate.
  56164        \note Can optionally include condenser pump power and evaporator fan power (see fields below).
  56165   N3 , \field Rated Sensible Heat Ratio
  56166        \type real
  56167        \minimum 0.5
  56168        \maximum 1
  56169        \default 0.85
  56170        \note Gross air-side sensible heat ratio at the rated inlet air temperatures,
  56171        \note rated condenser inlet water temperature, rated air flow rate, and rated water flow rate.
  56172        \note Sensible heat ratio equals gross sensible cooling capacity divided by gross total cooling
  56173        \note capacity. Rated SHR (gross) should not include evaporator fan heat, only sensible cooling
  56174        \note and dehumidification by the coil alone.
  56175   N4 , \field Rated Evaporator Inlet Air Dry-Bulb Temperature
  56176        \type real
  56177        \units C
  56178        \minimum> 5
  56179        \default 19.7
  56180        \note Evaporator inlet air dry-bulb temperature corresponding to rated coil performance
  56181        \note (heating capacity, COP and SHR).
  56182   N5 , \field Rated Evaporator Inlet Air Wet-Bulb Temperature
  56183        \type real
  56184        \units C
  56185        \minimum> 5
  56186        \default 13.5
  56187        \note Evaporator inlet air wet-bulb temperature corresponding to rated coil performance
  56188        \note (heating capacity, COP and SHR).
  56189   N6 , \field Rated Condenser Inlet Water Temperature
  56190        \type real
  56191        \units C
  56192        \minimum> 25
  56193        \default 57.5
  56194        \note Condenser inlet water temperature corresponding to rated coil performance
  56195        \note (heating capacity, COP and SHR).
  56196   N7 , \field Rated Evaporator Air Flow Rate
  56197        \type real
  56198        \units m3/s
  56199        \minimum> 0
  56200        \autocalculatable
  56201        \note Evaporator air flow rate corresponding to rated coil performance
  56202        \note (heating capacity, COP and SHR).
  56203        \note Default is 5.035E-5 m3/s/W (31.25 cfm/MBH) of rated heating capacity when autocalculated.
  56204   N8 , \field Rated Condenser Water Flow Rate
  56205        \type real
  56206        \units m3/s
  56207        \ip-units gal/min
  56208        \minimum> 0
  56209        \autocalculatable
  56210        \note Condenser water flow rate corresponding to rated coil performance
  56211        \note (heating capacity, COP and SHR).
  56212        \note Default is 4.487E-8 m3/s/W (0.208 gpm/MBH) of rated heating capacity when autocalculated.
  56213        \note A warning message will be issued if the ratio of Rated Condenser Water Flow Rate
  56214        \note to Heating Capacity is less than 1.79405E-8 m3/s/W (0.083 gpm/MBH)
  56215        \note or greater than 8.97024E-8 m3/s/W (0.417 gpm/MBH), but the simulation will continue.
  56216   A2 , \field Evaporator Fan Power Included in Rated COP
  56217        \type choice
  56218        \key Yes
  56219        \key No
  56220        \default Yes
  56221        \note Select Yes if the evaporator fan power is included in the rated COP. This choice field
  56222        \note impacts the calculation of compressor electric power.
  56223   A3 , \field Condenser Pump Power Included in Rated COP
  56224        \type choice
  56225        \key Yes
  56226        \key No
  56227        \default No
  56228        \note Select Yes if the condenser pump power is included in the rated COP. This choice field
  56229        \note impacts the calculation of compressor electric power.
  56230   A4 , \field Condenser Pump Heat Included in Rated Heating Capacity and Rated COP
  56231        \type choice
  56232        \key Yes
  56233        \key No
  56234        \default No
  56235        \note Select Yes if the condenser pump heat is included in the rated heating capacity and
  56236        \note rated COP. This choice field impacts the calculation of water heating capacity.
  56237   N9 , \field Condenser Water Pump Power
  56238        \type real
  56239        \units W
  56240        \minimum 0
  56241        \default 0
  56242        \note A warning message will be issued if the ratio of Condenser Water Pump Power to Rated
  56243        \note Heating Capacity exceeds 0.1422 W/W (41.67 Watts/MBH), but the simulation will continue.
  56244   N10, \field Fraction of Condenser Pump Heat to Water
  56245        \type real
  56246        \minimum 0
  56247        \maximum 1
  56248        \default 0.2
  56249        \note Fraction of pump heat transferred to the condenser water. The pump is assumed
  56250        \note to be located downstream of the condenser.
  56251   A5 , \field Evaporator Air Inlet Node Name
  56252        \required-field
  56253        \type node
  56254        \note The node from which the DX coil draws its inlet air.
  56255   A6 , \field Evaporator Air Outlet Node Name
  56256        \required-field
  56257        \type node
  56258        \note The node to which the DX coil sends its outlet air.
  56259   A7 , \field Condenser Water Inlet Node Name
  56260        \required-field
  56261        \type node
  56262        \note The node from which the DX coil condenser draws its inlet water.
  56263        \note This name should match the source side outlet node name in the associated
  56264        \note water heater tank object.
  56265   A8 , \field Condenser Water Outlet Node Name
  56266        \required-field
  56267        \type node
  56268        \note The node to which the DX coil condenser sends its outlet water.
  56269        \note This name should match the source side inlet node name in the associated
  56270        \note water heater tank object.
  56271   N11, \field Crankcase Heater Capacity
  56272        \type real
  56273        \minimum 0
  56274        \default 0
  56275        \units W
  56276        \note The compressor crankcase heater only operates when the dry-bulb temperature of air
  56277        \note surrounding the compressor is below the Maximum Ambient Temperature for Crankcase
  56278        \note Heater Operation and the DX coil is off.  The ambient temperature surrounding the
  56279        \note compressor is set by the WaterHeater:HeatPump:PumpedCondenser parent object (field Compressor Location).
  56280   N12, \field Maximum Ambient Temperature for Crankcase Heater Operation
  56281        \type real
  56282        \minimum 0
  56283        \default 10
  56284        \units C
  56285        \note The compressor crankcase heater only operates when the dry-bulb temperature of air
  56286        \note surrounding the compressor is below the Maximum Outdoor Temperature for Crankcase
  56287        \note Heater Operation and the unit is off. The ambient temperature surrounding the
  56288        \note compressor is set by the WaterHeater:HeatPump:PumpedCondenser parent object (field Compressor Location).
  56289   A9 , \field Evaporator Air Temperature Type for Curve Objects
  56290        \type choice
  56291        \key DryBulbTemperature
  56292        \key WetBulbTemperature
  56293        \default WetBulbTemperature
  56294        \note Determines temperature type for heating capacity curves and
  56295        \note heating COP curves. This input determines whether
  56296        \note the inlet air dry-bulb or wet-bulb temperature is used to evaluate these curves.
  56297   A10, \field Heating Capacity Function of Temperature Curve Name
  56298        \type object-list
  56299        \object-list UnivariateFunctions
  56300        \object-list BivariateFunctions
  56301        \note Heating capacity modifier curve (function of temperature) should be biquadratic or cubic.
  56302        \note Biquadratic curve = a + b(ta) + c(ta)^2 + d(tw) + e(tw)^2 + f(ta)(tw).
  56303        \note Cubic curve = a + b(ta) + c(ta)^2 + d(ta)^3.
  56304        \note ta = evaporator inlet air [dry-bulb or wet-bulb] temperature (C).
  56305        \note tw = condenser inlet water temperature (C).
  56306        \note The field Evaporator Air Temperature Type for Curve Objects determines if dry-bulb or wet-bulb
  56307        \note is used as the evaporator inlet air temperature (ta).
  56308   A11, \field Heating Capacity Function of Air Flow Fraction Curve Name
  56309        \type object-list
  56310        \object-list UnivariateFunctions
  56311        \note Heating capacity modifier curve (function of air flow fraction) should be quadratic or cubic.
  56312        \note Quadratic curve = a + b(ff) + c(ff)^2.
  56313        \note Cubic curve = a + b(ff) + c(ff)^2 + d(ff)^3.
  56314        \note ff = fraction of the rated evaporator air flow rate.
  56315        \note Use curve coefficients of 1,0,0 or leave this field blank when neglecting performance impacts
  56316        \note due to variations in air flow rate fraction.
  56317   A12, \field Heating Capacity Function of Water Flow Fraction Curve Name
  56318        \type object-list
  56319        \object-list UnivariateFunctions
  56320        \note Heating capacity modifier curve (function of water flow fraction) should be quadratic or cubic.
  56321        \note Quadratic curve = a + b(ff) + c(ff)^2.
  56322        \note Cubic curve = a + b(ff) + c(ff)^2 + d(ff)^3.
  56323        \note ff = fraction of the rated condenser water flow rate.
  56324        \note Use curve coefficients of 1,0,0 or leave this field blank when neglecting performance impacts
  56325        \note due to variations in water flow rate fraction.
  56326   A13, \field Heating COP Function of Temperature Curve Name
  56327        \type object-list
  56328        \object-list UnivariateFunctions
  56329        \object-list BivariateFunctions
  56330        \note Heating COP modifier curve (function of temperature) should be biquadratic or cubic.
  56331        \note Biquadratic curve = a + b(ta) + c(ta)^2 + d(tw) + e(tw)^2 + f(ta)(tw).
  56332        \note Cubic curve = a + b(ta) + c(ta)^2 + d(ta)^3.
  56333        \note ta = evaporator inlet air [dry-bulb or wet-bulb] temperature (C).
  56334        \note tw = condenser inlet water temperature (C).
  56335        \note The field Evaporator Air Temperature Type for Curve Objects determines if dry-bulb or wet-bulb
  56336        \note is used as the evaporator inlet air temperature (ta).
  56337   A14, \field Heating COP Function of Air Flow Fraction Curve Name
  56338        \type object-list
  56339        \object-list UnivariateFunctions
  56340        \note Heating COP modifier curve (function of air flow fraction) should be quadratic or cubic.
  56341        \note Quadratic curve = a + b(ff) + c(ff)^2.
  56342        \note Cubic curve = a + b(ff) + c(ff)^2 + d(ff)^3.
  56343        \note ff = fraction of the rated evaporator air flow rate.
  56344        \note Use curve coefficients of 1,0,0 or leave this field blank when neglecting performance impacts
  56345        \note due to variations in air flow rate fraction.
  56346   A15, \field Heating COP Function of Water Flow Fraction Curve Name
  56347        \type object-list
  56348        \object-list UnivariateFunctions
  56349        \note Heating COP modifier curve (function of water flow fraction) should be quadratic or cubic.
  56350        \note Quadratic curve = a + b(ff) + c(ff)^2.
  56351        \note Cubic curve = a + b(ff) + c(ff)^2 + d(ff)^3.
  56352        \note ff = fraction of the rated condenser water flow rate.
  56353        \note Use curve coefficients of 1,0,0 or leave this field blank when neglecting performance impacts
  56354        \note due to variations in water flow rate fraction.
  56355   A16; \field Part Load Fraction Correlation Curve Name
  56356        \type object-list
  56357        \object-list UnivariateFunctions
  56358        \note Part Load Fraction Correlation (function of part load ratio) should be quadratic or cubic.
  56359        \note Quadratic curve = a + b(PLR) + c(PLR)^2.
  56360        \note Cubic curve = a + b(PLR) + c(PLR)^2 + d(PLR)^3.
  56361        \note PLR = part load ratio (heating delivered/steady state heating capacity).
  56362        \note Use curve coefficients of 1,0,0 or leave this field blank when neglecting performance impacts
  56363        \note due to variations in part load ratio.
  56364 
