  57486 Coil:WaterHeating:Desuperheater,
  57487        \memo Desuperheater air heating coil. The heating energy provided by this coil is reclaimed
  57488        \memo from the superheated refrigerant gas leaving a compressor and does not impact the
  57489        \memo performance of the compressor. This coil must be used with a water heater tank, see
  57490        \memo Water Heater:Mixed.
  57491        \min-fields 18
  57492   A1 , \field Name
  57493        \required-field
  57494        \type alpha
  57495        \note Unique name for this instance of a desuperheater water heating coil.
  57496   A2 , \field Availability Schedule Name
  57497        \note Availability schedule name for this system. Schedule value > 0 means the system is available.
  57498        \note If this field is blank, the system is always available.
  57499        \type object-list
  57500        \object-list ScheduleNames
  57501        \note Schedule values of 0 denote the desuperheater heating coil is off and the parasitic electric
  57502        \note energy is also off.
  57503   A3 , \field Setpoint Temperature Schedule Name
  57504        \required-field
  57505        \type object-list
  57506        \object-list ScheduleNames
  57507        \note Defines the cut-out temperature where the desuperheater water heating coil turns off.
  57508        \note The desuperheater heating coil setpoint temperature should always be greater
  57509        \note than the water tank's heater (element or burner) setpoint temperature. Temperature
  57510        \note schedule values should be in degrees C.
  57511   N1 , \field Dead Band Temperature Difference
  57512        \type real
  57513        \units deltaC
  57514        \minimum> 0
  57515        \maximum 20
  57516        \default 5
  57517        \note Setpoint temperature minus the dead band temperature difference defines
  57518        \note the cut-in temperature where the desuperheater water heating coil turns on.
  57519        \note The water tank's heater (element or burner) setpoint temperature
  57520        \note should always be less than the desuperheater heating coil cut-in temperature.
  57521   N2 , \field Rated Heat Reclaim Recovery Efficiency
  57522        \type real
  57523        \minimum> 0.0
  57524        \note Enter the fraction of waste heat reclaimed by the desuperheater water heating coil.
  57525   N3 , \field Rated Inlet Water Temperature
  57526        \required-field
  57527        \type real
  57528        \units C
  57529        \note The inlet water temperature corresponding to the rated heat reclaim recovery efficiency.
  57530   N4 , \field Rated Outdoor Air Temperature
  57531        \required-field
  57532        \type real
  57533        \units C
  57534        \note The outdoor air dry-bulb temperature corresponding to the
  57535        \note rated heat reclaim recovery efficiency.
  57536   N5 , \field Maximum Inlet Water Temperature for Heat Reclaim
  57537        \required-field
  57538        \type real
  57539        \units C
  57540        \note The desuperheater water heating coil is off when the inlet water temperature is above
  57541        \note the maximum inlet water temperature for heat reclaim.
  57542   A4 , \field Heat Reclaim Efficiency Function of Temperature Curve Name
  57543        \type object-list
  57544        \object-list BivariateFunctions
  57545        \note A biquadratic curve defining the performance of the desuperheater heating coil.
  57546        \note Performance can be specified as a function of inlet water temperature, outdoor air
  57547        \note dry-bulb temperature, or both.
  57548        \note Curve = a + b*Tw + c*Tw**2 + d*odb + e*odb**2 + f*Tw*odb.
  57549        \note Tw = desuperheater heating coil entering water temperature (C).
  57550        \note Odb = outdoor dry-bulb temperature at DX system condenser (C).
  57551   A5 , \field Water Inlet Node Name
  57552        \required-field
  57553        \type node
  57554        \note The node from which the desuperheater heating coil draws its inlet water.
  57555        \note This name should match the source side outlet node name in the associated
  57556        \note water heater tank object.
  57557   A6 , \field Water Outlet Node Name
  57558        \required-field
  57559        \type node
  57560        \note The node to which the desuperheater heating coil sends its outlet water.
  57561        \note This name should match the source side inlet node name in the associated
  57562        \note water heater tank object.
  57563   A7 , \field Tank Object Type
  57564        \type choice
  57565        \key WaterHeater:Mixed
  57566        \key WaterHeater:Stratified
  57567        \default WaterHeater:Mixed
  57568        \note Specify the type of water heater tank used by this desuperheater water heating coil.
  57569   A8 , \field Tank Name
  57570        \required-field
  57571        \type object-list
  57572        \note The name of the water heater tank used by this desuperheater water heating coil.
  57573        \note Needs to match the name used in the corresponding water heater object.
  57574        \object-list WaterHeaterMixedNames
  57575        \object-list WaterHeaterStratifiedNames
  57576   A9 , \field Heating Source Object Type
  57577        \required-field
  57578        \type choice
  57579        \key Coil:Cooling:DX:SingleSpeed
  57580        \key Coil:Cooling:DX:TwoSpeed
  57581        \key Coil:Cooling:DX:TwoStageWithHumidityControlMode
  57582        \key Coil:Cooling:DX:VariableSpeed
  57583        \key Coil:Cooling:DX:MultiSpeed
  57584        \key Coil:Cooling:WaterToAirHeatPump:EquationFit
  57585        \key Refrigeration:CompressorRack
  57586        \key Refrigeration:Condenser:AirCooled
  57587        \key Refrigeration:Condenser:EvaporativeCooled
  57588        \key Refrigeration:Condenser:WaterCooled
  57589        \note The type of DX system that is providing waste heat for reclaim.
  57590   A10, \field Heating Source Name
  57591        \required-field
  57592        \type object-list
  57593        \object-list DesuperHeatingCoilSources
  57594        \object-list DesuperHeatingWaterOnlySources
  57595        \note The name of the DX system used for heat reclaim.
  57596   N6 , \field Water Flow Rate
  57597        \required-field
  57598        \type real
  57599        \units m3/s
  57600        \ip-units gal/min
  57601        \minimum> 0
  57602        \note The operating water flow rate.
  57603   N7 , \field Water Pump Power
  57604        \type real
  57605        \units W
  57606        \ip-units W
  57607        \minimum 0.0
  57608        \default 0.0
  57609        \note The water circulation pump electric power.
  57610   N8 , \field Fraction of Pump Heat to Water
  57611        \type real
  57612        \minimum 0
  57613        \maximum 1
  57614        \default 0.2
  57615        \note The fraction of pump heat transferred to the water. The pump is assumed to be downstream of
  57616        \note the desuperheater water heating coil.
  57617   N9 , \field On-Cycle Parasitic Electric Load
  57618        \type real
  57619        \units W
  57620        \minimum 0
  57621        \default 0
  57622        \note Parasitic electric power consumed when the desuperheater water heating coil operates.
  57623        \note Parasitic electric load does not contribute to water heating or the zone air heat balance.
  57624        \ip-units W
  57625   N10; \field Off-Cycle Parasitic Electric Load
  57626        \type real
  57627        \units W
  57628        \minimum 0
  57629        \default 0
  57630        \note Parasitic electric load consumed when the desuperheater water heating coil is off.
  57631        \note Parasitic electric load does not contribute to water heating or the zone air heat balance.
  57632        \note Off-cycle parasitic power is 0 when the availability schedule is 0.
  57633        \ip-units W
  57634 
  57635 CoilSystem:Cooling:DX,
  57636         \memo Virtual container component that consists of a DX cooling coil and its associated
  57637         \memo controls. This control object supports several different types of DX cooling coils
  57638         \memo and may be placed directly in an air loop branch or outdoor air equipment list.
  57639         \min-fields 7
  57640    A1 , \field Name
  57641         \required-field
  57642         \reference CoolingCoilSystemName
  57643         \type alpha
  57644         \reference-class-name validBranchEquipmentTypes
  57645         \reference validBranchEquipmentNames
  57646         \reference-class-name validOASysEquipmentTypes
  57647         \reference validOASysEquipmentNames
  57648    A2 , \field Availability Schedule Name
  57649         \note Availability schedule name for this system. Schedule value > 0 means the system is available.
  57650         \note If this field is blank, the system is always available.
  57651         \type object-list
  57652         \object-list ScheduleNames
  57653    A3 , \field DX Cooling Coil System Inlet Node Name
  57654         \required-field
  57655         \type node
  57656    A4 , \field DX Cooling Coil System Outlet Node Name
  57657         \required-field
  57658         \type node
  57659    A5 , \field DX Cooling Coil System Sensor Node Name
  57660         \required-field
  57661         \type node
  57662    A6,  \field Cooling Coil Object Type
  57663         \type choice
  57664         \required-field
  57665         \key Coil:Cooling:DX:SingleSpeed
  57666         \key CoilSystem:Cooling:DX:HeatExchangerAssisted
  57667         \key Coil:Cooling:DX:TwoSpeed
  57668         \key Coil:Cooling:DX:TwoStageWithHumidityControlMode
  57669         \key Coil:Cooling:DX:VariableSpeed
  57670         \key Coil:Cooling:DX:SingleSpeed:ThermalStorage
  57671    A7,  \field Cooling Coil Name
  57672         \required-field
  57673         \type object-list
  57674         \object-list CoolingCoilsDX
  57675         \object-list CoolingCoilsDXVariableSpeed
  57676    A8,  \field Dehumidification Control Type
  57677         \type choice
  57678         \key None
  57679         \key Multimode
  57680         \key CoolReheat
  57681         \default None
  57682         \note None = meet sensible load only
  57683         \note Multimode = activate enhanced dehumidification mode
  57684         \note as needed and meet sensible load. If no sensible load
  57685         \note exists, and Run on Latent Load = Yes, and a latent
  57686         \note load exists, the unit will operate to meet the latent load.
  57687         \note Valid only with Coil:Cooling:DX:TwoStageWithHumidityControlMode
  57688         \note or CoilSystem:Cooling:DX:HeatExchangerAssisted.
  57689         \note CoolReheat = cool beyond the dry-bulb setpoint.
  57690         \note as required to meet the humidity setpoint.
  57691         \note Valid for all coil types.
  57692         \note For all dehumidification controls, the max
  57693         \note humidity setpoint on the Sensor Node is used.
  57694         \note SetpointManager:SingleZone:Humidity:Maximum,
  57695         \note SetpointManager:MultiZone:Humidity:Maximum, or
  57696         \note SetpointManager:MultiZone:MaximumHumidity:Average, and
  57697         \note SetpointManager:OutdoorAirPretreat (optional) objects.
  57698    A9,  \field Run on Sensible Load
  57699         \type choice
  57700         \key Yes
  57701         \key No
  57702         \default Yes
  57703         \note If Yes, unit will run if there is a sensible load.
  57704         \note If No, unit will not run if there is only a sensible load.
  57705         \note Dehumidification controls will be active if specified.
  57706   A10,  \field Run on Latent Load
  57707         \type choice
  57708         \key Yes
  57709         \key No
  57710         \default No
  57711         \note If Yes, unit will run if there is a latent load.
  57712         \note even if there is no sensible load.
  57713         \note If No, unit will not run only if there is a latent load.
  57714         \note Dehumidification controls will be active if specified.
  57715   A11,  \field Use Outdoor Air DX Cooling Coil
  57716         \type choice
  57717         \key Yes
  57718         \key No
  57719         \default No
  57720         \note This input field is designed for use with DX cooling coils with low air flow
  57721         \note to capacity ratio range (100 - 300 cfm/ton). Typical application is 100% dedicated
  57722         \note outdoor air system (DOAS). Other air loop or zone HVAC systems with low flow
  57723         \note to capacity ratio range may also use this input field.  If Yes, the DX cooling
  57724         \note coil runs as 100% DOAS DX coil or low flow to capacity ratio range.
  57725         \note If No, the DX cooling coil runs as a regular DX coil. If left blank the
  57726         \note default is regular DX coil.
  57727   N1 ;  \field Outdoor Air DX Cooling Coil Leaving Minimum Air Temperature
  57728         \type real
  57729         \units C
  57730         \minimum 0.0
  57731         \maximum 7.2
  57732         \default 2.0
  57733         \note DX cooling coil leaving minimum air temperature defines the minimum DX cooling coil
  57734         \note leaving air temperature that should be maintained to avoid frost formation. This input
  57735         \note field is optional and only used along with the input field above.
  57736 
