  59191 Humidifier:Steam:Gas,
  59192       \memo Natural gas fired steam humidifier with optional blower fan.
  59193   A1, \field Name
  59194       \required-field
  59195       \reference-class-name validBranchEquipmentTypes
  59196       \reference validBranchEquipmentNames
  59197       \reference-class-name validOASysEquipmentTypes
  59198       \reference validOASysEquipmentNames
  59199   A2, \field Availability Schedule Name
  59200       \note Availability schedule name for this system. Schedule value > 0 means the system is available.
  59201       \note If this field is blank, the system is always available.
  59202       \type object-list
  59203       \object-list ScheduleNames
  59204   N1, \field Rated Capacity
  59205       \note Capacity is m3/s of water at 5.05 C
  59206       \type real
  59207       \units m3/s
  59208       \minimum 0.0
  59209       \ip-units gal/min
  59210       \autosizable
  59211       \note The nominal full capacity water addition rate in m3/s of water at 5.05 C
  59212   N2, \field Rated Gas Use Rate
  59213       \type real
  59214       \units W
  59215       \minimum 0.0
  59216       \ip-units W
  59217       \autosizable
  59218       \note if auto-sized, the rated gas use rate is calculated from the rated
  59219       \note capacity and enthalpy rise of water from 20.0C to 100.0C steam and user
  59220       \note input thermal efficiency value specified in the next input field. If this
  59221       \note input field is hard-sized and Inlet Water Temperature Option input field is
  59222       \note selected as FixedInletWaterTemperature, then the thermal efficiency input
  59223       \note field will not be used or else if the Inlet Water Temperature Option input
  59224       \note field is selected as VariableInletWaterTemperature, then the thermal efficiency
  59225       \note input value is overridden by a value calculated from the capacity, rated gas use
  59226       \note rate and design condition.
  59227   N3, \field Thermal Efficiency
  59228       \type real
  59229       \units dimensionless
  59230       \minimum> 0.0
  59231       \maximum 1.0
  59232       \default 0.80
  59233       \note Based on the higher heating value of fuel.
  59234       \note If "Rated Gas Use Rate" in the field above is not auto-sized and the Inlet Water
  59235       \note Temperature Option input field is specified as FixedInletWaterTemperature, then the
  59236       \note thermal efficiency specified will not be used in the calculation, or else if the
  59237       \note Inlet Water Temperature Option input field is selected as VariableInletWaterTemperature,
  59238       \note then the thermal efficiency value is overridden by a value calculated from the capacity,
  59239       \note rated gas use rate and design condition.
  59240   A3, \field Thermal Efficiency Modifier Curve Name
  59241       \type object-list
  59242       \object-list UnivariateFunctions
  59243       \note Linear, Quadratic and Cubic efficiency curves are solely a function of PLR.
  59244       \note Linear = C1 + C2*PLR
  59245       \note Quadratic = C1 + C2*PLR + C3*PLR^2
  59246       \note Cubic = C1 + C2*PLR + C3*PLR^2 + C4*PLR^3
  59247       \note This is thermal efficiency modifier curve name of gas fired steam humidifier.
  59248       \note This curve is normalized, i.e., curve output value at rated condition is 1.0.
  59249   N4, \field Rated Fan Power
  59250       \type real
  59251       \units W
  59252       \minimum 0.0
  59253       \ip-units W
  59254       \note The nominal full capacity electric power input to the blower fan in Watts. If no
  59255       \note blower fan is required to inject the dry steam to the supply air stream, then
  59256       \note this input field is set to zero.
  59257   N5, \field Auxiliary Electric Power
  59258       \type real
  59259       \units W
  59260       \minimum 0.0
  59261       \ip-units W
  59262       \default 0.0
  59263       \note The auxiliary electric power input in watts. This amount of power will be consumed
  59264       \note whenever the unit is available (as defined by the availability schedule). This
  59265       \note electric power is used for control purpose only.
  59266   A4, \field Air Inlet Node Name
  59267       \type node
  59268   A5, \field Air Outlet Node Name
  59269       \type node
  59270   A6, \field Water Storage Tank Name
  59271       \type object-list
  59272       \object-list WaterStorageTankNames
  59273   A7; \field Inlet Water Temperature Option
  59274       \note The inlet water temperature can be fixed at 20C as it is done for electric steam
  59275       \note humidifier or it can be allowed to vary with temperature of the water source.
  59276       \note Currently allowed water sources are main water or water storage tank in water use objects.
  59277       \note if FixedInletWaterTemperature is specified, then a fixed 20C water temperature will be
  59278       \note used, or else if VariableInletWaterTemperature is specified, then inlet water will vary
  59279       \note depending the source water temperature. If this input field is left blank, then fixed
  59280       \note inlet water temperature of 20C will be assumed.
  59281       \type choice
  59282       \key FixedInletWaterTemperature
  59283       \key VariableInletWaterTemperature
  59284       \default FixedInletWaterTemperature
  59285 
  59286 Dehumidifier:Desiccant:NoFans,
  59287        \memo This object models a solid desiccant dehumidifier. The process
  59288        \memo air stream is the air which is dehumidified. The regeneration air
  59289        \memo stream is the air which is heated to regenerate the desiccant.
  59290        \memo This object determines the process air outlet conditions, the
  59291        \memo load on the regeneration heating coil, the electric power consumption
  59292        \memo for the wheel rotor motor, and the regeneration air fan mass flow rate.
  59293        \memo All other heat exchangers are modeled as separate objects connected
  59294        \memo to the inlet and outlet nodes of the dehumidifier. The solid
  59295        \memo desiccant dehumidifier is typically used in an AirLoopHVAC:OutdoorAirSystem,
  59296        \memo but can also be specified in any AirLoopHVAC.
  59297    A1, \field Name
  59298        \required-field
  59299        \reference-class-name validBranchEquipmentTypes
  59300        \reference validBranchEquipmentNames
  59301        \reference-class-name validOASysEquipmentTypes
  59302        \reference validOASysEquipmentNames
  59303    A2, \field Availability Schedule Name
  59304        \note Availability schedule name for this system. Schedule value > 0 means the system is available.
  59305        \note If this field is blank, the system is always available.
  59306        \type object-list
  59307        \object-list ScheduleNames
  59308    A3, \field Process Air Inlet Node Name
  59309        \note This is the node entering the process side of the desiccant wheel.
  59310        \type node
  59311    A4, \field Process Air Outlet Node Name
  59312        \note This is the node leaving the process side of the desiccant wheel.
  59313        \type node
  59314    A5, \field Regeneration Air Inlet Node Name
  59315        \note This is the node entering the regeneration side of the desiccant wheel
  59316        \note after the regeneration coil.
  59317        \type node
  59318    A6, \field Regeneration Fan Inlet Node Name
  59319        \note Node for air entering the regeneration fan, mass flow is set
  59320        \note by the desiccant dehumidifier module.
  59321        \type node
  59322    A7, \field Control Type
  59323        \note Type of setpoint control:
  59324        \note LeavingMaximumHumidityRatioSetpoint means that the unit is controlled
  59325        \note to deliver air at the Leaving Max Humidity Ratio Setpoint (see below),
  59326        \note SystemNodeMaximumHumidityRatioSetpoint means that the leaving humidity
  59327        \note ratio setpoint is the System Node Humidity Ratio Max property
  59328        \note of the Process Air Outlet Node.  A Setpoint
  59329        \note object must be used to control this setpoint.
  59330        \note Both control types use bypass dampers to prevent over drying.
  59331        \type choice
  59332        \key LeavingMaximumHumidityRatioSetpoint
  59333        \key SystemNodeMaximumHumidityRatioSetpoint
  59334    N1, \field Leaving Maximum Humidity Ratio Setpoint
  59335        \note Fixed setpoint for maximum process air leaving humidity ratio
  59336        \note Applicable only when Control Type = LeavingMaximumHumidityRatioSetpoint.
  59337        \type real
  59338        \units kgWater/kgDryAir
  59339    N2, \field Nominal Process Air Flow Rate
  59340        \note Process air flow rate at nominal conditions
  59341        \type real
  59342        \units m3/s
  59343        \minimum> 0.0
  59344    N3, \field Nominal Process Air Velocity
  59345        \note Process air velocity at nominal flow
  59346        \note When using Performance Model Type of Default, must be 2.032 to 4.064 m/s (400 to 800 fpm)
  59347        \type real
  59348        \units m/s
  59349        \minimum> 0.0
  59350        \maximum 6
  59351    N4, \field Rotor Power
  59352        \note Power input to wheel rotor motor
  59353        \type real
  59354        \units W
  59355        \minimum 0.0
  59356        \ip-units W
  59357    A8, \field Regeneration Coil Object Type
  59358        \note heating coil type
  59359        \type choice
  59360        \key Coil:Heating:Electric
  59361        \key Coil:Heating:Fuel
  59362        \key Coil:Heating:Water
  59363        \key Coil:Heating:Steam
  59364        \note works with gas, electric, hot water and steam heating coils
  59365    A9, \field Regeneration Coil Name
  59366        \note Name of heating coil object for regeneration air
  59367        \type object-list
  59368        \object-list HeatingCoilName
  59369   A10, \field Regeneration Fan Object Type
  59370        \note Type of fan object for regeneration air.  When using the Default
  59371        \note Performance Model Type (see below), only Fan:VariableVolume or Fan:SystemModel are valid.
  59372        \type choice
  59373        \key Fan:SystemModel
  59374        \key Fan:VariableVolume
  59375        \key Fan:ConstantVolume
  59376   A11, \field Regeneration Fan Name
  59377        \note Name of fan object for regeneration air
  59378        \type object-list
  59379        \object-list FansCVandVAV
  59380        \object-list FansSystemModel
  59381   A12, \field Performance Model Type
  59382        \note Specifies whether the default performance model or user-specified
  59383        \note curves should be used to model the performance.  The default model
  59384        \note is a generic solid desiccant wheel using performance curves of the form:
  59385        \note curve = C1 + C2*edb + C3*edb**2 + C4*ew + C5*ew**2 + C6*vel + C7*vel**2
  59386        \note + C8*edb*ew + C9*edb**2*ew**2 + C10*edb*vel + C11*edb**2*vel**2
  59387        \note + C12*ew*vel + C13*ew**2*vel**2 + C14*ALOG(edb) + C15*ALOG(ew) + C16*ALOG(vel)
  59388        \note   edb = process entering dry-bulb temperature [C]
  59389        \note   ew  = process entering humidity ratio [kgWater/kgDryAir]
  59390        \note   vel = process air velocity [m/s]
  59391        \note If UserCurves are specified, then performance is calculated as follows:
  59392        \note   Leaving Dry-Bulb = (Leaving Dry-Bulb fTW Curve) * (Leaving Dry-Bulb fV Curve)
  59393        \note   Leaving Humidity Ratio = (Leaving Humidity Ratio fTW Curve) * (Leaving Humidity Ratio fV Curve)
  59394        \note   Regen Energy = (Regen Energy fTW Curve) * (Regen Energy fV Curve)
  59395        \note   Regen Velocity = (Regen Velocity fTW Curve) * (Regen Velocity fV Curve)
  59396        \type choice
  59397        \key Default
  59398        \key UserCurves
  59399   A13, \field Leaving Dry-Bulb Function of Entering Dry-Bulb and Humidity Ratio Curve Name
  59400        \note Leaving dry-bulb of process air as a function of entering dry-bulb
  59401        \note and entering humidity ratio, biquadratic curve
  59402        \type object-list
  59403        \object-list BivariateFunctions
  59404        \note curve = C1 + C2*edb + C3*edb**2 + C4*ew + C5*ew**2 + C6*edb*ew
  59405        \note edb = process entering dry-bulb temperature [C]
  59406        \note ew  = process entering humidity ratio [kgWater/kgDryAir]
  59407   A14, \field Leaving Dry-Bulb Function of Air Velocity Curve Name
  59408        \note Leaving dry-bulb of process air as a function of air velocity,
  59409        \note quadratic curve.
  59410        \type object-list
  59411        \object-list UnivariateFunctions
  59412        \note curve = C1 + C2*v + C3*v**2
  59413        \note v = process air velocity [m/s]
  59414   A15, \field Leaving Humidity Ratio Function of Entering Dry-Bulb and Humidity Ratio Curve Name
  59415        \note Leaving humidity ratio of process air as a function of entering dry-bulb
  59416        \note and entering humidity ratio, biquadratic curve
  59417        \type object-list
  59418        \object-list BivariateFunctions
  59419        \note curve = C1 + C2*edb + C3*edb**2 + C4*ew + C5*ew**2 + C6*edb*ew
  59420        \note edb = process entering dry-bulb temperature [C]
  59421        \note ew  = process entering humidity ratio [kgWater/kgDryAir]
  59422   A16, \field Leaving Humidity Ratio Function of Air Velocity Curve Name
  59423        \note Leaving humidity ratio of process air as a function of
  59424        \note process air velocity, quadratic curve.
  59425        \type object-list
  59426        \object-list UnivariateFunctions
  59427        \note curve = C1 + C2*v + C3*v**2
  59428        \note v = process air velocity [m/s]
  59429   A17, \field Regeneration Energy Function of Entering Dry-Bulb and Humidity Ratio Curve Name
  59430        \note Regeneration energy [J/kg of water removed] as a function of
  59431        \note entering dry-bulb and entering humidity ratio, biquadratic curve
  59432        \type object-list
  59433        \object-list BivariateFunctions
  59434        \note curve = C1 + C2*edb + C3*edb**2 + C4*ew + C5*ew**2 + C6*edb*ew
  59435        \note edb = process entering dry-bulb temperature [C]
  59436        \note ew  = process entering humidity ratio [kgWater/kgDryAir]
  59437   A18, \field Regeneration Energy Function of Air Velocity Curve Name
  59438        \note Regeneration energy [J/kg of water removed] as a function of
  59439        \note process air velocity, quadratic curve.
  59440        \type object-list
  59441        \object-list UnivariateFunctions
  59442        \note curve = C1 + C2*v + C3*v**2
  59443        \note v = process air velocity [m/s]
  59444   A19, \field Regeneration Velocity Function of Entering Dry-Bulb and Humidity Ratio Curve Name
  59445        \note Regeneration velocity [m/s] as a function of
  59446        \note entering dry-bulb and entering humidity ratio, biquadratic curve
  59447        \type object-list
  59448        \object-list BivariateFunctions
  59449        \note curve = C1 + C2*edb + C3*edb**2 + C4*ew + C5*ew**2 + C6*edb*ew
  59450        \note edb = process entering dry-bulb temperature [C]
  59451        \note ew  = process entering humidity ratio [kgWater/kgDryAir]
  59452   A20, \field Regeneration Velocity Function of Air Velocity Curve Name
  59453        \note Regeneration velocity [m/s] as a function of
  59454        \note process air velocity, quadratic curve.
  59455        \type object-list
  59456        \object-list UnivariateFunctions
  59457        \note curve = C1 + C2*v + C3*v**2
  59458        \note v = process air velocity [m/s]
  59459    N5; \field Nominal Regeneration Temperature
  59460        \note Nominal regen temperature upon which the regen energy modifier
  59461        \note  curve is based.  Not used if Default if chosen for the field Performance Mode Type.
  59462        \note 121 C is a commonly used value.
  59463        \type real
  59464        \units C
  59465        \minimum 40
  59466        \maximum 250
