  60093 \group Unitary Equipment
  60094 
  60095 AirLoopHVAC:UnitarySystem,
  60096        \memo AirloopHVAC:UnitarySystem is a generic HVAC system type that allows any
  60097        \memo configuration of coils and/or fan. This object is a replacement of other
  60098        \memo AirloopHVAC objects. This object can be used in outdoor air systems,
  60099        \memo outdoor air units, air loops, and as zone equipment if desired.
  60100        \min-fields 14
  60101   A1,  \field Name
  60102        \required-field
  60103        \type alpha
  60104        \reference DOAToZonalUnit
  60105        \note Unique name for the Unitary System.
  60106        \reference-class-name validBranchEquipmentTypes
  60107        \reference validBranchEquipmentNames
  60108        \reference-class-name validOASysEquipmentTypes
  60109        \reference validOASysEquipmentNames
  60110        \reference ZoneEquipmentNames
  60111   A2,  \field Control Type
  60112        \type choice
  60113        \key Load
  60114        \key SetPoint
  60115        \key SingleZoneVAV
  60116        \default Load
  60117        \note Load control requires a Controlling Zone name.
  60118        \note SetPoint control requires set points at coil outlet node.
  60119        \note SingleZoneVAV also requires a Controlling Zone name and allows
  60120        \note load control at low speed fan until the load exceeds capacity
  60121        \note or outlet air temperature limits. The fan speed is then increased.
  60122   A3,  \field Controlling Zone or Thermostat Location
  60123        \note Used only for Load based control
  60124        \type object-list
  60125        \object-list ZoneNames
  60126        \note Zone name where thermostat is located. Required when Control Type = Load.
  60127   A4,  \field Dehumidification Control Type
  60128        \type choice
  60129        \key None
  60130        \key Multimode
  60131        \key CoolReheat
  60132        \default None
  60133        \note None = meet sensible load only. Required when Control Type = SingleZoneVAV.
  60134        \note Multimode = activate enhanced dehumidification mode
  60135        \note as needed and meet sensible load.  Valid only with
  60136        \note cooling coil type Coil:Cooling:DX:TwoStageWithHumidityControlMode or CoilSystem:Cooling:DX:HeatExchangerAssisted.
  60137        \note This control mode either switches the coil mode or allows the heat exchanger to be turned
  60138        \note on and off based on the zone dehumidification requirements.
  60139        \note A ZoneControl:Humidistat object is also required.
  60140        \note CoolReheat = cool beyond the dry-bulb setpoint.
  60141        \note as required to meet the humidity setpoint.  Valid with all
  60142        \note cooling coil types. When a heat exchanger assisted cooling
  60143        \note coil is used, the heat exchanger is locked on at all times.
  60144        \note A ZoneControl:Humidistat object is also required.
  60145   A5,  \field Availability Schedule Name
  60146        \type object-list
  60147        \object-list ScheduleNames
  60148        \note Availability schedule name for this system. Schedule value > 0 means the system is available.
  60149        \note If this field is blank, the system is always available.
  60150        \note A schedule value greater than zero (usually 1 is used) indicates that the unit is
  60151        \note available to operate as needed. A value less than or equal to zero (usually zero
  60152        \note is used) denotes that the unit must be off.
  60153   A6,  \field Air Inlet Node Name
  60154        \required-field
  60155        \type node
  60156        \note Enter the node name used as the inlet air node for the unitary system.
  60157   A7,  \field Air Outlet Node Name
  60158        \required-field
  60159        \type node
  60160        \note Enter the node name used as the outlet air node for the unitary system.
  60161   A8, \field Supply Fan Object Type
  60162        \type choice
  60163        \key Fan:SystemModel
  60164        \key Fan:OnOff
  60165        \key Fan:ConstantVolume
  60166        \key Fan:VariableVolume
  60167        \key Fan:ComponentModel
  60168        \note Enter the type of supply air fan if included in the unitary system.
  60169        \note Fan:ConstantVolume only works with continuous fan operating mode (i.e. supply
  60170        \note air fan operating mode schedule values greater than 0).
  60171        \note Specify a Fan:SystemModel or a Fan:OnOff object when the Supply Air Fan Operating Mode Schedule Name
  60172        \note input field above is left blank.
  60173        \note Specify a Fan:SystemModel or a Fan:VariableVolume when modeling VAV systems which used setpoint based control
  60174        \note if the fan is included in the unitary system object.
  60175        \note The ComponentModel fan type may be substituted for the ConstantVolume or VariableVolume
  60176        \note fan types when more detailed fan modeling is required.
  60177        \note The variable or constant volume fan may be specified on the branch instead of contained
  60178        \note within the unitary system object (i.e., this field may be blank for certain configurations).
  60179   A9, \field Supply Fan Name
  60180        \type object-list
  60181        \object-list Fans
  60182        \note Enter the name of the supply air fan if included in the unitary system.
  60183   A10, \field Fan Placement
  60184        \type choice
  60185        \key BlowThrough
  60186        \key DrawThrough
  60187        \note Enter the type of supply air fan if included in the unitary system.
  60188   A11, \field Supply Air Fan Operating Mode Schedule Name
  60189        \type object-list
  60190        \object-list ScheduleNames
  60191        \note A fan operating mode schedule value of 0 indicates cycling fan mode (supply air
  60192        \note fan cycles on and off in tandem with the cooling or heating coil).
  60193        \note Any other schedule value indicates continuous fan mode (supply air fan operates
  60194        \note continuously regardless of cooling or heating coil operation). Provide a schedule
  60195        \note with non-zero values when high humidity control is specified.
  60196        \note Leaving this schedule name blank will default to constant fan mode for the
  60197        \note entire simulation period.
  60198        \note This field is not used when set point based control is used where a set point
  60199        \note controls the coil.
  60200        \note SingleZoneVAV control type is only active when constant fan operating mode is active.
  60201   A12, \field Heating Coil Object Type
  60202        \type choice
  60203        \key Coil:Heating:DX:SingleSpeed
  60204        \key Coil:Heating:DX:MultiSpeed
  60205        \key Coil:Heating:DX:VariableSpeed
  60206        \key Coil:Heating:WaterToAirHeatPump:ParameterEstimation
  60207        \key Coil:Heating:WaterToAirHeatPump:EquationFit
  60208        \key Coil:Heating:WaterToAirHeatPump:VariableSpeedEquationFit
  60209        \key Coil:Heating:Fuel
  60210        \key Coil:Heating:Gas:MultiStage
  60211        \key Coil:Heating:Electric
  60212        \key Coil:Heating:Electric:MultiStage
  60213        \key Coil:Heating:Water
  60214        \key Coil:Heating:Steam
  60215        \key Coil:Heating:Desuperheater
  60216        \key Coil:UserDefined
  60217        \note Enter the type of heating coil if included in the unitary system.
  60218   A13, \field Heating Coil Name
  60219        \type object-list
  60220        \object-list HeatingCoilsDX
  60221        \object-list HeatingCoilsDXMultiSpeed
  60222        \object-list HeatingCoilsDXVariableSpeed
  60223        \object-list HeatingCoilsWaterToAirHP
  60224        \object-list HeatingCoilsWaterToAirVSHP
  60225        \object-list HeatingCoilName
  60226        \object-list HeatingCoilsElectricMultiStage
  60227        \object-list HeatingCoilsGasMultiStage
  60228        \object-list HeatingCoilsDesuperheater
  60229        \object-list UserDefinedCoil
  60230        \note Enter the name of the heating coil if included in the unitary system.
  60231   N1 , \field DX Heating Coil Sizing Ratio
  60232        \type real
  60233        \default 1.0
  60234        \minimum> 0
  60235        \note Used to adjust heat pump heating capacity with respect to DX cooling capacity
  60236        \note used only for heat pump configurations (i.e., a DX cooling and DX heating coil is used).
  60237   A14, \field Cooling Coil Object Type
  60238        \type choice
  60239        \key Coil:Cooling:DX
  60240        \key Coil:Cooling:DX:SingleSpeed
  60241        \key Coil:Cooling:DX:TwoSpeed
  60242        \key Coil:Cooling:DX:MultiSpeed
  60243        \key Coil:Cooling:DX:VariableSpeed
  60244        \key Coil:Cooling:DX:TwoStageWithHumidityControlMode
  60245        \key Coil:Cooling:DX:SingleSpeed:ThermalStorage
  60246        \key CoilSystem:Cooling:DX:HeatExchangerAssisted
  60247        \key Coil:Cooling:WaterToAirHeatPump:ParameterEstimation
  60248        \key Coil:Cooling:WaterToAirHeatPump:EquationFit
  60249        \key Coil:Cooling:WaterToAirHeatPump:VariableSpeedEquationFit
  60250        \key Coil:Cooling:Water
  60251        \key Coil:Cooling:Water:DetailedGeometry
  60252        \key CoilSystem:Cooling:Water:HeatExchangerAssisted
  60253        \key Coil:UserDefined
  60254        \note Enter the type of cooling coil if included in the unitary system.
  60255   A15, \field Cooling Coil Name
  60256        \type object-list
  60257        \object-list CoilCoolingDX
  60258        \object-list CoolingCoilsDX
  60259        \object-list CoolingCoilsDXMultiSpeed
  60260        \object-list CoolingCoilsDXVariableSpeed
  60261        \object-list CoolingCoilsWaterToAirHP
  60262        \object-list CoolingCoilsWaterToAirVSHP
  60263        \object-list CoolingCoilsWater
  60264        \object-list UserDefinedCoil
  60265        \note Enter the name of the cooling coil if included in the unitary system.
  60266   A16, \field Use DOAS DX Cooling Coil
  60267        \type choice
  60268        \key Yes
  60269        \key No
  60270        \default No
  60271        \note If Yes, the DX cooling coil runs as 100% DOAS DX coil.
  60272        \note If No, the DX cooling coil runs as a regular DX coil.
  60273        \note If left blank the default is regular dx coil.
  60274   N2 , \field Minimum Supply Air Temperature
  60275        \type real
  60276        \units C
  60277        \minimum 0.0
  60278        \maximum 20.0
  60279        \default 2.0
  60280        \autosizable
  60281        \note When Use DOAS DX Cooling Coil is specified as Yes, Minimum Supply Air Temperature
  60282        \note defines the minimum DOAS DX cooling coil leaving air temperature that should
  60283        \note be maintained to avoid frost formation. This field is not autosizable when
  60284        \note the input for Use DOAS DX Cooling Coil = Yes.
  60285        \note When Control Type = SingleZoneVAV, enter the minimum air temperature limit for reduced fan speed.
  60286   A17, \field Latent Load Control
  60287        \type choice
  60288        \key SensibleOnlyLoadControl
  60289        \key LatentOnlyLoadControl
  60290        \key LatentWithSensibleLoadControl
  60291        \key LatentOrSensibleLoadControl
  60292        \default SensibleOnlyLoadControl
  60293        \note SensibleOnlyLoadControl is selected when thermostat or SingleZoneVAV control is used.
  60294        \note LatentOnlyLoadControl is selected when humidistat control is used.
  60295        \note LatentWithSensibleLoadControl is selected when thermostat control is used and
  60296        \note dehumidification is required only when a sensible load exists.
  60297        \note LatentOrSensibleLoadControl is selected when thermostat control is used and
  60298        \note dehumidification is required any time the humidistat set point is exceeded.
  60299   A18, \field Supplemental Heating Coil Object Type
  60300        \type choice
  60301        \key Coil:Heating:Fuel
  60302        \key Coil:Heating:Electric
  60303        \key Coil:Heating:Desuperheater
  60304        \key Coil:Heating:Water
  60305        \key Coil:Heating:Steam
  60306        \key Coil:UserDefined
  60307        \note Enter the type of supplemental heating or reheat coil if included in the unitary system.
  60308        \note Only required if dehumidification control type is "CoolReheat".
  60309        \note This coil supplements heating mode operation or reheats the supply air during dehumidification
  60310        \note mode operation. If set point based control is used the coils operate to meet their respective
  60311        \note supply air temperature set point.
  60312   A19, \field Supplemental Heating Coil Name
  60313        \type object-list
  60314        \object-list HeatingCoilName
  60315        \object-list HeatingCoilsDesuperheater
  60316        \object-list UserDefinedCoil
  60317        \note Enter the name of the supplemental heating coil if included in the unitary system.
  60318        \note Only required if dehumidification control type is "CoolReheat".
  60319   A20, \field Cooling Supply Air Flow Rate Method
  60320        \type choice
  60321        \key None
  60322        \key SupplyAirFlowRate
  60323        \key FlowPerFloorArea
  60324        \key FractionOfAutosizedCoolingValue
  60325        \key FlowPerCoolingCapacity
  60326        \note Enter the method used to determine the cooling supply air volume flow rate.
  60327        \note None is used when a cooling coil is not included in the unitary system or this field may be blank.
  60328        \note SupplyAirFlowRate is selected when the magnitude of the supply air volume is used.
  60329        \note FlowPerFloorArea is selected when the supply air volume flow rate is based on total floor area
  60330        \note served by the unitary system.
  60331        \note FractionOfAutosizedCoolingValue is selected when the supply air volume is a fraction of the
  60332        \note value determined by the simulation.
  60333        \note FlowPerCoolingCapacity is selected when the supply air volume is a fraction of the cooling
  60334        \note capacity as determined by the simulation.
  60335   N3 , \field Cooling Supply Air Flow Rate
  60336        \type real
  60337        \units m3/s
  60338        \minimum 0.0
  60339        \autosizable
  60340        \note Enter the magnitude of the supply air volume flow rate during cooling operation.
  60341        \note Required field when Cooling Supply Air Flow Rate Method is SupplyAirFlowRate.
  60342        \note This field may be blank if a cooling coil is not included in the unitary system.
  60343   N4 , \field Cooling Supply Air Flow Rate Per Floor Area
  60344        \type real
  60345        \units m3/s-m2
  60346        \minimum 0.0
  60347        \note Enter the supply air volume flow rate per total floor area fraction.
  60348        \note Required field when Cooling Supply Air Flow Rate Method is FlowPerFloorArea.
  60349        \note This field may be blank if a cooling coil is not included in the unitary system.
  60350   N5 , \field Cooling Fraction of Autosized Cooling Supply Air Flow Rate
  60351        \type real
  60352        \minimum 0.0
  60353        \note Enter the supply air volume flow rate as a fraction of the cooling supply air flow rate.
  60354        \note Required field when Cooling Supply Air Flow Rate Method is FractionOfAutosizedCoolingValue.
  60355        \note This field may be blank if a cooling coil is not included in the unitary system.
  60356   N6 , \field Cooling Supply Air Flow Rate Per Unit of Capacity
  60357        \type real
  60358        \units m3/s-W
  60359        \minimum 0.0
  60360        \note Enter the supply air volume flow rate as a fraction of the cooling capacity.
  60361        \note Required field when Cooling Supply Air Flow Rate Method is FlowPerCoolingCapacity.
  60362        \note This field may be blank if a cooling coil is not included in the unitary system.
  60363   A21, \field Heating Supply Air Flow Rate Method
  60364        \type choice
  60365        \key None
  60366        \key SupplyAirFlowRate
  60367        \key FlowPerFloorArea
  60368        \key FractionOfAutosizedHeatingValue
  60369        \key FlowPerHeatingCapacity
  60370        \note Enter the method used to determine the heating supply air volume flow rate.
  60371        \note None is used when a heating coil is not included in the unitary system or this field may be blank.
  60372        \note SupplyAirFlowRate is selected when the magnitude of the supply air volume is used.
  60373        \note FlowPerFloorArea is selected when the supply air volume flow rate is based on total floor area
  60374        \note served by the unitary system.
  60375        \note FractionOfAutosizedHeatingValue is selected when the supply air volume is a fraction of the
  60376        \note value determined by the simulation.
  60377        \note FlowPerHeatingCapacity is selected when the supply air volume is a fraction of the heating
  60378        \note capacity as determined by the simulation.
  60379   N7 , \field Heating Supply Air Flow Rate
  60380        \type real
  60381        \units m3/s
  60382        \minimum 0.0
  60383        \autosizable
  60384        \note Enter the magnitude of the supply air volume flow rate during heating operation.
  60385        \note Required field when Heating Supply Air Flow Rate Method is SupplyAirFlowRate.
  60386        \note This field may be blank if a heating coil is not included in the unitary system.
  60387   N8 , \field Heating Supply Air Flow Rate Per Floor Area
  60388        \type real
  60389        \units m3/s-m2
  60390        \minimum 0.0
  60391        \note Enter the supply air volume flow rate per total floor area fraction.
  60392        \note Required field when Heating Supply Air Flow Rate Method is FlowPerFloorArea.
  60393        \note This field may be blank if a heating coil is not included in the unitary system.
  60394   N9 , \field Heating Fraction of Autosized Heating Supply Air Flow Rate
  60395        \type real
  60396        \minimum 0.0
  60397        \note Enter the supply air volume flow rate as a fraction of the heating supply air flow rate.
  60398        \note Required field when Heating Supply Air Flow Rate Method is FractionOfAutosizedHeatingValue.
  60399        \note This field may be blank if a heating coil is not included in the unitary system.
  60400   N10, \field Heating Supply Air Flow Rate Per Unit of Capacity
  60401        \type real
  60402        \units m3/s-W
  60403        \minimum 0.0
  60404        \note Enter the supply air volume flow rate as a fraction of the heating capacity.
  60405        \note Required field when Heating Supply Air Flow Rate Method is FlowPerHeatingCapacity.
  60406        \note This field may be blank if a heating coil is not included in the unitary system.
  60407   A22, \field No Load Supply Air Flow Rate Method
  60408        \type choice
  60409        \key None
  60410        \key SupplyAirFlowRate
  60411        \key FlowPerFloorArea
  60412        \key FractionOfAutosizedCoolingValue
  60413        \key FractionOfAutosizedHeatingValue
  60414        \key FlowPerCoolingCapacity
  60415        \key FlowPerHeatingCapacity
  60416        \note Enter the method used to determine the supply air volume flow rate when no cooling or heating is required.
  60417        \note None is used when a cooling and heating coil is not included in the unitary system or this field may be blank.
  60418        \note SupplyAirFlowRate is selected when the magnitude of the supply air volume is used.
  60419        \note FlowPerFloorArea is selected when the supply air volume flow rate is based on total floor area
  60420        \note served by the unitary system.
  60421        \note FractionOfAutosizedCoolingValue is selected when the supply air volume is a fraction of the
  60422        \note cooling value determined by the simulation.
  60423        \note FractionOfAutosizedHeatingValue is selected when the supply air volume is a fraction of the
  60424        \note heating value determined by the simulation.
  60425        \note FlowPerCoolingCapacity is selected when the supply air volume is a fraction of the cooling
  60426        \note capacity as determined by the simulation.
  60427        \note FlowPerHeatingCapacity is selected when the supply air volume is a fraction of the heating
  60428        \note capacity as determined by the simulation.
  60429   N11, \field No Load Supply Air Flow Rate
  60430        \type real
  60431        \units m3/s
  60432        \minimum 0.0
  60433        \autosizable
  60434        \note Enter the magnitude of the supply air volume flow rate during when no cooling or heating is required.
  60435        \note Required field when No Load Supply Air Flow Rate Method is SupplyAirFlowRate.
  60436   N12, \field No Load Supply Air Flow Rate Per Floor Area
  60437        \type real
  60438        \units m3/s-m2
  60439        \minimum 0.0
  60440        \note Enter the supply air volume flow rate per total floor area fraction.
  60441        \note Required field when No Load Supply Air Flow Rate Method is FlowPerFloorArea.
  60442   N13, \field No Load Fraction of Autosized Cooling Supply Air Flow Rate
  60443        \type real
  60444        \minimum 0.0
  60445        \note Enter the supply air volume flow rate as a fraction of the cooling supply air flow rate.
  60446        \note Required field when No Load Supply Air Flow Rate Method is FractionOfAutosizedCoolingValue.
  60447   N14, \field No Load Fraction of Autosized Heating Supply Air Flow Rate
  60448        \type real
  60449        \minimum 0.0
  60450        \note Enter the supply air volume flow rate as a fraction of the heating supply air flow rate.
  60451        \note Required field when No Load Supply Air Flow Rate Method is FractionOfAutosizedHeatingValue.
  60452   N15, \field No Load Supply Air Flow Rate Per Unit of Capacity During Cooling Operation
  60453        \type real
  60454        \units m3/s-W
  60455        \minimum 0.0
  60456        \note Enter the supply air volume flow rate as a fraction of the cooling capacity.
  60457        \note Required field when No Load Supply Air Flow Rate Method is FlowPerCoolingCapacity.
  60458   N16, \field No Load Supply Air Flow Rate Per Unit of Capacity During Heating Operation
  60459        \type real
  60460        \units m3/s-W
  60461        \minimum 0.0
  60462        \note Enter the supply air volume flow rate as a fraction of the heating capacity.
  60463        \note Required field when No Load Supply Air Flow Rate Method is FlowPerHeatingCapacity.
  60464   N17, \field Maximum Supply Air Temperature
  60465        \type real
  60466        \units C
  60467        \autosizable
  60468        \default 80.0
  60469        \note Enter the maximum supply air temperature leaving the heating coil.
  60470        \note When Control Type = SingleZoneVAV, enter the maximum air temperature limit for reduced fan speed.
  60471   N18, \field Maximum Outdoor Dry-Bulb Temperature for Supplemental Heater Operation
  60472        \type real
  60473        \units C
  60474        \default 21.0
  60475        \note Enter the maximum outdoor dry-bulb temperature for supplemental heater operation.
  60476   A23, \field Outdoor Dry-Bulb Temperature Sensor Node Name
  60477        \type node
  60478        \note If this field is blank, outdoor temperature from the weather file is used.
  60479        \note If this field is not blank, the node name specified determines the outdoor temperature used
  60480        \note for controlling supplemental heater operation.
  60481   N19, \field Maximum Cycling Rate
  60482        \type real
  60483        \units cycles/hr
  60484        \minimum 0.0
  60485        \maximum 5.0
  60486        \default 2.5
  60487        \note Used only for water source heat pump.
  60488        \note The maximum on-off cycling rate for the compressor.
  60489        \note Suggested value is 2.5 for a typical heat pump.
  60490   N20, \field Heat Pump Time Constant
  60491        \type real
  60492        \units s
  60493        \minimum 0.0
  60494        \maximum 500.0
  60495        \default 60.0
  60496        \note Used only for water source heat pump.
  60497        \note Time constant for the cooling coil's capacity to reach steady state after startup.
  60498        \note Suggested value is 60 for a typical heat pump.
  60499   N21, \field Fraction of On-Cycle Power Use
  60500        \type real
  60501        \minimum 0.0
  60502        \maximum 0.05
  60503        \default 0.01
  60504        \note Used only for water source heat pump.
  60505        \note The fraction of on-cycle power use to adjust the part load fraction based on
  60506        \note the off-cycle power consumption due to crankcase heaters, controls, fans, and etc.
  60507        \note Suggested value is 0.01 for a typical heat pump.
  60508   N22, \field Heat Pump Fan Delay Time
  60509        \type real
  60510        \units s
  60511        \minimum 0.0
  60512        \default 60
  60513        \note Used only for water source heat pump.
  60514        \note Programmed time delay for heat pump fan to shut off after compressor cycle off.
  60515        \note Only required when fan operating mode is cycling.
  60516        \note Enter 0 when fan operating mode is continuous.
  60517   N23, \field Ancillary On-Cycle Electric Power
  60518        \type real
  60519        \units W
  60520        \minimum 0
  60521        \default 0
  60522        \note Enter the value of ancillary electric power for controls or other devices consumed during the on cycle.
  60523   N24, \field Ancillary Off-Cycle Electric Power
  60524        \type real
  60525        \units W
  60526        \minimum 0
  60527        \default 0
  60528        \note Enter the value of ancillary electric power for controls or other devices consumed during the off cycle.
  60529   N25, \field Design Heat Recovery Water Flow Rate
  60530        \type real
  60531        \units m3/s
  60532        \ip-units gal/min
  60533        \minimum 0.0
  60534        \default 0.0
  60535        \note If non-zero, then the heat recovery inlet and outlet node names must be entered.
  60536        \note Used for heat recovery to an EnergyPlus plant loop.
  60537   N26, \field Maximum Temperature for Heat Recovery
  60538        \type real
  60539        \units C
  60540        \maximum 100.0
  60541        \minimum 0.0
  60542        \default 80.0
  60543        \note Enter the maximum heat recovery inlet temperature allowed for heat recovery.
  60544   A24, \field Heat Recovery Water Inlet Node Name
  60545        \type node
  60546        \note Enter the name of the heat recovery water inlet node if plant water loop connections are present.
  60547   A25, \field Heat Recovery Water Outlet Node Name
  60548        \type node
  60549        \note Enter the name of the heat recovery water outlet node if plant water loop connections are present.
  60550   A26, \field Design Specification Multispeed Object Type
  60551        \type choice
  60552        \key UnitarySystemPerformance:Multispeed
  60553        \note Enter the type of performance specification object used to describe the multispeed coil.
