  60761 AirLoopHVAC:Unitary:Furnace:HeatOnly,
  60762         \memo Unitary system, heating-only with constant volume supply fan (continuous or cycling)
  60763         \memo and heating coil (gas, electric, hot water, or steam). Identical to
  60764         \memo AirLoopHVAC:UnitaryHeatOnly.
  60765         \min-fields 13
  60766    A1,  \field Name
  60767         \required-field
  60768         \type alpha
  60769         \reference-class-name validBranchEquipmentTypes
  60770         \reference validBranchEquipmentNames
  60771    A2,  \field Availability Schedule Name
  60772         \note Availability schedule name for this system. Schedule value > 0 means the system is available.
  60773         \note If this field is blank, the system is always available.
  60774         \type object-list
  60775         \object-list ScheduleNames
  60776    A3,  \field Furnace Air Inlet Node Name
  60777         \required-field
  60778         \type node
  60779    A4,  \field Furnace Air Outlet Node Name
  60780         \required-field
  60781         \type node
  60782    A5,  \field Supply Air Fan Operating Mode Schedule Name
  60783         \type object-list
  60784         \object-list ScheduleNames
  60785         \note A fan operating mode schedule value of 0 indicates cycling fan mode (supply air
  60786         \note fan cycles on and off in tandem with the heating coil).
  60787         \note Any other schedule value indicates continuous fan mode (supply air fan operates
  60788         \note continuously regardless of heating coil operation).
  60789         \note Leaving this schedule name blank will default to cycling fan mode for the
  60790         \note entire simulation period.
  60791    N1,  \field Maximum Supply Air Temperature
  60792         \type real
  60793         \units C
  60794         \autosizable
  60795         \default 80.0
  60796    N2,  \field Heating Supply Air Flow Rate
  60797         \required-field
  60798         \type real
  60799         \note  This value should be > 0 and <= than the fan air flow rate.
  60800         \units m3/s
  60801         \minimum> 0.0
  60802         \autosizable
  60803    A6,  \field Controlling Zone or Thermostat Location
  60804         \required-field
  60805         \type object-list
  60806         \object-list ZoneNames
  60807    A7,  \field Supply Fan Object Type
  60808         \required-field
  60809         \type choice
  60810         \key Fan:OnOff
  60811         \key Fan:ConstantVolume
  60812         \note Fan:ConstantVolume only works with continuous fan operating mode (i.e. fan
  60813         \note operating mode schedule values are greater than 0).
  60814    A8,  \field Supply Fan Name
  60815         \required-field
  60816         \type object-list
  60817         \object-list FansCVandOnOff
  60818    A9 , \field Fan Placement
  60819         \type choice
  60820         \key BlowThrough
  60821         \key DrawThrough
  60822         \default BlowThrough
  60823    A10, \field Heating Coil Object Type
  60824         \required-field
  60825         \type choice
  60826         \key Coil:Heating:Fuel
  60827         \key Coil:Heating:Electric
  60828         \key Coil:Heating:Water
  60829         \key Coil:Heating:Steam
  60830         \note works with gas, electric, hot water and steam heating coils
  60831    A11; \field Heating Coil Name
  60832         \required-field
  60833         \type object-list
  60834         \object-list HeatingCoilName
  60835 
  60836 AirLoopHVAC:Unitary:Furnace:HeatCool,
  60837         \memo Unitary system, heating and cooling with constant volume supply fan (continuous or
  60838         \memo cycling), direct expansion (DX) cooling coil, heating coil (gas, electric,
  60839         \memo hot water, or steam), and optional reheat coil for dehumidification control.
  60840         \memo Identical to AirLoopHVAC:UnitaryHeatCool.
  60841         \min-fields 17
  60842    A1,  \field Name
  60843         \required-field
  60844         \type alpha
  60845         \reference-class-name validBranchEquipmentTypes
  60846         \reference validBranchEquipmentNames
  60847    A2,  \field Availability Schedule Name
  60848         \note Availability schedule name for this system. Schedule value > 0 means the system is available.
  60849         \note If this field is blank, the system is always available.
  60850         \type object-list
  60851         \object-list ScheduleNames
  60852         \note A schedule value greater than zero (usually 1 is used) indicates that the unit is
  60853         \note available to operate as needed. A value less than or equal to zero (usually zero
  60854         \note is used) denotes that the unit must be off.
  60855    A3,  \field Furnace Air Inlet Node Name
  60856         \required-field
  60857         \type node
  60858    A4,  \field Furnace Air Outlet Node Name
  60859         \required-field
  60860         \type node
  60861    A5,  \field Supply Air Fan Operating Mode Schedule Name
  60862         \type object-list
  60863         \object-list ScheduleNames
  60864         \note A fan operating mode schedule value of 0 indicates cycling fan mode (supply air
  60865         \note fan cycles on and off in tandem with the cooling or heating coil).
  60866         \note Any other schedule value indicates continuous fan mode (supply air fan operates
  60867         \note continuously regardless of cooling or heating coil operation). Provide a schedule
  60868         \note with non-zero values when high humidity control is specified.
  60869         \note Leaving this schedule name blank will default to cycling fan mode for the
  60870         \note entire simulation period.
  60871    N1,  \field Maximum Supply Air Temperature
  60872         \type real
  60873         \units C
  60874         \autosizable
  60875         \default 80.0
  60876    N2,  \field Cooling Supply Air Flow Rate
  60877         \required-field
  60878         \type real
  60879         \units m3/s
  60880         \minimum> 0.0
  60881         \autosizable
  60882         \note Must be less than or equal to the fan's maximum flow rate.
  60883    N3,  \field Heating Supply Air Flow Rate
  60884         \required-field
  60885         \type real
  60886         \units m3/s
  60887         \minimum> 0.0
  60888         \autosizable
  60889         \note Must be less than or equal to the fan's maximum flow fate.
  60890    N4,  \field No Load Supply Air Flow Rate
  60891         \type real
  60892         \units m3/s
  60893         \minimum 0.0
  60894         \autosizable
  60895         \note Must be less than or equal to the fan's maximum flow rate.
  60896         \note Only used when fan operating mode is continuous (disregarded for cycling fan mode).
  60897         \note This air flow rate is used when no heating or cooling is required (i.e., the DX coil
  60898         \note compressor and heating coil are off). If this field is left blank or zero, the supply
  60899         \note air flow rate from the previous on cycle (either cooling or heating) is used.
  60900    A6,  \field Controlling Zone or Thermostat Location
  60901         \required-field
  60902         \type object-list
  60903         \object-list ZoneNames
  60904    A7,  \field Supply Fan Object Type
  60905         \required-field
  60906         \type choice
  60907         \key Fan:OnOff
  60908         \key Fan:ConstantVolume
  60909         \note Fan:ConstantVolume only works with continuous fan operating mode (i.e. supply
  60910         \note air fan operating mode schedule values not equal to 0).
  60911    A8,  \field Supply Fan Name
  60912         \required-field
  60913         \type object-list
  60914         \object-list FansCVandOnOff
  60915    A9 , \field Fan Placement
  60916         \type choice
  60917         \key BlowThrough
  60918         \key DrawThrough
  60919         \default BlowThrough
  60920    A10, \field Heating Coil Object Type
  60921         \required-field
  60922         \type choice
  60923         \key Coil:Heating:Fuel
  60924         \key Coil:Heating:Electric
  60925         \key Coil:Heating:Water
  60926         \key Coil:Heating:Steam
  60927         \note works with gas, electric, hot water and steam heating coils
  60928    A11, \field Heating Coil Name
  60929         \required-field
  60930         \type object-list
  60931         \object-list HeatingCoilName
  60932    A12, \field Cooling Coil Object Type
