  63033   N22, \field Outdoor Unit Fan Flow Rate Per Unit of Rated Evaporative Capacity
  63034        \note Enter the outdoor unit fan flow rate per Watt of rated evaporative capacity [W/W]
  63035        \units m3/s-W
  63036        \minimum> 0.0
  63037        \default 7.50E-5
  63038        \type real
  63039   A6 , \field Outdoor Unit Evaporating Temperature Function of Superheating Curve Name
  63040        \required-field
  63041        \type object-list
  63042        \object-list UnivariateFunctions
  63043   A7 , \field Outdoor Unit Condensing Temperature Function of Subcooling Curve Name
  63044        \required-field
  63045        \type object-list
  63046        \object-list UnivariateFunctions
  63047   N23, \field Diameter of Main Pipe for Suction Gas
  63048        \note used to calculate the piping loss
  63049        \type real
  63050        \units m
  63051        \minimum 0.0
  63052        \default 0.0762
  63053   N24, \field Diameter of Main Pipe for Discharge Gas
  63054        \note used to calculate the piping loss
  63055        \type real
  63056        \units m
  63057        \minimum 0.0
  63058        \default 0.0762
  63059   N25, \field Length of Main Pipe Connecting Outdoor Unit to the First Branch Joint
  63060        \note used to calculate the heat loss of the main pipe
  63061        \type real
  63062        \units m
  63063        \minimum 0.0
  63064        \default 30.0
  63065   N26, \field Equivalent Length of Main Pipe Connecting Outdoor Unit to the First Branch Joint
  63066        \note used to calculate the refrigerant pressure drop of the main pipe
  63067        \type real
  63068        \units m
  63069        \minimum 0.0
  63070        \default 36.0
  63071   N27, \field Height Difference Between Outdoor Unit and Indoor Units
  63072        \note Difference between outdoor unit height and indoor unit height
  63073        \note Positive means outdoor unit is higher than indoor unit
  63074        \note Negative means outdoor unit is lower than indoor unit
  63075        \type real
  63076        \units m
  63077        \default 5.0
  63078   N28, \field Main Pipe Insulation Thickness
  63079        \type real
  63080        \units m
  63081        \minimum 0.0
  63082        \default 0.02
  63083   N29, \field Main Pipe Insulation Thermal Conductivity
  63084        \type real
  63085        \units W/m-K
  63086        \minimum 0.0
  63087        \default 0.032
  63088   N30, \field Crankcase Heater Power per Compressor
  63089        \type real
  63090        \units W
  63091        \default 33.0
  63092        \note Enter the value of the resistive heater located in the compressor(s). This heater
  63093        \note is used to warm the refrigerant and oil when the compressor is off
  63094   N31, \field Number of Compressors
  63095        \type integer
  63096        \units dimensionless
  63097        \default 2
  63098        \note Enter the total number of compressor. This input is used only for crankcase
  63099        \note heater calculations.
  63100   N32, \field Ratio of Compressor Size to Total Compressor Capacity
  63101        \type real
  63102        \units W/W
  63103        \default 0.5
  63104        \note Enter the ratio of the first stage compressor to total compressor capacity
  63105        \note All other compressors are assumed to be equally sized. This inputs is used
  63106        \note only for crankcase heater calculations
  63107   N33, \field Maximum Outdoor Dry-Bulb Temperature for Crankcase Heater
  63108        \type real
  63109        \units C
  63110        \default 5.0
  63111        \note Enter the maximum outdoor temperature above which the crankcase heaters are disabled
  63112   A8, \field Defrost Strategy
  63113        \type choice
  63114        \key ReverseCycle
  63115        \key Resistive
  63116        \default Resistive
  63117        \note Select a defrost strategy.
  63118        \note Reverse cycle reverses the operating mode from heating to
  63119        \note cooling to melt frost formation on the condenser coil
  63120        \note The resistive strategy uses a resistive heater
  63121        \note to melt the frost.
  63122   A9, \field Defrost Control
  63123        \type choice
  63124        \key Timed
  63125        \key OnDemand
  63126        \default Timed
  63127        \note Choose a defrost control type
  63128        \note Either use a fixed Timed defrost period or select
  63129        \note OnDemand to defrost only when necessary
  63130   A10, \field Defrost Energy Input Ratio Modifier Function of Temperature Curve Name
  63131        \type object-list
  63132        \object-list BivariateFunctions
  63133        \note A valid performance curve must be used if ReverseCycle defrost strategy is selected
  63134   N34, \field Defrost Time Period Fraction
  63135        \type real
  63136        \minimum 0.0
  63137        \default 0.058333
  63138        \note Fraction of time in defrost mode
  63139        \note Only applicable if timed defrost control is specified
  63140   N35, \field Resistive Defrost Heater Capacity
  63141        \type real
  63142        \minimum 0.0
  63143        \default 0.0
  63144        \autosizable
  63145        \units W
  63146        \note Enter the size of the resistive defrost heating element
  63147        \note Only applicable if resistive defrost strategy is specified
  63148        \ip-units W
  63149   N36, \field Maximum Outdoor Dry-bulb Temperature for Defrost Operation
  63150        \type real
  63151        \units C
  63152        \default 5.0
  63153        \note Enter the maximum outdoor temperature above which the defrost operation is disabled
  63154   N37, \field Initial Heat Recovery Cooling Capacity Fraction
  63155        \type real
  63156        \units W/W
  63157        \default 1
  63158        \note This is used to describe the transition from Cooling Only mode to Heat Recovery mode
  63159        \note Enter the fractional capacity available at the start
  63160        \note of heat recovery mode. The capacity exponentially approaches
  63161        \note the steady-state value according to the inputs for
  63162        \note Heat Recovery Cooling Capacity Modifier and Heat Recovery
  63163        \note Cooling Capacity Time Constant
  63164   N38, \field Heat Recovery Cooling Capacity Time Constant
  63165        \type real
  63166        \units hr
  63167        \default 0
  63168        \note This is used to describe the transition from Cooling Only mode to Heat Recovery mode
  63169        \note Enter the time constant used to model the transition
  63170        \note from cooling only mode to heat recovery mode
  63171   N39, \field Initial Heat Recovery Cooling Energy Fraction
  63172        \type real
  63173        \units W/W
  63174        \default 1
  63175        \note This is used to describe the transition from Cooling Only mode to Heat Recovery mode
  63176        \note Enter the fractional electric consumption rate at the start
