  68444 PipingSystem:Underground:PipeSegment,
  68445         \memo The pipe segment to be used in an underground piping system
  68446         \memo This object represents a single pipe leg positioned axially
  68447         \memo  in the local z-direction, at a given x, y location in the domain
  68448         \min-fields 4
  68449    A1,  \field Name
  68450         \required-field
  68451         \type alpha
  68452         \reference PipingSystemUndergroundSegmentNames
  68453    N1,  \field X Position
  68454         \required-field
  68455         \type real
  68456         \units m
  68457         \minimum> 0
  68458         \note This segment will be centered at this distance from the x=0
  68459         \note  domain surface or the basement wall surface, based on whether
  68460         \note  a basement exists in this domain and the selection of the
  68461         \note  shift input field found in the domain object.
  68462    N2,  \field Y Position
  68463         \required-field
  68464         \type real
  68465         \units m
  68466         \minimum> 0
  68467         \note This segment will be centered at this distance away from the
  68468         \note  ground surface; thus this value represents the burial depth
  68469         \note  of this pipe segment.
  68470    A3;  \field Flow Direction
  68471         \required-field
  68472         \type choice
  68473         \key IncreasingZ
  68474         \key DecreasingZ
  68475         \note This segment will be simulated such that the flow is in the
  68476         \note  selected direction.  This can allow for detailed analysis
  68477         \note  of circuiting effects in a single domain.
  68478 
