  69327 SolarCollectorPerformance:IntegralCollectorStorage,
  69328        \memo Thermal and optical performance parameters for a single glazed solar collector with
  69329        \memo integral storage unit.
  69330        \min-fields 19
  69331   A1,  \field Name
  69332        \required-field
  69333        \type alpha
  69334        \reference CollectorStoragePerformance
  69335   A2,  \field ICS Collector Type
  69336        \type choice
  69337        \key RectangularTank
  69338        \default RectangularTank
  69339        \note Currently only RectangularTank ICS collector type is available.
  69340   N1,  \field Gross Area
  69341        \type real
  69342        \minimum> 0
  69343        \units m2
  69344   N2,  \field Collector Water Volume
  69345        \type real
  69346        \minimum> 0
  69347        \units m3
  69348        \ip-units gal
  69349   N3,  \field Bottom Heat Loss Conductance
  69350        \type real
  69351        \minimum> 0
  69352        \default 0.40
  69353        \units W/m2-K
  69354        \note Heat loss conductance of the collector bottom insulation
  69355   N4,  \field Side Heat Loss Conductance
  69356        \type real
  69357        \minimum> 0
  69358        \default 0.60
  69359        \units W/m2-K
  69360        \note heat loss conductance of the collector side insulation
  69361   N5,  \field Aspect Ratio
  69362        \type real
  69363        \minimum> 0.5
  69364        \maximum< 1.0
  69365        \default 0.8
  69366        \units m
  69367        \note This value is ratio of the width (short side) to length
  69368        \note (long side of) of the collector.  Used to calculate the
  69369        \note perimeter of the collector
  69370   N6,  \field Collector Side Height
  69371        \type real
  69372        \minimum> 0
  69373        \maximum< 0.30
  69374        \default 0.20
  69375        \units m
  69376        \note This value is used to estimate collector side area for the heat
  69377        \note loss calculation through the collector side
  69378   N7,  \field Thermal Mass of Absorber Plate
  69379        \type real
  69380        \minimum 0
  69381        \default 0
  69382        \units J/m2-K
  69383        \note Calculated from the specific heat, density and thickness
  69384        \note of the absorber plate.
  69385   N8,  \field Number of Covers
  69386        \type integer
  69387        \minimum 1
  69388        \maximum 2
  69389        \default 2
  69390        \note Number of transparent covers. Common practice is to use low-iron
  69391        \note glass as the outer cover and very thin transparent sheet such as
  69392        \note Teflon as the inner cover.
  69393   N9,  \field Cover Spacing
  69394        \type real
  69395        \minimum> 0
  69396        \maximum 0.20
  69397        \default 0.05
  69398        \units m
  69399        \note The gap between the transparent covers and between the inner cover
  69400        \note and the absorber plate
  69401   N10,  \field Refractive Index of Outer Cover
  69402        \type real
  69403        \minimum 1.0
  69404        \maximum 2.0
  69405        \default 1.526
  69406        \units dimensionless
  69407        \note Refractive index of outer cover. Typically low-iron glass is used
  69408        \note as the outer cover material, and used as the default outer cover
  69409        \note with a value of 1.526.
  69410   N11,  \field Extinction Coefficient Times Thickness of Outer Cover
  69411        \type real
  69412        \minimum 0.
  69413        \default 0.045
  69414        \units dimensionless
  69415        \note Clear glass has extinction coefficient of about 15 [1/m]
  69416        \note and with thickness of 3.0mm, the product of the extinction
  69417        \note coefficient and thickness becomes 0.045 (=15 * 0.003)
  69418   N12,  \field Emissivity of Outer Cover
  69419        \type real
  69420        \minimum> 0.
  69421        \maximum< 1.0
  69422        \default 0.88
  69423        \units dimensionless
  69424        \note Thermal emissivity of the outer cover, commonly glass is used as
  69425        \note the out collector cover material.
  69426   N13,  \field Refractive Index of Inner Cover
  69427        \type real
  69428        \minimum 1.0
  69429        \maximum 2.0
  69430        \default 1.37
  69431        \units dimensionless
  69432        \note Typical material is very thin sheet of Teflon (PTFE). The default
  69433        \note value is refractive index of Teflon.
  69434   N14, \field Extinction Coefficient Times Thickness of the inner Cover
  69435        \type real
  69436        \minimum 0.
  69437        \default 0.008
  69438        \units dimensionless
  69439        \note Default inner cover is very thin sheet of Teflon with
  69440        \note extinction coefficient of approximately 40.0 and a thickness
  69441        \note 0.2mm yields a default value of 0.008.
  69442   N15, \field Emissivity of Inner Cover
  69443        \type real
  69444        \minimum> 0.
  69445        \maximum< 1.0
  69446        \default 0.88
  69447        \units dimensionless
  69448        \note Thermal emissivity of the inner cover material
  69449   N16, \field Absorptance of Absorber Plate
  69450        \type real
  69451        \minimum> 0.
  69452        \maximum< 1.0
  69453        \default 0.96
  69454        \units dimensionless
  69455        \note The absorber plate solar absorptance.  Copper is assumed as
  69456        \note the default absorber plate.
  69457   N17; \field Emissivity of Absorber Plate
  69458        \type real
  69459        \minimum> 0.
  69460        \maximum< 1.0
  69461        \default 0.30
  69462        \units dimensionless
  69463        \note Thermal emissivity of the absorber plate
