  70036        \note when the basin heater is available (field Basin Heater Operating Schedule Name).
  70037        \note For this situation, the heater maintains the basin water temperature at the basin heater
  70038        \note setpoint temperature when the outdoor air temperature falls below the setpoint temperature.
  70039        \note The basin heater only operates when the chiller is not operating.
  70040   N17, \field Basin Heater Setpoint Temperature
  70041        \type real
  70042        \units C
  70043        \minimum 2.0
  70044        \default 2.0
  70045        \note This field is only used for Condenser Type = EvaporativelyCooled.
  70046        \note Enter the outdoor dry-bulb temperature when the basin heater turns on.
  70047   A13, \field Basin Heater Operating Schedule Name
  70048        \type object-list
  70049        \object-list ScheduleNames
  70050        \note This field is only used for Condenser Type = EvaporativelyCooled.
  70051        \note Schedule values greater than 0 allow the basin heater to operate whenever the outdoor
  70052        \note air dry-bulb temperature is below the basin heater setpoint temperature.
  70053        \note If a schedule name is not entered, the basin heater is allowed to operate
  70054        \note throughout the entire simulation.
