  70526        \type node
  70527        \note Enter the generator outlet node name which connects this chiller to a
  70528        \note steam or hot water plant, otherwise leave this field blank.
  70529        \note Generator nodes are used to model heat input to the chiller.
  70530   A11, \field Capacity Correction Function of Condenser Temperature Curve Name
  70531        \type object-list
  70532        \object-list UnivariateFunctions
  70533        \note Curve which shows the change in normalized capacity to changes in condenser temperature.
  70534   A12, \field Capacity Correction Function of Chilled Water Temperature Curve Name
  70535        \type object-list
  70536        \object-list UnivariateFunctions
  70537        \note Curve which shows the change in normalized capacity to changes in leaving chilled water temperature.
  70538   A13, \field Capacity Correction Function of Generator Temperature Curve Name
  70539        \type object-list
  70540        \object-list UnivariateFunctions
  70541        \note Used when generator fluid type is hot water
  70542        \note Curve which shows the change in normalized capacity to changes in generator temperature.
  70543   A14, \field Generator Heat Input Correction Function of Condenser Temperature Curve Name
  70544        \type object-list
  70545        \object-list UnivariateFunctions
  70546        \note Curve which shows the change in normalized heat input to changes in condenser temperature.
  70547   A15, \field Generator Heat Input Correction Function of Chilled Water Temperature Curve Name
  70548        \type object-list
  70549        \object-list UnivariateFunctions
  70550        \note Curve which shows the change in normalized heat input to changes in leaving chilled water temperature.
  70551   A16, \field Generator Heat Source Type
  70552        \type choice
  70553        \key HotWater
  70554        \key Steam
  70555        \default Steam
  70556        \note The Generator side of the chiller can be connected to a hot water or steam plant where the
  70557        \note generator inlet and outlet nodes are connected to a plant loop. If the generator is not
  70558        \note connected to a plant loop, and the generator inlet/outlet nodes are not used, this field should be
  70559        \note specified as steam or left blank. When a plant is not used, the model assumes steam as the heat source.
  70560   N11, \field Design Generator Fluid Flow Rate
  70561        \type real
  70562        \units m3/s
  70563        \ip-units gal/min
  70564        \autosizable
  70565        \note  For variable flow this is the max flow and for constant flow this is the flow.
  70566   N12, \field Temperature Lower Limit Generator Inlet
  70567        \type real
  70568        \units C
  70569        \default 0.0
  70570        \note Provides warnings when entering generator temperature is below minimum.
  70571        \note Capacity is not adjusted when entering generator temperature is below minimum.
  70572   N13, \field Degree of Subcooling in Steam Generator
  70573        \type real
  70574        \units C
  70575        \minimum 0.0
  70576        \maximum 20.0
  70577        \default 1.0
  70578        \note This field is not used when the generator inlet/outlet nodes are not specified or
  70579        \note the generator is connected to a hot water loop.
  70580   N14, \field Degree of Subcooling in Steam Condensate Loop
  70581        \type real
  70582        \units C
  70583        \minimum 0.0
  70584        \default 0.0
  70585        \note This field is not used when the generator inlet/outlet nodes are not specified or
  70586        \note the generator is connected to a hot water loop.
  70587   N15; \field Sizing Factor
  70588        \note Multiplies the autosized capacity and flow rates
  70589        \type real
  70590        \minimum> 0.0
  70591        \default 1.0
  70592 
