  72518 ChillerHeaterPerformance:Electric:EIR,
  72519        \min-fields 29
  72520        \memo This chiller model is a generic chiller-heater where the cooling mode performance is a
  72521        \memo function of condenser entering or leaving fluid temperature and the heating mode performance
  72522        \memo is typically a function of condenser leaving fluid temperature. Performance at off-reference
  72523        \memo conditions is modeled using three polynomial equations per mode. Six curve objects are required.
  72524   A1 , \field Name
  72525        \type alpha
  72526        \required-field
  72527        \reference ChillerHeaterEIRNames
  72528   N1 , \field Reference Cooling Mode Evaporator Capacity
  72529        \type real
  72530        \units W
  72531        \required-field
  72532        \minimum> 0.0
  72533        \autosizable
  72534   N2 , \field Reference Cooling Mode COP
  72535        \note Efficiency of the chiller compressor (cooling output/compressor energy input).
  72536        \type real
  72537        \units W/W
  72538        \required-field
  72539        \minimum> 0.0
  72540   N3 , \field Reference Cooling Mode Leaving Chilled Water Temperature
  72541        \type real
  72542        \default 6.67
  72543        \units C
  72544   N4 , \field Reference Cooling Mode Entering Condenser Fluid Temperature
  72545        \type real
  72546        \default 29.44
  72547        \units C
  72548   N5 , \field Reference Cooling Mode Leaving Condenser Water Temperature
  72549        \type real
  72550        \default 35.0
  72551        \units C
  72552   N6 , \field Reference Heating Mode Cooling Capacity Ratio
  72553        \note During simultaneous cooling-heating mode, this ratio is relative to the Reference Cooling Mode Cooling Capacity
  72554        \note (Evaporator capacity at simul clg-htg mode ref condition)/ (Evaporator capacity at cooling mode ref condition)
  72555        \type real
  72556        \default 0.75
  72557   N7 , \field Reference Heating Mode Cooling Power Input Ratio
  72558        \note During simultaneous cooling-heating mode, this ratio is relative to the Reference Cooling Mode COP
  72559        \note (Power at simultaneous clg-htg mode reference condition)/ (Power at cooling mode reference condition)
  72560        \type real
  72561        \default 1.38
  72562        \minimum> 0.0
  72563   N8 , \field Reference Heating Mode Leaving Chilled Water Temperature
  72564        \note During simultaneous cooling-heating mode
  72565        \type real
  72566        \default 6.67
  72567        \units C
  72568   N9 , \field Reference Heating Mode Leaving Condenser Water Temperature
  72569        \note During simultaneous cooling-heating mode
  72570        \type real
  72571        \default 49
  72572        \units C
  72573   N10, \field Reference Heating Mode Entering Condenser Fluid Temperature
  72574        \type real
  72575        \default 29.44
  72576        \units C
  72577   N11, \field Heating Mode Entering Chilled Water Temperature Low Limit
  72578        \note During simultaneous cooling-heating mode
  72579        \type real
  72580        \default 12.22
  72581        \units C
  72582   A2 , \field Chilled Water Flow Mode Type
  72583        \note Sets chilled water flow rate to either constant or variable.
  72584        \type choice
  72585        \key ConstantFlow
  72586        \key VariableFlow
  72587        \default ConstantFlow
  72588   N12, \field Design Chilled Water Flow Rate
  72589        \type real
  72590        \units m3/s
  72591        \minimum> 0
  72592        \autosizable
  72593        \ip-units gal/min
  72594   N13, \field Design Condenser Water Flow Rate
  72595        \type real
  72596        \units m3/s
  72597        \autosizable
  72598        \minimum> 0.0
  72599        \autosizable
  72600        \ip-units gal/min
  72601   N14, \field Design Hot Water Flow Rate
  72602        \type real
  72603        \units m3/s
  72604        \minimum 0.0
  72605        \default 0.0
  72606        \ip-units gal/min
  72607   N15, \field Compressor Motor Efficiency
  72608        \type real
  72609        \note Fraction of compressor electrical energy that must be rejected by the condenser.
  72610        \note Enter 1.0 or leave this field blank for a hermetic compressor.
  72611        \minimum 0.0
  72612        \maximum 1.0
  72613        \default 1.0
  72614   A3 , \field Condenser Type
  72615        \type choice
  72616        \key AirCooled
  72617        \key WaterCooled
  72618        \default WaterCooled
  72619   A4 , \field Cooling Mode Temperature Curve Condenser Water Independent Variable
  72620        \type choice
  72621        \key EnteringCondenser
  72622        \key LeavingCondenser
  72623        \default EnteringCondenser
  72624        \note Sets the second independent variable in the three temperature dependent performance
  72625        \note curves to either the leaving or entering condenser water temperature. Manufacturers
  72626        \note express the performance of their chillers using either the leaving condenser water
  72627        \note temperature (to the tower) or the entering condenser water temperature (from the tower).
  72628        \note Cooling mode is generally a stronger function of Entering Condenser Fluid Temperature
  72629   A5 , \field Cooling Mode Cooling Capacity Function of Temperature Curve Name
  72630        \note Cooling capacity as a function of leaving chilled water temperature
  72631        \note and either entering or leaving condenser fluid temperature
  72632        \required-field
  72633        \type object-list
  72634        \object-list BivariateFunctions
  72635        \note curve = a + b*CWS + c*CWS**2 + d*TCond + e*TCond**2 + f*CWS*TCond
  72636        \note    If ClgModeCondWaterCurveInputVariable = EnteringCondenser, TCond = ECT
  72637        \note    If ClgModeCondWaterCurveInputVariable = LeavingCondenser, TCond = LCT
  72638        \note CWS = supply (leaving) chilled water temperature(C)
  72639        \note LCT = leaving condenser fluid temperature(C)
  72640        \note ECT = entering condenser fluid temperature(C)
  72641   A6 , \field Cooling Mode Electric Input to Cooling Output Ratio Function of Temperature Curve Name
  72642        \note Electric Input Ratio (EIR) as a function of supply (leaving) chilled water temperature
  72643        \note and leaving condenser fluid temperature.   EIR = 1/COP.
  72644        \required-field
  72645        \type object-list
  72646        \object-list BivariateFunctions
  72647        \note curve = a + b*CWS + c*CWS**2 + d*TCond + e*TCond**2 + f*CWS*TCond
  72648        \note If ClgModeCondWaterCurveInputVariable = EnteringCondenser, TCond = ECT
  72649        \note If ClgModeCondWaterCurveInputVariable = LeavingCondenser, TCond = LCT
  72650        \note CWS = supply (leaving) chilled water temperature(C)
  72651        \note LCT = leaving condenser fluid temperature(C)
  72652        \note ECT = entering condenser fluid temperature(C)
  72653   A7 , \field Cooling Mode Electric Input to Cooling Output Ratio Function of Part Load Ratio Curve Name
  72654        \note Electric Input Ratio (EIR) as a function of Part Load Ratio (PLR)
  72655        \note EIR = 1/COP
  72656        \required-field
  72657        \type object-list
  72658        \object-list UnivariateFunctions
  72659        \object-list BivariateFunctions
  72660        \note  Bicubic = a + b*TCond + c*TCond**2 + d*PLR + e*PLR**2 + f*TCond*PLR +g*0 + h*PLR**3+i*0+j*0
  72661        \note    If ClgModeCondWaterCurveInputVariable = EnteringCondenser, TCond = ECT
  72662        \note    If ClgModeCondWaterCurveInputVariable = LeavingCondenser, TCond = LCT
  72663        \note    Normally, a bicubic curve here should be in terms of LCT rather than ECT
  72664        \note    Also, a bicubic curve is more applicable for variable-speed compressor motor drives
  72665        \note or
  72666        \note  Quadratic = a + b*PLR + c*PLR**2
  72667        \note PLR = part load ratio (cooling load/steady-state capacity)
  72668        \note LCT = leaving condenser fluid temperature(C)
  72669        \note ECT = entering condenser fluid temperature(C)
  72670   N16, \field Cooling Mode Cooling Capacity Optimum Part Load Ratio
  72671        \type real
  72672        \note Optimum part load ratio where the chiller is most efficient.
  72673        \note Must be greater than or equal to the Minimum Part Load Ratio
  72674        \note and less than or equal to the Maximum Part Load Ratio.
  72675        \note The Min/Max PLR are taken from their associated EIR-FPLR curve references.
  72676        \minimum> 0.0
  72677        \default 1.0
  72678   A8 , \field Heating Mode Temperature Curve Condenser Water Independent Variable
  72679        \type choice
  72680        \key EnteringCondenser
  72681        \key LeavingCondenser
  72682        \default LeavingCondenser
  72683        \note Sets the second independent variable in the three temperature dependent performance
  72684        \note curves to either the leaving or entering condenser water temperature. Manufacturers
  72685        \note express the performance of their chillers using either the leaving condenser water
  72686        \note temperature (to the tower) or the entering condenser water temperature (from the tower).
  72687        \note Heating mode (or Simul Clg/Htg Load) should be a function of Leaving Condenser Fluid Temperature
  72688        \note Only use EnteringCondenser as a last resort in case no performance data exists for LeavingCondenser
  72689   A9 , \field Heating Mode Cooling Capacity Function of Temperature Curve Name
  72690        \note Evaporator (cooling) capacity as a function of leaving chilled water temperature
  72691        \note and leaving condenser fluid temperature when in heating or simultaneous cool/heat mode
  72692        \required-field
  72693        \type object-list
  72694        \object-list BivariateFunctions
  72695        \note curve = a + b*CWS + c*CWS**2 + d*TCond + e*TCond**2 + f*CWS*TCond
  72696        \note    If independent variable = EnteringCondenser, TCond = ECT
  72697        \note    If independent variable = LeavingCondenser, TCond = LCT
  72698        \note CWS = supply (leaving) chilled water temperature(C)
  72699        \note LCT = leaving condenser fluid temperature(C)
  72700        \note ECT = entering condenser fluid temperature(C)
  72701   A10, \field Heating Mode Electric Input to Cooling Output Ratio Function of Temperature Curve Name
  72702        \note Electric Input Ratio (EIR) as a function of leaving chilled water temperature when in heating or simultaneous cool/heat mode
  72703        \note and leaving condenser fluid temperature.   EIR = 1/COP.
  72704        \required-field
  72705        \type object-list
  72706        \object-list BivariateFunctions
  72707        \note curve = a + b*CWS + c*CWS**2 + d*TCond + e*TCond**2 + f*CWS*TCond
  72708        \note    If independent variable = EnteringCondenser, TCond = ECT
  72709        \note    If independent variable = LeavingCondenser, TCond = LCT
  72710        \note CWS = leaving chilled water temperature(C)
  72711        \note LCT = leaving condenser fluid temperature(C)
  72712        \note ECT = entering condenser fluid temperature(C)
  72713   A11, \field Heating Mode Electric Input to Cooling Output Ratio Function of Part Load Ratio Curve Name
  72714        \note Electric Input Ratio (EIR) as a function of Part Load Ratio (PLR) when in heating or simultaneous cool/heat mode
  72715        \note EIR = 1/COP
  72716        \required-field
  72717        \type object-list
  72718        \object-list UnivariateFunctions
  72719        \object-list BivariateFunctions
  72720        \note  Bicubic = a + b*LCT + c*LCT**2 + d*PLR + e*PLR**2 + f*LCT*PLR + g*0 + h*PLR**3 + i*0 + j*0
  72721        \note    Normally, a bicubic curve here should be in terms of LCT rather than ECT
  72722        \note    Also, a bicubic curve is more applicable for variable-speed compressor motor drives
  72723        \note or
  72724        \note  Quadratic = a + b*PLR + c*PLR**2
  72725        \note PLR = part load ratio (cooling load/steady-state capacity)
  72726        \note LCT = leaving condenser fluid temperature(C)
  72727        \note ECT = entering condenser fluid temperature(C)
  72728   N17, \field Heating Mode Cooling Capacity Optimum Part Load Ratio
  72729        \type real
  72730        \note Optimum part load ratio where the chiller is most efficient when in heating or simultaneous cool/heat mode.
  72731        \note Must be greater than or equal to the Minimum Part Load Ratio
  72732        \note and less than or equal to the Maximum Part Load Ratio.
  72733        \note The Min/Max PLR are taken from their associated EIR-FPLR curve references.
  72734        \minimum> 0.0
  72735        \default 1.0
  72736   N18; \field Sizing Factor
  72737        \note Multiplies the autosized capacity and flow rates
  72738        \type real
  72739        \minimum> 0.0
  72740        \default 1.0
  72741 
  72742 \group Condenser Equipment and Heat Exchangers
  72743 
  72744 !*****************CONDENSING EQUIPMENT*********************
  72745 CoolingTower:SingleSpeed,
  72746        \min-fields 16
  72747        \memo This tower model is based on Merkel's theory, which is also the basis
  72748        \memo for the tower model in ASHRAE's HVAC1 Toolkit. The open wet cooling tower
  72749        \memo is modeled as a counter flow heat exchanger with a single-speed fan drawing air
  72750        \memo through the tower (induced-draft configuration).
  72751        \memo Added fluid bypass as an additional capacity control. 8/2008.
  72752        \memo For a multi-cell tower, the capacity and air/water flow rate inputs are for the entire tower.
  72753   A1 , \field Name
  72754        \required-field
  72755        \type alpha
  72756        \reference CoolingTowers
  72757        \reference CoolingTowersWithUA
  72758        \note Tower Name
  72759        \reference-class-name validPlantEquipmentTypes
  72760        \reference validPlantEquipmentNames
  72761        \reference-class-name validCondenserEquipmentTypes
  72762        \reference validCondenserEquipmentNames
  72763        \reference-class-name validBranchEquipmentTypes
  72764        \reference validBranchEquipmentNames
  72765   A2 , \field Water Inlet Node Name
  72766        \required-field
  72767        \type node
  72768        \note Name of tower water inlet node
  72769   A3 , \field Water Outlet Node Name
  72770        \required-field
  72771        \type node
  72772        \note Name of tower water outlet node
  72773   N1 , \field Design Water Flow Rate
  72774        \type real
  72775        \units m3/s
  72776        \minimum> 0.0
  72777        \autosizable
  72778        \note Leave field blank if tower performance input method is NominalCapacity
  72779        \ip-units gal/min
  72780   N2 , \field Design Air Flow Rate
  72781        \required-field
  72782        \type real
  72783        \units m3/s
  72784        \minimum> 0.0
  72785        \autosizable
  72786   N3 , \field Design Fan Power
  72787        \required-field
  72788        \type real
  72789        \units W
  72790        \minimum> 0.0
  72791        \autosizable
  72792        \ip-units W
  72793        \note This is the fan motor electric input power
  72794   N4 , \field Design U-Factor Times Area Value
  72795        \type real
  72796        \units W/K
  72797        \minimum> 0.0
  72798        \maximum 2100000.0
  72799        \autosizable
  72800        \note Leave field blank if tower performance input method is NominalCapacity
  72801   N5 , \field Free Convection Regime Air Flow Rate
  72802        \type real
  72803        \units m3/s
  72804        \minimum 0.0
  72805        \default 0.0
  72806        \autocalculatable
  72807   N6 , \field Free Convection Regime Air Flow Rate Sizing Factor
  72808        \type real
  72809        \default 0.1
  72810        \minimum> 0.0
  72811        \maximum< 1.0
  72812        \note This field is only used if the previous field is set to autocalculate.
  72813   N7 , \field Free Convection Regime U-Factor Times Area Value
  72814        \type real
  72815        \units W/K
  72816        \minimum 0.0
  72817        \maximum 300000.0
  72818        \default 0.0
  72819        \autocalculatable
  72820   N8 , \field Free Convection U-Factor Times Area Value Sizing Factor
  72821        \type real
  72822        \default 0.1
  72823        \minimum> 0.0
  72824        \maximum< 1.0
  72825        \note This field is only used if the previous field is set to autocalculate and
  72826        \note the Performance Input Method is UFactorTimesAreaAndDesignWaterFlowRate
  72827   A4 , \field Performance Input Method
  72828        \type choice
  72829        \key UFactorTimesAreaAndDesignWaterFlowRate
  72830        \key NominalCapacity
  72831        \default UFactorTimesAreaAndDesignWaterFlowRate
  72832        \note User can define tower thermal performance by specifying the tower UA,
  72833        \note the Design Air Flow Rate and the Design Water Flow Rate,
  72834        \note or by specifying the tower nominal capacity
  72835   N9 , \field Heat Rejection Capacity and Nominal Capacity Sizing Ratio
  72836        \type real
  72837        \default 1.25
  72838   N10, \field Nominal Capacity
  72839        \type real
  72840        \units W
  72841        \minimum> 0.0
  72842        \note Nominal tower capacity with entering water at 35C (95F), leaving water at
  72843        \note 29.44C (85F), entering air at 25.56C (78F) wet-bulb temperature and 35C (95F)
  72844        \note dry-bulb temperature. Design water flow rate assumed to be 5.382E-8 m3/s per watt
  72845        \note (3 gpm/ton). Nominal tower capacity times (1.25) gives the actual tower
  72846        \note heat rejection at these operating conditions.
  72847   N11, \field Free Convection Capacity
  72848        \type real
  72849        \units W
  72850        \minimum 0.0
  72851        \autocalculatable
  72852        \note Tower capacity in free convection regime with entering water at 35C (95F),
  72853        \note leaving water at 29.44C (85F), entering air at 25.56C (78F) wet-bulb temperature
  72854        \note and 35C (95F) dry-bulb temperature. Design water flow rate assumed to be
  72855        \note 5.382E-8 m3/s per watt of nominal tower capacity (3 gpm/ton). Tower free
  72856        \note convection capacity times (1.25) gives the actual tower heat rejection at these
  72857        \note operating conditions.
  72858   N12, \field Free Convection Nominal Capacity Sizing Factor
  72859        \type real
  72860        \default 0.1
  72861        \minimum> 0.0
  72862        \maximum< 1.0
  72863        \note This field is only used if the previous field is set to autocalculate
  72864   N13, \field Design Inlet Air Dry-Bulb Temperature
  72865        \type real
  72866        \units C
  72867        \default 35.0
  72868        \minimum 20.0
  72869        \note Enter the tower's design inlet air dry-bulb temperature
  72870   N14, \field Design Inlet Air Wet-Bulb Temperature
  72871        \type real
  72872        \units C
  72873        \default 25.6
  72874        \minimum 20.0
  72875        \note Enter the tower's design inlet air wet-bulb temperature
  72876   N15, \field Design Approach Temperature
  72877        \type real
  72878        \units deltaC
  72879        \autosizable
  72880        \default autosize
  72881        \minimum> 0
  72882        \note Enter the approach temperature corresponding to the design inlet air
  72883        \note wet-bulb temperature and design range temperature.
  72884        \note Design approach temp = outlet water temperature minus inlet air wet-bulb temperature
  72885        \note at design conditions. Autosized to 3.9 deltaC.
  72886   N16, \field Design Range Temperature
  72887        \type real
  72888        \units deltaC
  72889        \autosizable
  72890        \default autosize
  72891        \minimum> 0
  72892        \note Enter the range temperature corresponding to the design inlet air
  72893        \note wet-bulb temperature and design approach temperature.
  72894        \note Design range = inlet water temperature minus outlet water temperature
  72895        \note at design conditions. Autosized to 5.5 deltaC.
  72896   N17, \field Basin Heater Capacity
  72897        \type real
  72898        \units W/K
  72899        \minimum 0.0
  72900        \default 0.0
  72901        \note This heater maintains the basin water temperature at the basin heater setpoint
  72902        \note temperature when the outdoor air temperature falls below the setpoint temperature.
  72903        \note The basin heater only operates when water is not flowing through the tower.
  72904   N18, \field Basin Heater Setpoint Temperature
  72905        \type real
  72906        \units C
  72907        \minimum 2.0
  72908        \default 2.0
  72909        \note Enter the outdoor dry-bulb temperature when the basin heater turns on
  72910   A5 , \field Basin Heater Operating Schedule Name
  72911        \type object-list
  72912        \object-list ScheduleNames
  72913        \note Schedule values greater than 0 allow the basin heater to operate whenever the outdoor
  72914        \note air dry-bulb temperature is below the basin heater setpoint temperature.
  72915        \note If a schedule name is not entered, the basin heater is allowed to operate
  72916        \note throughout the entire simulation.
  72917   A6 , \field Evaporation Loss Mode
  72918        \type choice
  72919        \key LossFactor
  72920        \key SaturatedExit
  72921   N19, \field Evaporation Loss Factor
  72922        \type real
  72923        \units percent/K
  72924        \note Rate of water evaporation from the cooling tower and lost to the outdoor air [%/K]
  72925        \note Evaporation loss is calculated as percentage of the circulating condenser water rate
  72926        \note Value entered here is percent-per-degree K of temperature drop in the condenser water
  72927        \note Typical values are from 0.15 to 0.27 [%/K].
  72928        \default 0.2
  72929   N20, \field Drift Loss Percent
  72930        \type real
  72931        \default 0.008
  72932        \units percent
  72933        \note Rate of drift loss as a percentage of circulating condenser water flow rate
  72934        \note Typical values are between 0.002 and 0.2% The default value is 0.008%
  72935   A7 , \field Blowdown Calculation Mode
  72936        \type choice
  72937        \key ConcentrationRatio
  72938        \key ScheduledRate
  72939   N21, \field Blowdown Concentration Ratio
  72940        \type real
  72941        \minimum 2.0
  72942        \default 3.0
  72943        \note Characterizes the rate of blowdown in the cooling tower.
  72944        \note Blowdown is water intentionally drained from the tower in order to offset the build up
  72945        \note of solids in the water that would otherwise occur because of evaporation.
  72946        \note Ratio of solids in the blowdown water to solids in the make up water.
  72947        \note Typical values for tower operation are 3 to 5.  The default value is 3.
  72948   A8 , \field Blowdown Makeup Water Usage Schedule Name
  72949        \type object-list
  72950        \object-list ScheduleNames
  72951        \note Makeup water usage due to blowdown results from occasionally draining a small amount
  72952        \note of water in the tower basin to purge scale or other contaminants to reduce their
  72953        \note concentration in order to maintain an acceptable level of water quality.
  72954        \note Schedule values should reflect water usage in m3/s.
  72955   A9 , \field Supply Water Storage Tank Name
  72956        \type object-list
  72957        \object-list WaterStorageTankNames
  72958   A10, \field Outdoor Air Inlet Node Name
  72959        \type node
  72960        \note Enter the name of an outdoor air node
  72961   A11, \field Capacity Control
  72962        \type choice
  72963        \key FanCycling
  72964        \key FluidBypass
  72965        \default FanCycling
  72966   N22, \field Number of Cells
  72967        \type integer
  72968        \minimum 1
  72969        \default 1
  72970   A12, \field Cell Control
  72971        \type choice
  72972        \key MinimalCell
  72973        \key MaximalCell
  72974        \default MinimalCell
  72975   N23, \field Cell Minimum  Water Flow Rate Fraction
  72976        \type real
  72977        \minimum> 0.0
  72978        \maximum 1.0
  72979        \default 0.33
  72980        \note The allowable minimal fraction of the nominal flow rate per cell
  72981   N24, \field Cell Maximum Water Flow Rate Fraction
  72982        \type real
  72983        \minimum 1
  72984        \default 2.5
  72985        \note The allowable maximal fraction of the nominal flow rate per cell
  72986   N25, \field Sizing Factor
  72987        \note Multiplies the autosized capacity and flow rates
  72988        \type real
  72989        \minimum> 0.0
  72990        \default 1.0
  72991   A13; \field End-Use Subcategory
  72992        \note Any text may be used here to categorize the end-uses in the ABUPS End Uses by Subcategory table.
  72993        \type alpha
  72994        \retaincase
  72995        \default General
