  73226        \type object-list
  73227        \object-list ScheduleNames
  73228        \note Schedule values greater than 0 allow the basin heater to operate whenever the outdoor
  73229        \note air dry-bulb temperature is below the basin heater setpoint temperature.
  73230        \note If a schedule name is not entered, the basin heater is allowed to operate
  73231        \note throughout the entire simulation.
  73232   A6 , \field Evaporation Loss Mode
  73233        \type choice
  73234        \key LossFactor
  73235        \key SaturatedExit
  73236   N27, \field Evaporation Loss Factor
  73237        \type real
  73238        \units percent/K
  73239        \note Rate of water evaporated from the cooling tower and lost to the outdoor air [%/K]
  73240        \note Evaporation loss is calculated as percentage of the circulating condenser water rate
  73241        \note Value entered here is percent-per-degree K of temperature drop in the condenser water
  73242        \note Typical values are from 0.15 to 0.27 [%/K].
  73243        \default 0.2
  73244   N28, \field Drift Loss Percent
  73245        \type real
  73246        \units percent
  73247        \default 0.008
  73248        \note Rate of drift loss as a percentage of circulating condenser water flow rate
  73249        \note Typical values are between 0.002 and 0.2% The default value is 0.008%
  73250   A7 , \field Blowdown Calculation Mode
  73251        \type choice
  73252        \key ConcentrationRatio
  73253        \key ScheduledRate
  73254   N29, \field Blowdown Concentration Ratio
  73255        \type real
  73256        \minimum 2.0
  73257        \default 3.0
  73258        \note Characterizes the rate of blowdown in the cooling tower.
  73259        \note Blowdown is water intentionally drained from the tower in order to offset the build up
  73260        \note of solids in the water that would otherwise occur because of evaporation.
  73261        \note Ratio of solids in the blowdown water to solids in the make up water.
  73262        \note Typical values for tower operation are 3 to 5.  The default value is 3.
  73263   A8 , \field Blowdown Makeup Water Usage Schedule Name
  73264        \type object-list
  73265        \object-list ScheduleNames
  73266        \note Makeup water usage due to blowdown results from occasionally draining some amount
  73267        \note of water in the tower basin to purge scale or other contaminants to reduce their
  73268        \note concentration in order to maintain an acceptable level of water quality.
  73269        \note Schedule values should reflect water usage in m3/s.
  73270   A9 , \field Supply Water Storage Tank Name
  73271        \type object-list
  73272        \object-list WaterStorageTankNames
  73273   A10 , \field Outdoor Air Inlet Node Name
  73274        \type node
  73275        \note Enter the name of an outdoor air node
  73276   N30, \field Number of Cells
  73277        \type integer
  73278        \minimum 1
  73279        \default 1
  73280   A11, \field Cell Control
  73281        \type choice
  73282        \key MinimalCell
  73283        \key MaximalCell
  73284        \default MinimalCell
  73285   N31, \field Cell Minimum  Water Flow Rate Fraction
  73286        \type real
  73287        \minimum> 0.0
  73288        \maximum 1.0
  73289        \default 0.33
  73290        \note The allowable minimal fraction of the nominal flow rate per cell
  73291   N32, \field Cell Maximum Water Flow Rate Fraction
  73292        \type real
  73293        \minimum 1
  73294        \default 2.5
  73295        \note The allowable maximal fraction of the nominal flow rate per cell
  73296   N33, \field Sizing Factor
  73297        \note Multiplies the autosized capacity and flow rates
  73298        \type real
  73299        \minimum> 0.0
  73300        \default 1.0
  73301   A12; \field End-Use Subcategory
  73302        \note Any text may be used here to categorize the end-uses in the ABUPS End Uses by Subcategory table.
  73303        \type alpha
  73304        \retaincase
  73305        \default General
  73306 
  73307 CoolingTower:VariableSpeed:Merkel,
  73308        \min-fields 24
  73309        \memo This tower model is based on Merkel's theory, which is also the basis
  73310        \memo for the tower model in ASHRAE's HVAC1 Toolkit. The open wet cooling tower
  73311        \memo is modeled as a counter flow heat exchanger with a variable-speed fan drawing air
  73312        \memo through the tower (induced-draft configuration).
  73313        \memo For a multi-cell tower, the capacity and air/water flow rate inputs are for the entire tower.
  73314   A1 , \field Name
  73315        \required-field
  73316        \type alpha
  73317        \reference CoolingTowers
  73318        \reference CoolingTowersWithUA
  73319        \note Tower Name
  73320        \reference-class-name validPlantEquipmentTypes
  73321        \reference validPlantEquipmentNames
  73322        \reference-class-name validCondenserEquipmentTypes
  73323        \reference validCondenserEquipmentNames
  73324        \reference-class-name validBranchEquipmentTypes
  73325        \reference validBranchEquipmentNames
  73326   A2 , \field Water Inlet Node Name
  73327        \required-field
  73328        \type node
  73329        \note Name of tower water inlet node
  73330   A3 , \field Water Outlet Node Name
  73331        \required-field
  73332        \type node
  73333        \note Name of tower water outlet node
  73334   A4 , \field Performance Input Method
  73335        \type choice
  73336        \key UFactorTimesAreaAndDesignWaterFlowRate
  73337        \key NominalCapacity
  73338        \default NominalCapacity
  73339        \note User can define tower thermal performance by specifying the tower UA,
  73340        \note the Design Air Flow Rate and the Design Water Flow Rate,
  73341        \note or by specifying the tower nominal capacity
  73342   N1,  \field Heat Rejection Capacity and Nominal Capacity Sizing Ratio
  73343        \type real
  73344        \default 1.25
  73345   N2,  \field Nominal Capacity
  73346        \type real
  73347        \units W
  73348        \minimum> 0.0
  73349        \autosizable
  73350        \note Nominal tower capacity with entering water at 35C (95F), leaving water at
  73351        \note 29.44C (85F), entering air at 25.56C (78F) wet-bulb temperature and 35C (95F)
  73352        \note dry-bulb temperature, with the tower fan operating at Design Air Flow Rate (full speed). Design water
  73353        \note flow rate is as set in Design Water Flow Rate per Unit of Nominal Capacity. Nominal tower capacity
  73354        \note times the Heat Rejection Capacity and Nominal Capacity Sizing Ratio (e.g. 1.25)
  73355        \note gives the actual tower heat rejection at these operating conditions.
  73356   N3,  \field Free Convection Nominal Capacity
  73357        \note required field when performance method is NominalCapacity
  73358        \type real
  73359        \units W
  73360        \minimum 0.0
  73361        \autocalculatable
  73362        \note Tower capacity in free convection regime with entering water at 35C (95F),
  73363        \note leaving water at 29.44C (85F), entering air at 25.56C (78F) wet-bulb temperature
  73364        \note and 35C (95F) dry-bulb temperature. Design water flow rate is as set
  73365        \note  in Design Water Flow Rate per Unit of Nominal Capacity. Tower
  73366        \note free convection capacity times the Heat Rejection Capacity and Nominal Capacity Sizing Ratio
  73367        \note (e.g. 1.25)  gives the actual tower heat rejection at these operating conditions
  73368   N4,  \field Free Convection Nominal Capacity Sizing Factor
  73369        \type real
  73370        \default 0.1
  73371        \minimum> 0.0
  73372        \maximum< 1.0
  73373        \note This field is only used if the previous field is set to autocalculate
  73374   N5 , \field Design Water Flow Rate
  73375        \required-field
  73376        \type real
  73377        \units m3/s
  73378        \minimum> 0.0
  73379        \autosizable
  73380        \ip-units gal/min
  73381   N6 , \field Design Water Flow Rate per Unit of Nominal Capacity
  73382        \note This field is only used if the previous is set to autocalculate and performance input method is NominalCapacity
  73383        \units m3/s-W
  73384        \ip-units (gal/min)/(Btu/h)
  73385        \default 5.382E-8
  73386        \type real
  73387   N7 , \field Design Air Flow Rate
  73388        \note This is the air flow rate at full fan speed
  73389        \required-field
  73390        \type real
  73391        \units m3/s
  73392        \minimum> 0.0
  73393        \autocalculatable
  73394   N8 , \field Design Air Flow Rate Per Unit of Nominal Capacity
  73395        \note This field is only used if the previous is set to autocalculate
  73396        \units m3/s-W
  73397        \default 2.76316E-5
  73398        \type real
  73399        \note When field is left blank the default scaling factor is adjusted for elevation to increase volume flow at altitude
  73400        \note When field has a value the scaling factor is used without adjusting for elevation
  73401   N9 , \field Minimum Air Flow Rate Ratio
  73402        \type real
  73403        \minimum 0.1
  73404        \maximum 0.5
  73405        \default 0.2
  73406        \note Enter the minimum air flow rate ratio. This is typically determined by the variable
  73407        \note speed drive that controls the fan motor speed. Valid entries are from 0.1 to 0.5.
  73408   N10, \field Design Fan Power
  73409        \required-field
  73410        \type real
  73411        \units W
  73412        \minimum> 0.0
  73413        \autocalculatable
  73414        \ip-units W
  73415        \note This is the fan motor electric input power at high speed
  73416   N11, \field Design Fan Power Per Unit of Nominal Capacity
  73417        \note This field is only used if the previous is set to autocalculate
  73418        \note [W/W] Watts of fan power per Watt of tower nominal capacity
  73419        \units dimensionless
  73420        \default 0.0105
  73421        \type real
  73422   A5 , \field Fan Power Modifier Function of Air Flow Rate Ratio Curve Name
  73423        \required-field
  73424        \type object-list
  73425        \object-list UnivariateFunctions
  73426        \note Any curve or table with one independent variable can be used
  73427        \note cubic curve = a + b*AFR + c*AFR**2 + d*AFR**3
  73428        \note quartic curve = a + b*AFR + c*AFR**2 + d*AFR**3 + e*AFR**4
  73429        \note x = AFR = Ratio of current operating air flow rate to Design Air Flow Rate
  73430   N12, \field Free Convection Regime Air Flow Rate
  73431        \type real
  73432        \units m3/s
  73433        \minimum 0.0
  73434        \default 0.0
  73435        \autocalculatable
  73436   N13, \field Free Convection Regime Air Flow Rate Sizing Factor
  73437        \type real
  73438        \default 0.1
  73439        \minimum> 0.0
  73440        \maximum< 1.0
  73441        \note This field is only used if the previous field is set to autocalculate.
  73442   N14, \field Design Air Flow Rate U-Factor Times Area Value
  73443        \note required field when performance method is UFactorTimesAreaAndDesignWaterFlowRate
  73444        \note when performance method is NominalCapacity the program will solve for this UA
  73445        \type real
  73446        \units W/K
  73447        \autosizable
  73448   N15, \field Free Convection Regime U-Factor Times Area Value
  73449        \note required field when performance input method is UFactorTimesAreaAndDesignWaterFlowRate
  73450        \type real
  73451        \units W/K
  73452        \minimum 0.0
  73453        \maximum 300000.0
  73454        \default 0.0
  73455        \autocalculatable
  73456        \note Leave field blank if performance input method is NominalCapacity
  73457   N16, \field Free Convection U-Factor Times Area Value Sizing Factor
  73458        \note required field when performance input method is UFactorTimesAreaAndDesignWaterFlowRate
  73459        \type real
  73460        \default 0.1
  73461        \minimum> 0.0
  73462        \maximum< 1.0
  73463        \note This field is only used if the previous field is set to autocalculate and
  73464        \note the performance input method is UFactorTimesAreaAndDesignWaterFlowRate
  73465   A6 , \field U-Factor Times Area Modifier Function of Air Flow Ratio Curve Name
  73466        \required-field
  73467        \note This curve describes how tower's design UA changes with variable air flow rate
  73468        \type object-list
  73469        \object-list UnivariateFunctions
  73470        \note Any curve or table with one independent variable can be used
  73471        \note cubic curve = a + b*AFR + c*AFR**2 + d*AFR**3
  73472        \note quartic curve = a + b*AFR + c*AFR**2 + d*AFR**3 + e*AFR**4
  73473        \note x = AFR = Ratio of current operating air flow rate to Design Air Flow Rate
  73474   A7 , \field U-Factor Times Area Modifier Function of Wetbulb Temperature Difference Curve Name
  73475        \required-field
  73476        \note curve describes how tower UA changes with outdoor air wet-bulb temperature difference from design wet-bulb
  73477        \type object-list
  73478        \object-list UnivariateFunctions
  73479        \note Any curve or table with one independent variable can be used
  73480        \note cubic curve = a + b*DeltaWB + c*DeltaWB**2 + d*DeltaWB**3
  73481        \note quartic curve = a + b*DeltaWB + c*DeltaWB**2 + d*DeltaWB**3 + e*DeltaWB**4
  73482        \note x = DeltaWB = (design wet-bulb temperature in C - current wet-bulb temperature in C)
  73483        \note where design wet-bulb temperature of entering air is 25.56C (78F)
  73484   A8 , \field U-Factor Times Area Modifier Function of Water Flow Ratio Curve Name
  73485        \required-field
  73486        \note curve describes how tower UA changes with the flow rate of condenser water through the tower
  73487        \type object-list
  73488        \object-list UnivariateFunctions
  73489        \note Any curve or table with one independent variable can be used
  73490        \note cubic curve = a + b*WFR + c*WFR**2 + d*WFR**3
  73491        \note quartic curve = a + b*WFR + c*WFR**2 + d*WFR**3 + e*WFR**4
  73492        \note x = WFR = Ratio of current operating water flow rate to Design Water Flow Rate
  73493   N17, \field Design Inlet Air Dry-Bulb Temperature
  73494        \type real
  73495        \units C
  73496        \default 35.0
  73497        \minimum 20.0
  73498        \note Enter the tower's design inlet air dry-bulb temperature
  73499   N18, \field Design Inlet Air Wet-Bulb Temperature
  73500        \type real
  73501        \units C
  73502        \default 25.6
  73503        \minimum 20.0
  73504        \note Enter the tower's design inlet air wet-bulb temperature
  73505   N19, \field Design Approach Temperature
  73506        \type real
  73507        \units deltaC
  73508        \autosizable
  73509        \default autosize
  73510        \minimum> 0
  73511        \note Enter the approach temperature corresponding to the design inlet air
  73512        \note wet-bulb temperature and design range temperature.
  73513        \note Design approach temp = outlet water temperature minus inlet air wet-bulb temperature
  73514        \note at design conditions. Autosized to 3.9 deltaC.
  73515   N20, \field Design Range Temperature
  73516        \type real
  73517        \units deltaC
  73518        \autosizable
  73519        \default autosize
  73520        \minimum> 0
  73521        \note Enter the range temperature corresponding to the design inlet air
  73522        \note wet-bulb temperature and design approach temperature.
  73523        \note Design range = inlet water temperature minus outlet water temperature
  73524        \note at design conditions. Autosized to 5.5 deltaC.
  73525   N21, \field Basin Heater Capacity
  73526        \type real
  73527        \units W/K
  73528        \minimum 0.0
  73529        \default 0.0
  73530        \note This heater maintains the basin water temperature at the basin heater setpoint
  73531        \note temperature when the outdoor air temperature falls below the setpoint temperature.
  73532        \note The basin heater only operates when water is not flowing through the tower.
  73533   N22, \field Basin Heater Setpoint Temperature
  73534        \type real
  73535        \units C
  73536        \minimum 2.0
  73537        \default 2.0
  73538        \note Enter the outdoor dry-bulb temperature when the basin heater turns on
  73539   A9 , \field Basin Heater Operating Schedule Name
  73540        \type object-list
  73541        \object-list ScheduleNames
  73542        \note Schedule values greater than 0 allow the basin heater to operate whenever the outdoor
  73543        \note air dry-bulb temperature is below the basin heater setpoint temperature.
  73544        \note If a schedule name is not entered, the basin heater is allowed to operate
  73545        \note throughout the entire simulation.
  73546   A10, \field Evaporation Loss Mode
  73547        \type choice
  73548        \key LossFactor
  73549        \key SaturatedExit
  73550   N23, \field Evaporation Loss Factor
  73551        \type real
  73552        \units percent/K
  73553        \note Rate of water evaporated from the cooling tower and lost to the outdoor air [%/K]
  73554        \note Evaporation loss is calculated as percentage of the circulating condenser water rate
  73555        \note Value entered here is percent-per-degree K of temperature drop in the condenser water
  73556        \note Typical values are from 0.15 to 0.27 [%/K].
  73557        \default 0.2
  73558   N24, \field Drift Loss Percent
  73559        \type real
  73560        \units percent
  73561        \default 0.008
  73562        \note Rate of drift loss as a percentage of circulating condenser water flow rate
  73563        \note Typical values are between 0.002 and 0.2% The default value is 0.008%
  73564   A11 , \field Blowdown Calculation Mode
  73565        \type choice
  73566        \key ConcentrationRatio
  73567        \key ScheduledRate
  73568   N25, \field Blowdown Concentration Ratio
  73569        \type real
  73570        \minimum 2.0
  73571        \default 3.0
  73572        \note Characterizes the rate of blowdown in the cooling tower.
  73573        \note Blowdown is water intentionally drained from the tower in order to offset the build up
  73574        \note of solids in the water that would otherwise occur because of evaporation.
  73575        \note Ratio of solids in the blowdown water to solids in the make up water.
  73576        \note Typical values for tower operation are 3 to 5.  The default value is 3.
  73577   A12, \field Blowdown Makeup Water Usage Schedule Name
  73578        \type object-list
  73579        \object-list ScheduleNames
  73580        \note Makeup water usage due to blowdown results from occasionally draining some amount
  73581        \note of water in the tower basin to purge scale or other contaminants to reduce their
  73582        \note concentration in order to maintain an acceptable level of water quality.
  73583        \note Schedule values should reflect water usage in m3/s.
  73584   A13, \field Supply Water Storage Tank Name
  73585        \type object-list
  73586        \object-list WaterStorageTankNames
  73587   A14, \field Outdoor Air Inlet Node Name
  73588        \type node
  73589        \note Enter the name of an outdoor air node
  73590   N26, \field Number of Cells
  73591        \type integer
  73592        \minimum 1
  73593        \default 1
  73594   A15, \field Cell Control
  73595        \type choice
  73596        \key MinimalCell
  73597        \key MaximalCell
  73598        \default MinimalCell
  73599   N27, \field Cell Minimum  Water Flow Rate Fraction
  73600        \type real
  73601        \minimum> 0.0
  73602        \maximum 1.0
  73603        \default 0.33
  73604        \note The allowable minimal fraction of the nominal flow rate per cell
  73605   N28, \field Cell Maximum Water Flow Rate Fraction
  73606        \type real
  73607        \minimum 1
  73608        \default 2.5
  73609        \note The allowable maximal fraction of the nominal flow rate per cell
  73610   N29, \field Sizing Factor
  73611        \note Multiplies the autosized capacity and flow rates
  73612        \type real
  73613        \minimum> 0.0
  73614        \default 1.0
  73615   A16; \field End-Use Subcategory
  73616        \note Any text may be used here to categorize the end-uses in the ABUPS End Uses by Subcategory table.
  73617        \type alpha
  73618        \retaincase
  73619        \default General
  73620 
  73621 CoolingTower:VariableSpeed,
  73622        \min-fields 15
  73623        \memo This open wet tower model is based on purely empirical algorithms derived from manufacturer's
  73624        \memo performance data or field measurements. The user can select from two existing
  73625        \memo algorithms (CoolTools or YorkCalc), or they can enter their own correlation for
  73626        \memo approach temperature by using a variable speed tower model coefficient object.
  73627        \memo For a multi-cell tower, the capacity and air/water flow rate inputs are for the entire tower.
  73628   A1 , \field Name
  73629        \required-field
  73630        \type alpha
  73631        \reference CoolingTowers
  73632        \note Tower Name
  73633        \reference-class-name validPlantEquipmentTypes
  73634        \reference validPlantEquipmentNames
  73635        \reference-class-name validCondenserEquipmentTypes
  73636        \reference validCondenserEquipmentNames
  73637        \reference-class-name validBranchEquipmentTypes
  73638        \reference validBranchEquipmentNames
  73639   A2 , \field Water Inlet Node Name
  73640        \required-field
  73641        \type node
  73642        \note Name of tower water inlet node
  73643   A3 , \field Water Outlet Node Name
  73644        \required-field
  73645        \type node
  73646        \note Name of tower water outlet node
  73647   A4 , \field Model Type
  73648        \type choice
  73649        \key CoolToolsCrossFlow
  73650        \key CoolToolsUserDefined
  73651        \key YorkCalc
  73652        \key YorkCalcUserDefined
  73653        \default YorkCalc
  73654        \note Determines the coefficients and form of the equation for calculating
  73655        \note approach temperature
  73656   A5 , \field Model Coefficient Name
  73657        \type object-list
  73658        \object-list VariableSpeedTowerCoefficient
  73659        \note Name of the tower model coefficient object.
  73660        \note Used only when tower Model Type is either CoolToolsUserDefined or YorkCalcUserDefined.
  73661   N1 , \field Design Inlet Air Wet-Bulb Temperature
  73662        \type real
  73663        \units C
  73664        \default 25.6
  73665        \minimum 20.0
  73666        \note Enter the tower's design inlet air wet-bulb temperature
  73667   N2 , \field Design Approach Temperature
  73668        \type real
  73669        \units deltaC
  73670        \default 3.9
  73671        \minimum> 0
  73672        \note Enter the approach temperature corresponding to the design inlet air
  73673        \note wet-bulb temperature and design range temperature.
  73674        \note Design approach temp = outlet water temperature minus inlet air wet-bulb temperature
  73675        \note at design conditions.
  73676   N3 , \field Design Range Temperature
  73677        \type real
  73678        \units deltaC
  73679        \default 5.6
  73680        \minimum> 0
  73681        \note Enter the range temperature corresponding to the design inlet air
  73682        \note wet-bulb temperature and design approach temperature.
  73683        \note Design range = inlet water temperature minus outlet water temperature
  73684        \note at design conditions.
  73685   N4 , \field Design Water Flow Rate
  73686        \required-field
  73687        \type real
  73688        \units m3/s
  73689        \minimum> 0.0
  73690        \autosizable
  73691        \ip-units gal/min
  73692        \note Water flow rate through the tower at design conditions
  73693   N5 , \field Design Air Flow Rate
  73694        \required-field
  73695        \type real
  73696        \units m3/s
  73697        \minimum> 0.0
  73698        \autosizable
  73699        \note Design (maximum) air flow rate through the tower
  73700   N6 , \field Design Fan Power
  73701        \required-field
  73702        \type real
  73703        \units W
  73704        \minimum> 0.0
  73705        \autosizable
  73706        \ip-units W
  73707        \note Enter the fan motor electric input power at design (max) air flow through the tower
  73708        \note Standard conversion for horsepower is 1 HP = 745.7 W
  73709   A6 , \field Fan Power Ratio Function of Air Flow Rate Ratio Curve Name
  73710        \type object-list
  73711        \object-list UnivariateFunctions
  73712        \note FPR = a + b*AFR + c*AFR**2 + d*AFR**3
  73713        \note FPR = fraction of the design fan power
  73714        \note AFR = fraction of the design air flow rate
  73715        \note If left blank, then fan power is assumed to be proportional to
  73716        \note (air flow rate ratio)^3
  73717   N7 , \field Minimum Air Flow Rate Ratio
  73718        \type real
  73719        \minimum 0.2
  73720        \maximum 0.5
  73721        \default 0.2
  73722        \note Enter the minimum air flow rate ratio. This is typically determined by the variable
  73723        \note speed drive that controls the fan motor speed. Valid entries are from 0.2 to 0.5.
  73724   N8 , \field Fraction of Tower Capacity in Free Convection Regime
  73725        \type real
  73726        \minimum 0.0
  73727        \maximum 0.2
  73728        \default 0.125
  73729        \note Enter the fraction of tower capacity in the free convection regime. This is the
  73730        \note fraction of the tower capacity, at the current inlet air wet-bulb temperature,
  73731        \note that is available when the tower fan is off. Manufacturers typically estimate the
  73732        \note free convection capacity at approximately 10-15%. Values are entered as a fraction
  73733        \note and can range from 0 to 0.2.
  73734   N9 , \field Basin Heater Capacity
  73735        \type real
  73736        \units W/K
  73737        \minimum 0.0
  73738        \default 0.0
  73739        \note This heater maintains the basin water temperature at the basin heater setpoint
  73740        \note temperature when the outdoor air temperature falls below the setpoint temperature.
  73741        \note The basin heater only operates when water is not flowing through the tower.
  73742   N10, \field Basin Heater Setpoint Temperature
  73743        \type real
  73744        \units C
  73745        \minimum 2.0
  73746        \default 2.0
  73747        \note Enter the outdoor dry-bulb temperature when the basin heater turns on
  73748   A7 , \field Basin Heater Operating Schedule Name
  73749        \type object-list
  73750        \object-list ScheduleNames
  73751        \note Schedule values greater than 0 allow the basin heater to operate whenever the outdoor
  73752        \note air dry-bulb temperature is below the basin heater setpoint temperature.
  73753        \note If a schedule name is not entered, the basin heater is allowed to operate
  73754        \note throughout the entire simulation.
  73755   A8 , \field Evaporation Loss Mode
  73756        \type choice
  73757        \key LossFactor
  73758        \key SaturatedExit
  73759   N11, \field Evaporation Loss Factor
  73760        \type real
  73761        \units percent/K
  73762        \note Rate of water evaporated from the cooling tower and lost to the outdoor air [%/K]
  73763        \note Evaporation loss is calculated as percentage of the circulating condenser water rate
  73764        \note Value entered here is percent-per-degree K of temperature drop in the condenser water
  73765        \note Typical values are from 0.15 to 0.27 [percent/K].
  73766        \default 0.2
  73767   N12, \field Drift Loss Percent
  73768        \type real
  73769        \units percent
  73770        \note Rate of drift loss as a percentage of circulating condenser water flow rate
  73771        \note Typical values are between 0.002 and 0.2% The default value is 0.008%
  73772   A9 , \field Blowdown Calculation Mode
  73773        \type choice
  73774        \key ConcentrationRatio
  73775        \key ScheduledRate
  73776   N13, \field Blowdown Concentration Ratio
  73777        \type real
  73778        \minimum 2.0
  73779        \default 3.0
  73780        \note Characterizes the rate of blowdown in the cooling tower.
  73781        \note Blowdown is water intentionally drained from the tower in order to offset the build up
  73782        \note of solids in the water that would otherwise occur because of evaporation.
  73783        \note Ratio of solids in the blowdown water to solids in the make up water.
  73784        \note Typical values for tower operation are 3 to 5.  The default value is 3.
  73785   A10, \field Blowdown Makeup Water Usage Schedule Name
  73786        \type object-list
  73787        \object-list ScheduleNames
  73788        \note Makeup water usage due to blowdown results from occasionally draining a small amount
  73789        \note of water in the tower basin to purge scale or other contaminants to reduce their
  73790        \note concentration in order to maintain an acceptable level of water quality.
  73791        \note Schedule values should reflect water usage in m3/s.
  73792   A11, \field Supply Water Storage Tank Name
  73793        \type object-list
  73794        \object-list WaterStorageTankNames
  73795   A12, \field Outdoor Air Inlet Node Name
  73796        \type node
  73797        \note Enter the name of an outdoor air node
  73798   N14, \field Number of Cells
  73799        \type integer
  73800        \minimum 1
  73801        \default 1
  73802   A13, \field Cell Control
  73803        \type choice
  73804        \key MinimalCell
  73805        \key MaximalCell
  73806        \default MinimalCell
  73807   N15, \field Cell Minimum  Water Flow Rate Fraction
  73808        \type real
  73809        \minimum> 0.0
  73810        \maximum 1.0
  73811        \default 0.33
  73812        \note The allowable minimal fraction of the nominal flow rate per cell
  73813   N16, \field Cell Maximum Water Flow Rate Fraction
  73814        \type real
  73815        \minimum 1
  73816        \default 2.5
  73817        \note The allowable maximal fraction of the nominal flow rate per cell
  73818   N17, \field Sizing Factor
  73819        \note Multiplies the autosized capacity and flow rates
  73820        \type real
  73821        \minimum> 0.0
  73822        \default 1.0
  73823   A14; \field End-Use Subcategory
  73824        \note Any text may be used here to categorize the end-uses in the ABUPS End Uses by Subcategory table.
  73825        \type alpha
  73826        \retaincase
  73827        \default General
  73828 
