  74128 EvaporativeFluidCooler:SingleSpeed,
  74129        \min-fields 10
  74130        \memo This model is based on Merkel's theory, which is also the basis
  74131        \memo for the cooling tower model in EnergyPlus. The Evaporative fluid cooler
  74132        \memo is modeled as a counter flow heat exchanger.
  74133   A1 , \field Name
  74134        \required-field
  74135        \type alpha
  74136        \note Fluid Cooler Name
  74137        \reference-class-name validPlantEquipmentTypes
  74138        \reference validPlantEquipmentNames
  74139        \reference-class-name validCondenserEquipmentTypes
  74140        \reference validCondenserEquipmentNames
  74141        \reference-class-name validBranchEquipmentTypes
  74142        \reference validBranchEquipmentNames
  74143   A2 , \field Water Inlet Node Name
  74144        \required-field
  74145        \type node
  74146        \note Name of Fluid Cooler water inlet node
  74147   A3 , \field Water Outlet Node Name
  74148        \required-field
  74149        \type node
  74150        \note Name of Fluid Cooler water outlet node
  74151   N1 , \field Design Air Flow Rate
  74152        \required-field
  74153        \type real
  74154        \units m3/s
  74155        \minimum> 0.0
  74156        \autosizable
  74157   N2 , \field Design Air Flow Rate Fan Power
  74158        \required-field
  74159        \type real
  74160        \units W
  74161        \minimum> 0.0
  74162        \autosizable
  74163        \ip-units W
  74164        \note This is the fan motor electric input power
  74165   N3 , \field Design Spray Water Flow Rate
  74166        \required-field
  74167        \type real
  74168        \units m3/s
  74169        \minimum> 0.0
  74170        \ip-units gal/min
  74171   A4 , \field Performance Input Method
  74172        \type choice
  74173        \key UFactorTimesAreaAndDesignWaterFlowRate
  74174        \key StandardDesignCapacity
  74175        \key UserSpecifiedDesignCapacity
  74176        \note User can define fluid cooler thermal performance by specifying the fluid cooler UA
  74177        \note and the Design Water Flow Rate, or by specifying the fluid cooler Standard Design
  74178        \note Capacity or by specifying Design Capacity for Non standard conditions.
  74179   A5 , \field Outdoor Air Inlet Node Name
  74180        \type node
  74181        \note Enter the name of an outdoor air node
  74182   N4 , \field Heat Rejection Capacity and Nominal Capacity Sizing Ratio
  74183        \type real
  74184        \default 1.25
  74185   N5 , \field Standard Design Capacity
  74186        \type real
  74187        \units W
  74188        \minimum> 0.0
  74189        \note Standard design capacity with entering water at 35C (95F), leaving water at
  74190        \note 29.44C (85F), entering air at 25.56C (78F) wet-bulb temperature and 35C (95F)
  74191        \note dry-bulb temperature. Design water flow rate assumed to be 5.382E-8 m3/s per watt
  74192        \note (3 gpm/ton). Standard design capacity times the Heat Rejection Capacity and
  74193        \note Nominal Capacity Sizing Ratio (e.g. 1.25) gives the actual fluid cooler
  74194        \note heat rejection at these operating conditions.
  74195        \note Only used for Performance Input Method = StandardDesignCapacity;
  74196        \note for other input methods, this field is ignored.
  74197        \note The standard conditions mentioned above for Standard design capacity are already
  74198        \note specified in the EnergyPlus. So the input fields such as design entering water
  74199        \note temp., design entering air wet-bulb and dry-bulb temp. and design water flow rate, if
  74200        \note provided in the input, will be ignored for the StandardDesignCapacity performance input
  74201        \note method. Also, the standard conditions are for water as a fluid type so this performance input
  74202        \note method can only be used with water as a fluid type (as specified in CondenserLoop object).
  74203   N6 , \field Design Air Flow Rate U-factor Times Area Value
  74204        \type real
  74205        \units W/K
  74206        \minimum> 0.0
  74207        \maximum 2100000.0
  74208        \autosizable
  74209        \note Only used for Performance Input Method = UFactorTimesAreaAndDesignWaterFlowRate;
  74210        \note for other Performance Input Methods, this field is ignored.
  74211   N7 , \field Design Water Flow Rate
  74212        \type real
  74213        \units m3/s
  74214        \minimum> 0.0
  74215        \autosizable
  74216        \ip-units gal/min
  74217        \note Input value is ignored if fluid cooler Performance Input Method= StandardDesignCapacity.
  74218   N8 , \field User Specified Design Capacity
  74219        \type real
  74220        \units W
  74221        \minimum> 0.0
  74222        \note Only used for Performance Input Method = UserSpecifiedDesignCapacity;
  74223        \note for other Performance Input Methods, this field is ignored.
  74224   N9 , \field Design Entering Water Temperature
  74225        \type real
  74226        \units C
  74227        \minimum> 0.0
  74228        \ip-units F
  74229        \note Only used for Performance Input Method = UserSpecifiedDesignCapacity;
  74230        \note for other Performance Input Methods, this field is ignored.
  74231        \note Design Entering Water Temperature must be greater than Design Entering Air Temperature.
  74232   N10, \field Design Entering Air Temperature
  74233        \type real
  74234        \units C
  74235        \minimum> 0.0
  74236        \ip-units F
  74237        \note Only used for Performance Input Method = UserSpecifiedDesignCapacity;
  74238        \note for other Performance Input Methods, this field is ignored.
  74239        \note Design Entering Air Temperature must be greater than Design Entering Air Wet-bulb
  74240        \note Temperature.
  74241   N11, \field Design Entering Air Wet-bulb Temperature
  74242        \type real
  74243        \units C
  74244        \minimum> 0.0
  74245        \ip-units F
  74246        \note Only used for Performance Input Method = UserSpecifiedDesignCapacity;
  74247        \note for other Performance Input Methods, this field is ignored.
  74248        \note Design Entering Air Wet-bulb Temperature must be less than Design Entering Air
  74249        \note Temperature.
  74250   A6 , \field Capacity Control
  74251        \type choice
  74252        \key FanCycling
  74253        \key FluidBypass
  74254        \default FanCycling
  74255   N12, \field Sizing Factor
  74256        \note Multiplies the autosized capacity and flow rates
  74257        \type real
  74258        \minimum> 0.0
  74259        \default 1.0
  74260   A7 , \field Evaporation Loss Mode
  74261        \type choice
  74262        \key LossFactor
  74263        \key SaturatedExit
  74264        \default SaturatedExit
  74265   N13, \field Evaporation Loss Factor
  74266        \type real
  74267        \units percent/K
  74268        \note Rate of water evaporation from the Fluid Cooler and lost to the outdoor air [%/K]
  74269        \note Empirical correlation is used to calculate default loss factor if it not explicitly provided.
  74270   N14, \field Drift Loss Percent
  74271        \type real
  74272        \default 0.008
  74273        \units percent
  74274        \note Rate of drift loss as a percentage of circulating spray water flow rate
  74275        \note Default value for this field is under investigation. For now Cooling tower's drift loss
  74276        \note percent default value is taken here.
  74277   A8 , \field Blowdown Calculation Mode
  74278        \type choice
  74279        \key ConcentrationRatio
  74280        \key ScheduledRate
  74281        \default ConcentrationRatio
  74282   N15, \field Blowdown Concentration Ratio
  74283        \type real
  74284        \minimum 2.0
  74285        \default 3.0
  74286        \note Characterizes the rate of blowdown in the Evaporative Fluid Cooler.
  74287        \note Blowdown is water intentionally drained from the basin in order to offset the build
  74288        \note up of solids in the water that would otherwise occur because of evaporation.
  74289        \note Ratio of solids in the blowdown water to solids in the make up water.
  74290        \note Default value for this field is under investigation. For now Cooling tower's
  74291        \note Blowdown Concentration Ratio percent default value is taken here.
  74292   A9 , \field Blowdown Makeup Water Usage Schedule Name
  74293        \type object-list
  74294        \object-list ScheduleNames
  74295        \note Makeup water usage due to blowdown results from occasionally draining a small
  74296        \note amount of water in the Fluid Cooler basin to purge scale or other contaminants to
  74297        \note reduce their concentration in order to maintain an acceptable level of water quality.
  74298        \note Schedule values should reflect water usage in m3/s.
  74299   A10; \field Supply Water Storage Tank Name
  74300        \type object-list
  74301        \object-list WaterStorageTankNames
  74302 
  74303 EvaporativeFluidCooler:TwoSpeed,
