  74382        \type real
  74383        \default 1.25
  74384   N9 , \field High Speed Standard Design Capacity
  74385        \type real
  74386        \units W
  74387        \minimum> 0.0
  74388        \note Standard design capacity with entering water at 35C (95F), leaving water at
  74389        \note 29.44C (85F), entering air at 25.56C (78F) wet-bulb temperature and 35C (95F)
  74390        \note dry-bulb temperature. Design water flow rate assumed to be 5.382E-8 m3/s per watt
  74391        \note (3 gpm/ton). Standard design capacity times the Heat Rejection Capacity and
  74392        \note Nominal Capacity Sizing Ratio (e.g. 1.25) gives the actual fluid cooler
  74393        \note heat rejection at these operating conditions.
  74394        \note Only used for Performance Input Method = StandardDesignCapacity;
  74395        \note for other input methods, this field is ignored.
  74396        \note The standard conditions mentioned above for Standard design capacity are already
  74397        \note specified in the EnergyPlus. So the input fields such as design entering water
  74398        \note temp., design entering air wet-bulb and dry-bulb temp. and design water flow rate, if
  74399        \note provided in the input, will be ignored for the StandardDesignCapacity performance input
  74400        \note method. Also, the standard conditions are for water as a fluid type so this performance input
  74401        \note method can only be used with water as a fluid type (as specified in CondenserLoop object).
  74402   N10 , \field Low Speed Standard Design Capacity
  74403        \type real
  74404        \units W
  74405        \minimum> 0.0
  74406        \autocalculatable
  74407        \note Standard design capacity with entering water at 35C (95F), leaving water at
  74408        \note 29.44C (85F), entering air at 25.56C (78F) wet-bulb temperature and 35C (95F)
  74409        \note dry-bulb temperature. Design water flow rate assumed to be 5.382E-8 m3/s per watt
  74410        \note (3 gpm/ton). Standard design capacity times the Heat Rejection Capacity and
  74411        \note Nominal Capacity Sizing Ratio (e.g. 1.25) gives the actual fluid cooler
  74412        \note heat rejection at these operating conditions.
  74413        \note Only used for Performance Input Method = StandardDesignCapacity;
  74414        \note for other input methods, this field is ignored.
  74415        \note The standard conditions mentioned above for Standard design capacity are already
  74416        \note specified in the EnergyPlus. So the input fields such as design entering water
  74417        \note temp., design entering air wet-bulb and dry-bulb temp. and design water flow rate, if
  74418        \note provided in the input, will be ignored for the StandardDesignCapacity performance input
  74419        \note method. Also, the standard conditions are for water as a fluid type so this performance input
  74420        \note method can only be used with water as a fluid type (as specified in CondenserLoop object).
  74421   N11, \field Low Speed Standard Capacity Sizing Factor
  74422        \type real
  74423        \default 0.5
