  74523        \type real
  74524        \minimum 2.0
  74525        \default 3.0
  74526        \note Characterizes the rate of blowdown in the Evaporative Fluid Cooler.
  74527        \note Blowdown is water intentionally drained from the Evaporative Fluid Cooler in order to offset the
  74528        \note build up of solids in the water that would otherwise occur because of evaporation.
  74529        \note Ratio of solids in the blowdown water to solids in the make up water.
  74530        \note Default value is under investigation. For now cooling tower's default value is taken.
  74531   A8 , \field Blowdown Makeup Water Usage Schedule Name
  74532        \type object-list
  74533        \object-list ScheduleNames
  74534        \note Makeup water usage due to blowdown results from occasionally draining some amount
  74535        \note of water in the Evaporative Fluid Cooler basin to purge scale or other contaminants to reduce
  74536        \note their concentration in order to maintain an acceptable level of water quality.
  74537        \note Schedule values should reflect water usage in m3/s.
  74538   A9 ; \field Supply Water Storage Tank Name
  74539        \type object-list
  74540        \object-list WaterStorageTankNames
