  77617        \default 0.0
  77618   N5,  \field Temperature Sensor Height
  77619        \units m
  77620        \minimum 0.0
  77621   N6 , \field Minimum Temperature Limit
  77622        \type real
  77623        \units C
  77624   N7 , \field Nominal Cooling Capacity
  77625        \type real
  77626        \units W
  77627   A4 , \field Ambient Temperature Indicator
  77628        \required-field
  77629        \type choice
  77630        \key Schedule
  77631        \key Zone
  77632        \key Outdoors
  77633   A5 , \field Ambient Temperature Schedule Name
  77634        \type object-list
  77635        \object-list ScheduleNames
  77636   A6 , \field Ambient Temperature Zone Name
  77637        \type object-list
  77638        \object-list ZoneNames
  77639   A7 , \field Ambient Temperature Outdoor Air Node Name
  77640        \type node
  77641        \note required for Ambient Temperature Indicator=Outdoors
  77642   N8, \field Uniform Skin Loss Coefficient per Unit Area to Ambient Temperature
  77643        \type real
  77644        \units W/m2-K
  77645        \minimum 0.0
  77646   A8 , \field Use Side Inlet Node Name
  77647        \type node
  77648   A9, \field Use Side Outlet Node Name
  77649        \type node
  77650   N9 , \field Use Side Heat Transfer Effectiveness
  77651        \type real
  77652        \minimum 0.0
  77653        \maximum 1.0
  77654        \default 1.0
  77655        \note The use side effectiveness in the stratified tank model is a simplified analogy of
  77656        \note a heat exchanger's effectiveness. This effectiveness is equal to the fraction of
  77657        \note use mass flow rate that directly mixes with the tank fluid. And one minus the
  77658        \note effectiveness is the fraction that bypasses the tank. The use side mass flow rate
  77659        \note that bypasses the tank is mixed with the fluid or water leaving the stratified tank.
  77660   A10, \field Use Side Availability Schedule Name
