  77691        \minimum> 0.0
  77692        \maximum 1.0
  77693        \default 1.0
  77694        \note The source side effectiveness in the stratified tank model is a simplified analogy of
  77695        \note a heat exchanger's effectiveness. This effectiveness is equal to the fraction of
  77696        \note source mass flow rate that directly mixes with the tank fluid. And one minus the
  77697        \note effectiveness is the fraction that bypasses the tank. The source side mass flow rate
  77698        \note that bypasses the tank is mixed with the fluid or water leaving the stratified tank.
  77699   A13, \field Source Side Availability Schedule Name
  77700        \note Availability schedule name for use side. Schedule value > 0 means the system is available.
  77701        \note If this field is blank, the system is always available.
  77702        \type object-list
  77703        \object-list ScheduleNames
  77704   N14, \field Source Side Inlet Height
  77705        \type real
