  80795 \group External Interface
  80796 
  80797 ExternalInterface,
  80798         \memo This object activates the external interface of EnergyPlus. If the object
  80799         \memo ExternalInterface is present, then all ExtnernalInterface:* objects will receive
  80800         \memo their values from the BCVTB interface or from FMUs at each zone time step.
  80801         \memo If this object is not present, then the values of these objects will be fixed at the
  80802         \memo value declared in the "initial value" field of the corresponding object, and a
  80803         \memo warning will be written to the EnergyPlus error file.
  80804    A1;  \field Name of External Interface
  80805         \note Name of External Interface
  80806         \required-field
  80807         \type choice
  80808         \key PtolemyServer
  80809         \key FunctionalMockupUnitImport
  80810         \key FunctionalMockupUnitExport
  80811         \note Currently, the only valid entries are PtolemyServer, FunctionalMockupUnitImport, and FunctionalMockupUnitExport.
  80812 
  80813 ExternalInterface:Schedule,
  80814        \min-fields 3
  80815        \memo A ExternalInterface:Schedule contains only one value,
  80816        \memo which is used during the warm-up period and the system sizing.
  80817   A1 , \field Name
  80818        \required-field
  80819        \type alpha
  80820        \reference ScheduleNames
  80821   A2 , \field Schedule Type Limits Name
  80822        \type object-list
  80823        \object-list ScheduleTypeLimitsNames
  80824   N1 ; \field Initial Value
  80825        \type real
  80826        \required-field
  80827        \note Used during warm-up and system sizing.
  80828 
  80829 ExternalInterface:Variable,
  80830        \memo This input object is similar to EnergyManagementSystem:GlobalVariable. However, at
  80831        \memo the beginning of each zone time step, its value is set to the value received from the
  80832        \memo external interface. During the warm-up period and the system sizing, its value
  80833        \memo is set to the value specified by the field "initial value." This object can be used
  80834        \memo to move data into Erl subroutines.
  80835   A1 , \field Name
  80836        \required-field
  80837        \type alpha
  80838        \note This name becomes a variable for use in Erl programs
  80839        \note no spaces allowed in name
  80840   N1 ; \field Initial Value
  80841        \type real
  80842        \required-field
  80843        \note Used during warm-up and system sizing.
  80844 
  80845 ExternalInterface:Actuator,
  80846        \memo Hardware portion of EMS used to set up actuators in the model
  80847        \min-fields 4
  80848   A1 , \field Name
  80849        \required-field
  80850        \type alpha
  80851        \note This name becomes a variable for use in Erl programs
  80852        \note no spaces allowed in name
  80853   A2 , \field Actuated Component Unique Name
  80854        \required-field
  80855        \type alpha
  80856   A3 , \field Actuated Component Type
  80857        \required-field
  80858        \type alpha
  80859   A4 , \field Actuated Component Control Type
  80860        \required-field
  80861        \type alpha
  80862   N1 ; \field Optional Initial Value
  80863        \type real
  80864        \note If specified, it is used during warm-up and system sizing.
  80865        \note If not specified, then the actuator only overwrites the
  80866        \note actuated component after the warm-up and system sizing.
  80867 
