  81693 AvailabilityManager:NightVentilation,
  81694        \min-fields 7
  81695        \memo depending on zone and outdoor conditions overrides fan schedule to do
  81696        \memo precooling with outdoor air
  81697   A1 , \field Name
  81698        \required-field
  81699        \type alpha
  81700        \reference SystemAvailabilityManagers
  81701   A2 , \field Applicability Schedule Name
  81702        \required-field
  81703        \type object-list
  81704        \object-list ScheduleNames
  81705   A3 , \field Fan Schedule Name
  81706        \required-field
  81707        \type object-list
  81708        \object-list ScheduleNames
  81709   A4 , \field Ventilation Temperature Schedule Name
  81710        \type object-list
  81711        \object-list ScheduleNames
  81712        \note One zone temperature must be above this scheduled temperature
  81713        \note for night ventilation to be enabled
  81714   N1 , \field Ventilation Temperature Difference
  81715        \units deltaC
  81716        \default 2.0
  81717        \note The outdoor air temperature minus the control zone temperature
  81718        \note must be greater than the ventilation delta T
  81719   N2 , \field Ventilation Temperature Low Limit
  81720        \units C
  81721        \default 15.
  81722        \note Night ventilation is disabled if any conditioned zone served by
  81723        \note the system falls below this temperature
  81724   N3 , \field Night Venting Flow Fraction
  81725        \minimum 0.0
  81726        \default 1.
  81727        \note the fraction (could be > 1) of the design system Flow Rate at which
  81728        \note night ventilation will be done
  81729   A5 ; \field Control Zone Name
  81730        \type object-list
  81731        \object-list ZoneNames
  81732        \required-field
  81733        \note When AvailabilityManager:NightVentilation is used in the zone component availability
  81734        \note manager assignment list, the Control Zone Name should be the name of the zone in which the
  81735        \note zone component is.
  81736 
  81737 AvailabilityManager:HybridVentilation,
  81738        \min-fields 13
  81739        \memo Depending on zone and outdoor conditions overrides window/door opening controls
  81740        \memo to maximize natural ventilation and turn off an HVAC system when ventilation control
  81741        \memo conditions are met.
  81742        \memo This object (zone ventilation object name) has not been instrumented to work with
  81743        \memo global Zone or Zone List names option for Ventilation:DesignFlowRate.  In order to
  81744        \memo use, you must enter the single <Ventilation:DesignFlowRate> name in that
  81745        \memo field. If it is a part of a global ventilation assignment the name will be
  81746        \memo <Zone Name> <global Ventilation:DesignFlowRate> name.
  81747        \memo Currently, hybrid ventilation manager is restricted to one per zone. It can either be applied
  81748        \memo through the air loop or directly to the zone. If hybrid ventilation manager is applied to an
  81749        \memo air loop and one of the zones served by that air loop also has hybrid ventilation manager,
  81750        \memo then zone hybrid ventilation manager is disabled.
  81751   A1 , \field Name
  81752        \required-field
  81753        \type alpha
  81754        \reference SystemAvailabilityManagers
  81755   A2 , \field HVAC Air Loop Name
  81756        \note Enter the name of an AirLoopHVAC or HVACTemplate:System:* object.
  81757        \type object-list
  81758        \object-list AirPrimaryLoops
  81759        \object-list HVACTemplateSystems
  81760        \note If this field is left blank, hybrid ventilation managers will be
  81761        \note simulated for zone equipment control
  81762   A3 , \field Control Zone Name
  81763        \required-field
  81764        \type object-list
  81765        \object-list ZoneNames
  81766        \note the zone name should be a zone where a thermostat or humidistat is located
  81767        \note served by an air primary loop.
  81768   A4 , \field Ventilation Control Mode Schedule Name
  81769        \required-field
  81770        \type object-list
  81771        \object-list ScheduleNames
  81772        \note The Ventilation control mode contains appropriate integer control types.
  81773        \note 0 - uncontrolled (Natural ventilation and HVAC system are controlled by themselves)
  81774        \note 1 = Temperature control
  81775        \note 2 = Enthalpy control
  81776        \note 3 = Dewpoint control
  81777        \note 4 = Outdoor ventilation air control
  81778        \note 5 = Operative temperature control with 80% adaptive comfort acceptability limits
  81779        \note 6 = Operative temperature control with 90% adaptive comfort acceptability limits
  81780        \note 7 = Carbon dioxide control
  81781   A5 , \field Use Weather File Rain Indicators
  81782        \type choice
  81783        \key Yes
  81784        \key No
  81785        \default Yes
  81786        \note If Yes, ventilation is shutoff when there is rain
  81787        \note If No, there is no rain control
  81788   N1 , \field Maximum Wind Speed
  81789        \type real
  81790        \units m/s
  81791        \minimum 0.0
  81792        \maximum 40.0
  81793        \default 40.0
  81794        \note this is the wind speed above which ventilation is shutoff
  81795   N2 , \field Minimum Outdoor Temperature
  81796        \note this is the outdoor temperature below which ventilation is shutoff
  81797        \units C
  81798        \type real
  81799        \minimum -100
  81800        \maximum 100
  81801        \default -100
  81802   N3 , \field Maximum Outdoor Temperature
  81803        \note this is the outdoor temperature above which ventilation is shutoff
  81804        \units C
  81805        \type real
  81806        \minimum -100
  81807        \maximum 100
  81808        \default 100
  81809   N4 , \field Minimum Outdoor Enthalpy
  81810        \note this is the outdoor Enthalpy below which ventilation is shutoff
  81811        \units J/kg
  81812        \type real
  81813        \minimum> 0.0
  81814        \maximum< 300000.0
  81815   N5 , \field Maximum Outdoor Enthalpy
  81816        \note this is the outdoor Enthalpy above which ventilation is shutoff
  81817        \units J/kg
  81818        \type real
  81819        \minimum> 0
  81820        \maximum< 300000.0
  81821   N6 , \field Minimum Outdoor Dewpoint
  81822        \note this is the outdoor temperature below which ventilation is shutoff
  81823        \units C
  81824        \type real
  81825        \minimum -100
  81826        \maximum 100
  81827        \default -100
  81828        \note Applicable only if Ventilation Control Mode = 3
  81829   N7 , \field Maximum Outdoor Dewpoint
  81830        \note this is the outdoor dewpoint above which ventilation is shutoff
  81831        \units C
  81832        \type real
  81833        \minimum -100
  81834        \maximum 100
  81835        \default 100
  81836        \note Applicable only if Ventilation Control Mode = 3
  81837   A6 , \field Minimum Outdoor Ventilation Air Schedule Name
  81838        \type object-list
  81839        \object-list ScheduleNames
  81840        \note Used only if Ventilation Control Mode = 4
  81841   A7 , \field Opening Factor Function of Wind Speed Curve Name
  81842        \type object-list
  81843        \object-list UnivariateFunctions
  81844        \note linear curve = a + b*WS
  81845        \note quadratic curve = a + b*WS + c*WS**2
  81846        \note WS = wind speed (m/s)
  81847   A8 , \field AirflowNetwork Control Type Schedule Name
  81848        \type object-list
  81849        \object-list ScheduleNames
  81850        \note The schedule is used to incorporate operation of AirflowNetwork large opening
  81851        \note objects and HVAC system operation.
  81852   A9 , \field Simple Airflow Control Type Schedule Name
  81853        \type object-list
  81854        \object-list ScheduleNames
  81855        \note The schedule is used to incorporate operation of simple airflow objects and HVAC
  81856        \note system operation.
  81857        \note The simple airflow objects are Ventilation and Mixing only
  81858   A10, \field ZoneVentilation Object Name
  81859        \note This field has not been instrumented to work with
  81860        \note global Zone or Zone List names option for Ventilation:DesignFlowRate.  In order to
  81861        \note use, you must enter the single <Ventilation:DesignFlowRate> name in this field.
  81862        \note If it is a part of a global ventilation assignment the name will be
  81863        \note <Zone Name> <global Ventilation:DesignFlowRate> name.
  81864        \type object-list
  81865        \object-list VentilationNames
  81866        \note The other ZoneVentilation:* and ZoneMixing objects controlled in the same AirLoopHVAC
  81867        \note will work in the same way as this ventilation object.
  81868   N8 , \field Minimum HVAC Operation Time
  81869        \note Minimum operation time when HVAC system is forced on.
  81870        \type real
  81871        \units minutes
  81872        \minimum 0.0
  81873        \default 0.0
  81874   N9 ; \field Minimum Ventilation Time
  81875        \note Minimum ventilation time when natural ventilation is forced on.
  81876        \type real
  81877        \units minutes
  81878        \minimum 0.0
  81879        \default 0.0
  81880 
  81881 AvailabilityManagerAssignmentList,
  81882        \memo Defines the applicable managers used for an AirLoopHVAC or PlantLoop. The priority of
  81883        \memo availability managers is based on a set of rules and are specific to the type of loop.
  81884        \memo The output from each availability manager is an availability status flag:
  81885        \memo NoAction, ForceOff, CycleOn, or CycleOnZoneFansOnly (used only for air loops).
  81886        \min-fields 3
  81887        \extensible:2 - repeat last two fields, remembering to remove ; from "inner" fields.
  81888   A1 , \field Name
