  81992 \group Setpoint Managers
  81993 ! We have a two level hierarchy: Setpoint Managers and Controllers.  Set
  81994 ! Point Managers are simulated at a high level - they resemble the function
  81995 ! of an Energy Management System.  A Setpoint Manager can sense any node
  81996 ! variables and use them to determine the setpoint of any other node variables.
  81997 
  81998 SetpointManager:Scheduled,
  81999      \memo The simplest Setpoint Manager simply uses a schedule to determine one
  82000      \memo or more setpoints. Values of the nodes are not used as input.
  82001   A1 , \field Name
  82002        \required-field
  82003   A2 , \field Control Variable
  82004        \type choice
  82005        \key Temperature
  82006        \key MaximumTemperature
  82007        \key MinimumTemperature
  82008        \key HumidityRatio
  82009        \key MaximumHumidityRatio
  82010        \key MinimumHumidityRatio
  82011        \key MassFlowRate
  82012        \key MaximumMassFlowRate
  82013        \key MinimumMassFlowRate
  82014        \required-field
  82015   A3 , \field Schedule Name
  82016        \type object-list
  82017        \object-list ScheduleNames
  82018        \required-field
  82019   A4 ; \field Setpoint Node or NodeList Name
  82020        \note Node(s) at which control variable will be set
  82021        \required-field
  82022        \type node
  82023 
  82024 SetpointManager:Scheduled:DualSetpoint,
  82025      \memo This setpoint manager places a high and low schedule value
  82026      \memo on one or more nodes.
  82027   A1 , \field Name
  82028        \required-field
  82029   A2 , \field Control Variable
  82030        \type choice
  82031        \key Temperature
  82032        \default Temperature
  82033   A3 , \field High Setpoint Schedule Name
  82034        \type object-list
  82035        \object-list ScheduleNames
  82036        \required-field
  82037   A4 , \field Low Setpoint Schedule Name
  82038        \type object-list
  82039        \object-list ScheduleNames
  82040        \required-field
  82041   A5 ; \field Setpoint Node or NodeList Name
  82042        \note Node(s) at which temperature will be set
  82043        \required-field
  82044        \type node
  82045 
  82046 SetpointManager:OutdoorAirReset,
  82047      \memo This Setpoint Manager is used to place a setpoint temperature on system node
  82048      \memo according to the outdoor air temperature using a reset rule. The outdoor air
  82049      \memo temperature is obtained from the weather information during the simulation.
  82050   A1 , \field Name
  82051        \required-field
  82052   A2 , \field Control Variable
  82053        \type choice
  82054        \key Temperature
  82055        \key MaximumTemperature
  82056        \key MinimumTemperature
  82057        \default Temperature
  82058   N1 , \field Setpoint at Outdoor Low Temperature
  82059        \units C
  82060        \required-field
  82061   N2 , \field Outdoor Low Temperature
  82062        \units C
  82063        \required-field
  82064   N3 , \field Setpoint at Outdoor High Temperature
  82065        \units C
  82066        \required-field
  82067   N4 , \field Outdoor High Temperature
  82068        \units C
  82069        \required-field
  82070   A3 , \field Setpoint Node or NodeList Name
  82071        \note Node(s) at which temperature will be set
  82072        \required-field
  82073        \type node
  82074   A4 , \field Schedule Name
  82075        \type object-list
  82076        \object-list ScheduleNames
  82077        \note Optional input.
  82078        \note Schedule allows scheduling of the outdoor air reset rule - a schedule value
  82079        \note of 1 means use the first rule; a value of 2 means use the second rule.
  82080   N5 , \field Setpoint at Outdoor Low Temperature 2
  82081        \note 2nd outdoor air temperature reset rule
  82082        \units C
  82083   N6 , \field Outdoor Low Temperature 2
  82084        \note 2nd outdoor air temperature reset rule
  82085        \units C
  82086   N7 , \field Setpoint at Outdoor High Temperature 2
  82087        \note 2nd outdoor air temperature reset rule
  82088        \units C
  82089   N8 ; \field Outdoor High Temperature 2
  82090        \note 2nd outdoor air temperature reset rule
  82091        \units C
  82092 
  82093 SetpointManager:SingleZone:Reheat,
  82094        \memo This setpoint manager detects the control zone load, zone inlet node flow rate, and
  82095        \memo zone node temperature and calculates a setpoint temperature for the supply air that
  82096        \memo will satisfy the zone load (heating or cooling) for the control zone. This setpoint
  82097        \memo manager is not limited to reheat applications.
  82098   A1 , \field Name
  82099        \required-field
  82100   A2 , \field Control Variable
  82101        \type choice
  82102        \key Temperature
  82103        \default Temperature
  82104   N1 , \field Minimum Supply Air Temperature
  82105        \units C
  82106        \default -99
  82107   N2 , \field Maximum Supply Air Temperature
  82108        \units C
  82109        \default 99
  82110   A3 , \field Control Zone Name
  82111        \type object-list
  82112        \object-list ZoneNames
  82113        \required-field
  82114   A4 , \field Zone Node Name
  82115        \required-field
  82116        \type node
  82117   A5 , \field Zone Inlet Node Name
  82118        \required-field
  82119        \type node
  82120   A6 ; \field Setpoint Node or NodeList Name
  82121        \note Node(s) at which the temperature will be set
  82122        \required-field
  82123        \type node
  82124 
  82125 SetpointManager:SingleZone:Heating,
  82126        \memo This setpoint manager detects the control zone load to meet the current heating
  82127        \memo setpoint, zone inlet node flow rate, and zone node temperature, and calculates a
  82128        \memo setpoint temperature for the supply air that will satisfy the zone heating load for
  82129        \memo the control zone.
